	"election.bar_accept": "ACCEPT:",
	"election.bar_reject": "REJECT:",
	"election.clock": "OCT $DAY$, $HOUR$:$MIN$ $AMPM$",
	"election.clock.am": "AM",
	"election.clock.pm": "PM",
	"election.col_accept": "ACCEPT",
	"election.col_blank": "ABSTAIN",
	"election.col_caucus": "Parliamentary Caucus",
	"election.col_reject": "REJECT",
	"election.col_seats": "SEATS",
	"election.defeat_alt": "Rejected",
	"election.lose_decisive.desc": "Chairman Amien Rais brings the gavel down over a restless hall. The Assembly has decisively voted down your Pertanggungjawaban, bringing your seventeen-month caretaker presidency to its close.",
	"election.lose_decisive.title": "ACCOUNTABILITY REJECTED",
	"election.lose_narrow.desc": "Promises made in the hotel suites evaporated inside the voting booths. Pulled down by last-minute defections under the cover of the secret ballot, your Pertanggungjawaban falls agonizingly short before dawn.",
	"election.lose_narrow.title": "UNDONE BEHIND THE CURTAIN",
	"election.lose_overwhelming.desc": "A wholesale mutiny on the Senayan floor. Uniting across every ideological fault line, the delegates have buried your Pertanggungjawaban in a historic landslide.",
	"election.lose_overwhelming.title": "REPUDIATED BY THE ASSEMBLY",
	"election.majority_marker": "Constitutional Majority",
	"election.nav.dossier": "State of the Republic",
	"election.nav.verdict": "Plenary Decree",
	"election.plenary_title": "12th Plenary Sitting of the 1999 MPR General Session",
	"election.quorum_failure": "The ayes outnumber the nays, but $VOTES$ votes fall short of the 351 needed for an absolute majority of the original Assembly.",
	"election.result_heading": "$TITLE$ ($FOR$ – $AGAINST$)",
	"election.skip_animation": "SKIP TO FINAL COUNT",
	"election.speed": "Tally Pace:",
	"election.tally": "FLOOR TALLY:",
	"election.verdict_accepted": "ACCEPTED",
	"election.verdict_rejected": "REJECTED",
	"election.victory_alt": "Accepted",
	"election.win_comfortable.desc": "Despite weeks of backroom intrigue at the Hotel Mulia, your floor whips kept the blocs in line. The Assembly has formally accepted your Pertanggungjawaban with breathing room to spare, clearing the runway for your presidential bid.",
	"election.win_comfortable.title": "THE COALITION HOLDS FIRM",
	"election.win_narrow.desc": "A breathless count in the dead of night. As the last slips of paper are tallied at the rostrum, your Pertanggungjawaban clears the chamber by a razor's edge.",
	"election.win_narrow.title": "SURVIVAL BEFORE DAWN",
	"election.win_overwhelming.desc": "The Nusantara Building erupts as the final ballots are read aloud. Defying every forecast in Jakarta, the Assembly has ratified your Pertanggungjawaban by a sweeping margin, turning a caretaker presidency into an unassailable mandate through 2004.",
	"election.win_overwhelming.title": "A NEW MANDATE",
	"epilogue.btn_back": "Review Plenary Verdict",
	"epilogue.btn_title": "Close Presidential Dossier",
	"epilogue.closing": "Thank you for playing!",
	"epilogue.end.caption": "Jakarta, 1999–2026",
	"epilogue.end.p1": "In the history that actually transpired, the People’s Consultative Assembly voted 355 to 322 shortly after midnight on October 20, 1999—with nine abstentions and four spoiled ballots—to reject B.J. Habibie’s accountability speech. He withdrew from the presidential race before dawn. Hours later, Abdurrahman Wahid, the nearly blind Nahdlatul Ulama cleric known across the archipelago as Gus Dur, defeated Megawati Sukarnoputri 373 to 313 in the Republic’s first contested presidential election. Megawati, whose party had won the June polls, was elected vice president the following day to calm the red-shirted crowds in the streets. Whatever course the ballots took in Senayan, the larger watershed was the same: a seventeen-month caretaker presidency ended on green slips of paper counted aloud in a parliamentary hall, rather than by tanks at the gates.",
	"epilogue.end.p2": "To measure the distance traveled, one need only recall the wreckage of 1998. The rupiah, trading near 2,400 to the dollar in mid-1997, had plunged past 16,800 by June 1998. Real GDP contracted by roughly 13 percent in a single year, while inflation neared 80 percent. Suharto had signed his second letter of intent with the IMF on January 15, 1998, under the folded arms of Michel Camdessus, after the abrupt closure of sixteen banks in November 1997 triggered a systemic run. Then came the Trisakti shootings on May 12, the three days of arson and pogroms from May 13 to 15 in which over a thousand people perished in burning shopping malls and ethnic Chinese women were subjected to organized terror, and finally Suharto’s resignation on the morning of May 21 as students held the roofs of Senayan.",
	"epilogue.end.p3": "Rebuilding the financial system cost roughly Rp 658 trillion in bank recapitalization bonds—more than half a year’s GDP—driving public debt from 24 percent of GDP before the crash to nearly 93 percent. The Indonesian Bank Restructuring Agency spent six years liquidating seized assets and pursuing delinquent tycoons before winding down in 2004, while four insolvent state banks were fused into Bank Mandiri in 1999. Across the IMF programs from 1997 to 2003, Jakarta drew roughly SDR 7.4 billion (around $$11.1 billion). In 2006, riding a commodity boom and tighter fiscal discipline, the administration of Susilo Bambang Yudhoyono paid down $$3.75 billion in June and cleared the remaining $$3.2 billion that October, four years ahead of the December 2010 schedule, before dissolving the World Bank-led Consultative Group on Indonesia in January 2007. Indonesia exited the decade owing the Fund nothing and growing at over 5 percent a year.",
	"epilogue.end.p4": "Between 1999 and 2002, the MPR amended the 1945 Constitution four times: capping presidents at two terms, establishing direct presidential elections, creating the Constitutional Court, and phasing out the military’s appointed legislative seats by 2004. Regional autonomy took effect on January 1, 2001, followed by direct local elections for governors, regents, and mayors in 2005. The Press Law of September 1999 buried the old SIUPP licensing regime for good, returning Tempo, Detik, and Editor to the newsstands, while the Corruption Eradication Commission (KPK), established in 2002, spent its first decade putting cabinet ministers, central bankers, and police generals behind bars.",
	"epilogue.end.p5": "In East Timor, 78.5 percent of voters rejected autonomy within Indonesia on August 30, 1999. Army-backed militias torched Dili and displaced hundreds of thousands before Australian-led INTERFET peacekeepers under Major General Peter Cosgrove came ashore on September 20. The MPR ratified the separation that October, and Timor-Leste raised its flag as an independent nation on May 20, 2002.",
	"epilogue.end.p6": "Peace in Aceh came out of catastrophe. After the Indian Ocean tsunami of December 26, 2004 claimed some 170,000 lives across the province, former Finnish president Martti Ahtisaari brokered the Helsinki Memorandum of Understanding between Jakarta and the Free Aceh Movement on August 15, 2005. Earlier accords at Malino had quieted the sectarian bloodshed in Poso and Ambon, even as the Bali bombings of October 12, 2002 underscored the rise of militant networks. Yet impunity endured: no senior commander answered in court for May 1998, disappeared activists such as Wiji Thukul were never found, and Suharto died on January 27, 2008 without ever standing trial.",
	"epilogue.end.p7": "Habibie lived to witness two decades of the order he helped usher in. He established The Habibie Center in 1999 to champion democratization and scientific advancement, and passed away on September 11, 2019, at the age of 83—having seen Yudhoyono win re-election in 2009 and Joko Widodo, a former furniture exporter from Surakarta from outside the old Jakarta establishment, win the presidency in 2014.",
	"epilogue.end.p8": "Yet the struggle over Reformasi’s legacy never truly closed. In September 2019, days after Habibie’s passing, parliament revised the KPK statute over massive student protests. In February 2024, Prabowo Subianto—Suharto’s former son-in-law, whose removal from Kostrad command in May 1998 defined the opening hours of Habibie’s presidency—won the presidency in a landslide and took the oath on October 20, 2024, twenty-five years to the day after Gus Dur. In March 2025, parliament unanimously expanded the civilian posts open to active-duty officers under a revised Armed Forces Law, and in August 2025 demonstrations convulsed more than a hundred cities after 21-year-old ride-hailing driver Affan Kurniawan was killed beneath a police tactical vehicle. Human Rights Watch’s 2026 assessment highlighted the renewed encroachment of the military into civilian governance—yet across the archipelago, an unruly press and a generation born after 1998 continued to contest the streets, refusing to surrender the republic Habibie’s brief caretaker presidency had pried open.",
	"epilogue.end.title": "",
	"epilogue.intro_common": "You took the oath of office over a country in receivership and a capital still smelling of smoke. You leave behind an unfettered press, rival parties contending in the open, and a parliament that no longer rubber-stamps Bina Graha. What followed was not your work alone, but none of it could have begun without the doors you unbolted.",
	"epilogue.intro_lost": "The Assembly rejected your [i]Pidato Pertanggungjawaban[/i]. The defeat stung, yet the verdict was rendered in open session by seven hundred delegates, and power passed the way it must in a constitutional republic: peacefully, before dawn, under the rules.",
	"epilogue.intro_won": "The Assembly ratified your [i]Pidato Pertanggungjawaban[/i]. For the first time in the Republic’s history, a sitting president stood before the representatives of the nation to answer for his stewardship—and prevailed not by decree or by force, but by the count of the ballot box.",
	"epilogue.title": "EPILOGUE",
	"error.fatal_body": "Failed to fetch local JSON files. Check the console for missing files or syntax errors.",
	"error.fatal_title": "Fatal Error Loading Assets",
	"event.ev_aceh_insurgency.date": "July 8, 1999",
	"event.ev_aceh_insurgency.desc": "The lifting of Aceh's Military Operations Area (DOM) status last August, followed by your personal apology at the Baiturrahman Grand Mosque in Banda Aceh in March, was meant to open a path toward reconciliation. Instead, the province is spiraling into an even bloodier cycle of insurgency and reprisal. Free Aceh Movement (GAM) guerrillas have ambushed military convoys across Pidie, North Aceh, and East Aceh, while tens of thousands of villagers flee into mosque compounds. Worse, following the May shooting of protesters at Simpang KKA in Lhokseumawe, territorial troops and Kostrad units are executing ruthless sweeps across the countryside, culminating in reports of a brutal military raid on charismatic cleric Teungku Bantaqiah's boarding school in Beutong Ateuh.\n\nWhile student leaders of SIRA demand an East Timor-style independence referendum in Banda Aceh, General Wiranto's field commanders are demanding the restoration of emergency military authority, and human rights advocates led by Amran Zamzami are pressing you to sign a Presidential Decree establishing an Independent Commission for the Investigation of Violence in Aceh (KPTKA).",
	"event.ev_aceh_insurgency.opt.0.body": "President Habibie's signing of Keppres No. 88/1999 chartering the 27-member Independent Commission for the Investigation of Violence in Aceh (KPTKA) was greeted in Banda Aceh with bitter skepticism. While human rights lawyers welcome the mandate to investigate the Simpang KKA and Beutong Ateuh massacres, KontraS coordinator Munir pointed out the glaring flaw in the Palace's decree: KPTKA has power only to compile reports, not to prosecute a single Kopassus or Kostrad officer in a civilian court. Meanwhile, inside Cilangkap, senior generals are livid that Jakarta is parading army abuses in public while soldiers are being ambushed daily along the Banda Aceh–Medan highway.",
	"event.ev_aceh_insurgency.opt.0.headline": "KOMISI INDEPENDEN DIBENTUK, TAPI SIAPA BERANI ADILI JENDERAL?",
	"event.ev_aceh_insurgency.opt.0.text": "\"Sign Keppres No. 88/1999 establishing the Independent Commission for the Investigation of Violence in Aceh (KPTKA), paired with the new Special Autonomy cultural and religious guarantees. If soldiers committed atrocities in Beutong Ateuh and Simpang KKA, the state must investigate its own uniform.\"",
	"event.ev_aceh_insurgency.opt.1.body": "The Palace's abrupt order pulling non-organic Kostrad and Brimob battalions out of Pidie and North Aceh has triggered an immediate security vacuum across the province's industrial corridor. Within hours of the troop trucks rolling out of Lhokseumawe, armed GAM guerrillas raised their crescent-and-star banners over three sub-district offices and forced the Arun LNG complex to scale back operations. At ABRI headquarters in Cilangkap, furious colonels accuse Habibie of stabbing soldiers in the back for a cheap public-relations stunt that GAM's exiled leadership in Sweden has already mocked as a sign of Jakarta's impending collapse.",
	"event.ev_aceh_insurgency.opt.1.headline": "TENTARA DITARIK MENDADAK, ACEH UTARA JATUH KE TANGAN GAM",
	"event.ev_aceh_insurgency.opt.1.text": "\"An apology means nothing if the conduct on the ground never changes. Order an immediate pullback of non-organic Kostrad and Brimob units from North Aceh and invite Acehnese ulama and civic leaders directly to Merdeka Palace.\"",
	"event.ev_aceh_insurgency.opt.2.body": "Faced with mass graves from the DOM era and student banners demanding a referendum across Banda Aceh, the Habibie administration has reached for the only tool technocrats seem to understand: a checkbook. While provincial elites in the Aceh DPRD and Jakarta's Utusan Daerah caucus eagerly pocketed the promise of 70 percent oil-and-gas revenue retention, student leaders of SIRA burned copies of the fiscal package outside the Baiturrahman Grand Mosque yesterday. 'Jakarta thinks ten years of military torture and widowed mothers can be paid off like an overdue gas invoice,' SIRA leader Muhammad Nazar told reporters.",
	"event.ev_aceh_insurgency.opt.2.headline": "HABIBIE COBA BELI LUKA ACEH DENGAN UANG GAS ARUN",
	"event.ev_aceh_insurgency.opt.2.text": "\"Money alone will not erase the DOM years, but starved provinces breed rebellion. Fast-track the new fiscal balance allocations for Aceh, guaranteeing the province 70% of its oil and gas revenues alongside reconstruction aid for Pidie and Lhokseumawe.\"",
	"event.ev_aceh_insurgency.opt.3.body": "Four months after President Habibie stood weeping in Banda Aceh to beg forgiveness for a decade of military terror, the terror is back under a polite new bureaucratic euphemism. By authorizing [i]Operasi Sadar Rencong[/i] nominally under a police badge while BKO military intelligence units conduct midnight sweeps through Pidie and West Aceh, the Palace has fooled nobody. Local Legal Aid Foundation (LBH) offices in Banda Aceh documented nineteen Mysterious killings and burned shop-houses this week alone, proving that Habibie's March apology was merely a rhetorical curtain for the same old New Order security reflex.",
	"event.ev_aceh_insurgency.opt.3.headline": "GANTI BAJU OPERASI MILITER: DARI JARING MERAH KE SADAR RENCONG",
	"event.ev_aceh_insurgency.opt.3.text": "\"Keep the counter-insurgency campaign out of the headlines. Authorize Joint Intelligence and Police Operations (Operasi Sadar Rencong) to target GAM cells quietly without formally re-declaring a Military Operations Area.\"",
	"event.ev_aceh_insurgency.opt.4.body": "All pretense of a 'New Paradigm' evaporated in Aceh this week as fresh combat battalions poured into Lhokseumawe, Pidie, and West Aceh with carte blanche from Merdeka Palace. In response to the renewed military offensive, a two-day general strike has turned Banda Aceh into a ghost town while over 100,000 villagers flee into refugee camps inside mosque compounds. In Jakarta, PPP legislators and Acehnese community figures accused Habibie of washing his hands in Acehnese blood solely to curry favor with General Wiranto's bloc ahead of the October MPR session.",
	"event.ev_aceh_insurgency.opt.4.headline": "SERAMBI MEKKAH KEMBALI MEMBARA, MOGOK MASSAL LUMPUHKAN BANDA ACEH",
	"event.ev_aceh_insurgency.opt.4.text": "\"Restraint stops looking like wisdom when separatists are ambushing soldiers daily. Grant General Wiranto's commanders full operational latitude to crush GAM by force, a Republic that cannot hold its borders together has nothing left to govern.\"",
	"event.ev_aceh_insurgency.title": "Bloodshed in Aceh",
	"event.ev_assembly_convenes.date": "October 1, 1999",
	"event.ev_assembly_convenes.desc": "All 700 delegates of the People's Consultative Assembly (MPR), 462 elected DPR party representatives, 38 appointed ABRI officers, 135 provincial delegates (Utusan Daerah) elected by the 27 regional parliaments, and 65 civic and functional delegates (Utusan Golongan), have taken their oaths beneath the green tortoiseshell dome of the Senayan complex. Before your Accountability Speech or the presidential election can take place, the Assembly must elect two crucial leaders: the Speaker of the MPR (who will preside over the General Session and set the rules for your Accountability Vote) on October 3, and the Speaker of the DPR on October 6. In the hotel suites of the Hilton and the Mulia, a high-stakes three-way chess match is underway between Amien Rais, PKB Chairman Matori Abdul Djalil (backed by Megawati's PDI-P), and Golkar Chairman Akbar Tandjung.",
	"event.ev_assembly_convenes.opt.0.body": "On paper, the hotel-suite pact engineered between Golkar and the Islamic parties was a surgical triumph, electing Amien Rais as MPR Speaker (305–279 over PDI-P's Matori Abdul Djalil) and handing Akbar Tandjung the DPR Speakership by a landslide (411 votes). Yet seasoned Senayan veterans are asking whether President Habibie just built the gallows for his own presidency: Amien Rais now holds the MPR gavel to advance his own 'Central Axis' candidate, and Akbar Tandjung has already secured the five-year prize he wanted most, leaving him with zero incentive to go down with Habibie's sinking ship on October 19.",
	"event.ev_assembly_convenes.opt.0.headline": "AMIEN RAIS KETUA MPR, AKBAR TANDJUNG KETUA DPR: KEMENANGAN TAKTIS YANG MENYIMPAN RANJAU BAGI HABIBIE",
	"event.ev_assembly_convenes.opt.0.text": "\"Execute a grand parliamentary bargain: instruct Golkar's whips to back Amien Rais for MPR Speaker against PDI-P's candidate Matori Abdul Djalil on October 3, in exchange for the Islamic parties backing Akbar Tandjung for DPR Speaker on October 6.\"",
	"event.ev_assembly_convenes.opt.1.body": "With Palace whips delivering the regional and Golkar blocs en masse, Akbar Tandjung coasted to the DPR Speakership yesterday with 411 votes. But inside the Hilton Hotel suites where Akbar's former HMI (Islamic Students Association) lieutenants gather late at night, the mood was anything but grateful toward Merdeka Palace. 'Habibie paid cash up front to make Akbar the second most powerful man in the country, and now Akbar holds all the cards for the next two weeks,' observed political analyst Eep Saefulloh Fatah.",
	"event.ev_assembly_convenes.opt.1.headline": "AKBAR TANDJUNG AMANKAN KURSI KETUA DPR, HABIBIE BELUM TENTU KEBAGIAN KURSI PRESIDEN",
	"event.ev_assembly_convenes.opt.1.text": "\"Throw the Palace's full weight behind Akbar Tandjung for the DPR Speakership unconditionally, rallying both Golkar wings and the regional delegates to demonstrate the Banyan Tree's discipline.\"",
	"event.ev_assembly_convenes.opt.2.body": "President Habibie's backchannel offer to trade away Golkar's claim on the parliamentary leadership in exchange for a softer PDI-P stance on his Accountability Speech triggered an open mutiny inside his own party caucus yesterday. Defying Bina Graha's emissaries outright, Akbar Tandjung's 120 DPR legislators cut their own deal with Amien Rais and ABRI to seize the Speakerships anyway, leaving Habibie alienated from his own party apparatus while PDI-P pockets his concessions with a smirk.",
	"event.ev_assembly_convenes.opt.2.headline": "MANUVER ISTANA DEKATI PDI-P PICU PEMBERONTAKAN FRAKSI GOLKAR DI SENAYAN",
	"event.ev_assembly_convenes.opt.2.text": "\"Reach across the aisle to Diponegoro: offer Golkar support for PDI-P's preferred leadership slate in the DPR and MPR in exchange for PDI-P toning down its attacks on your upcoming Accountability Speech.\"",
	"event.ev_assembly_convenes.opt.3.body": "After wining and dining 200 regional and functional delegates at Istana Negara in a blatant attempt to reconstruct Suharto's old 200-vote rubber-stamp [i]Fraksi Utusan Daerah[/i], Bina Graha suffered a humiliating defeat on the MPR floor yesterday afternoon. United for once in their determination to stop the Palace from herding regional delegates like cattle, PDI-P, PKB, PAN, and even Akbar Tandjung's Golkar voted to abolish the standalone Regional Faction, forcing provincial delegates to sit inside the regular party caucuses!",
	"event.ev_assembly_convenes.opt.3.headline": "JAMUAN KAVIAR DI ISTANA GAGAL! DPR BUBARKAN FRAKSI UTUSAN DAERAH ANDALAN HABIBIE",
	"event.ev_assembly_convenes.opt.3.text": "\"Host the 135 Utusan Daerah and 65 Utusan Golongan delegates at Istana Negara to organize an independent non-partisan 'Fraksi Utusan' bloc loyal directly to the Presidency.\"",
	"event.ev_assembly_convenes.opt.4.body": "While Amien Rais, Akbar Tandjung, Taufik Kiemas, and General Wiranto spent the last seventy-two hours locked in marathon horse-trading across the hotel suites of central Jakarta to divide the MPR and DPR Speakerships, Merdeka Palace sat on its hands piously preaching 'separation of powers.' The result is a parliamentary leadership that owes its gavels entirely to its own backroom deals and nothing whatsoever to B.J. Habibie.",
	"event.ev_assembly_convenes.opt.4.headline": "HABIBIE JADI PENONTON DI SENAYAN SAAT AMIEN RAIS DAN AKBAR BAGI-BAGI KEKUASAAN",
	"event.ev_assembly_convenes.opt.4.text": "\"Respect the separation of powers strictly: keep Merdeka Palace out of the parliamentary Speakership elections and let the 700 delegates choose their own presiding officers.\"",
	"event.ev_assembly_convenes.title": "MPR Convenes",
	"event.ev_bank_bali.date": "August 3, 1999",
	"event.ev_bank_bali.desc": "A political bombshell has detonated across every front page in Jakarta. Banking law analyst Pradjoto, backed by leaked central bank transfer records, has revealed that Rp 546 billion ($80 million), nearly 60% of an interbank debt claim owed to nationalized Bank Bali by closed banks BDNI, BUN, and Bank Tiara, was paid out as an extraordinary 'collection fee' to PT Era Giat Prima (EGP), a private firm run by businessman Djoko S. Tjandra and Golkar Deputy Treasurer Setya Novanto. Worse still, because interbank claims were already fully guaranteed by the government under Presidential Decree No. 26/1998, no private collector was ever needed, meaning state recapitalization funds from the Indonesian Bank Restructuring Agency (IBRA) were effectively siphoned straight into EGP. Opposition MPs and investigative reporters have already dubbed it 'Baligate,' alleging that the Rp 546 billion war chest was engineered by your closest confidant, Supreme Advisory Council (DPA) Chairman A.A. Baramuli, and State Enterprises Minister Tanri Abeng to buy MPR delegates for your October re-election campaign ([i]Tim Sukses[/i]).",
	"event.ev_bank_bali.opt.0.body": "Cornered by banking analyst Pradjoto's explosive revelations and threats of an immediate IMF freeze, President Habibie has ordered the Rp 546 billion PT Era Giat Prima accounts frozen and opened the door to foreign forensic auditors. Yet nobody in Jakarta believes the Palace was an innocent bystander: as banking investigator Pradjoto noted yesterday, EGP is run by Golkar Deputy Treasurer Setya Novanto and backed by Habibie's own chief lobbyist, DPA Chairman A.A. Baramuli. Inside Golkar's Slipi headquarters, furious party bosses accuse Habibie of handing prosecutors the rope to hang his own campaign treasurers while pretending his own hands are clean.",
	"event.ev_bank_bali.opt.0.headline": "SENJATA MAKAN TUAN DI BANK BALI: HABIBIE KORBANKAN TIM SUKSES DEMI SELAMATKAN DIRI",
	"event.ev_bank_bali.opt.0.text": "\"No presidency survives a half-measure on a scandal of this magnitude. Order Supreme Audit Agency (BPK) Chairman Billy Joedono and IBRA Chairman Glenn Yusuf to freeze the PT Era Giat Prima accounts immediately and invite an independent international forensic audit.\"",
	"event.ev_bank_bali.opt.1.body": "Shoving half a trillion rupiah of skimmed state recapitalization funds into a Bank Indonesia escrow account after being caught red-handed does not erase a felony; that was the blunt verdict from legal experts and DPR Commission VIII members yesterday. 'If a pickpocket hands back the wallet only after the whole bus grabs his wrist, he still goes to prison,' Indonesia Corruption Watch (ICW) coordinator Teten Masduki told reporters. By attempting to settle the Bank Bali heist like an accounting clerical error, the Palace has only convinced the public that the trail leads straight into Bina Graha.",
	"event.ev_bank_bali.opt.1.headline": "UANG RP 546 MILIAR MASUK ESCROW, TAPI SIAPA OTAK PENJARAHAN BANK BALI?",
	"event.ev_bank_bali.opt.1.text": "\"Have IBRA Chairman Glenn Yusuf and Bank Bali's Rudy Ramli quietly place the disputed Rp 546 billion into a frozen escrow account at Bank Indonesia, returning the money to the state balance sheet before the scandal metastasizes.\"",
	"event.ev_bank_bali.opt.2.body": "After months of letting DPA Chairman A.A. Baramuli and the shadowy 'Tim Sukses' roam Senayan with suitcases of campaign promises, President Habibie is suddenly pretending he barely knows the men running his own re-election bid! Opposition legislators in DPR Commission VIII laughed openly at the Palace's announcement dissolving the campaign team yesterday. 'Who was the Rp 546 billion war chest meant to elect, Baramuli or Habibie?' asked PDI-P economist Kwik Kian Gie, while inside the Sulawesi caucus, Baramuli's loyalists are fuming at being thrown under the bus.",
	"event.ev_bank_bali.opt.2.headline": "CUCI TANGAN ALA HABIBIE: BARAMULI DIJADIKAN KAMBING HITAM SKANDAL BANK BALI!",
	"event.ev_bank_bali.opt.2.text": "\"Create immediate political distance between Merdeka Palace and the implicated operatives: publicly dissolve the informal 'Tim Sukses' campaign team and instruct A.A. Baramuli to step back from all MPR lobbying operations.\"",
	"event.ev_bank_bali.opt.3.body": "At a time when millions of Indonesians are queuing for subsidized rice and IBRA is bleeding hundreds of trillions of rupiah in taxpayer bonds to recapitalize collapsed banks, Merdeka Palace has the audacity to call an Rp 546 billion fee paid to Golkar treasurer Setya Novanto's shell company a 'routine commercial dispute.' Anti-corruption protesters burned effigies of Baramuli and Djoko Tjandra outside Bank Indonesia yesterday, while World Bank officials warned that Jakarta's brazen whitewash will cost the country every cent of its remaining international bailout.",
	"event.ev_bank_bali.opt.3.headline": "KEBOHONGAN PUBLIK RP 546 MILIAR: ISTANA SEBUT PERAMPOKAN UANG RAKYAT CUMA SENGKETA KOMISI",
	"event.ev_bank_bali.opt.3.text": "\"Treat this as a technical banking dispute between Rudy Ramli's management at Bank Bali and PT Era Giat Prima. Leave the review entirely to Bank Indonesia Governor Sjahril Sabirin and Finance Minister Bambang Subianto behind closed doors.\"",
	"event.ev_bank_bali.opt.4.body": "In a display of authoritarian shamelessness that would make the old New Order blush, the Habibie administration has responded to the biggest banking corruption scandal of the Reformasi era by siccing the police on whistleblower Pradjoto and the journalists who exposed it. As Setya Novanto, Djoko Tjandra, and A.A. Baramuli parade into National Police headquarters to file defamation suits rather than sit in the dock, foreign institutional investors dumped Indonesian bonds in disgust, sending the Jakarta Stock Exchange tumbling 6 percent in a single afternoon.",
	"event.ev_bank_bali.opt.4.headline": "MALING TERIAK MALING: PENYINGKAP SKANDAL BANK BALI DIPOLISIKAN ISTANA",
	"event.ev_bank_bali.opt.4.text": "\"Go on the offensive: support A.A. Baramuli and Djoko Tjandra in filing criminal defamation complaints against Pradjoto and the newspapers, questioning why Rudy Ramli leaked internal banking records right before the MPR session.\"",
	"event.ev_bank_bali.title": "Bank Bali Scandal Breaks",
	"event.ev_central_axis.date": "October 7, 1999",
	"event.ev_central_axis.desc": "Fresh off his election as MPR Speaker on October 3, Amien Rais has pulled off a political masterstroke that has shattered the two-horse race between you and Megawati Sukarnoputri. At a packed press conference today, flanked by leaders of the Reform Faction (PAN and PK), PPP Chairman Hamzah Haz, PKB Chairman Matori Abdul Djalil, and PBB Chairman Yusril Ihza Mahendra, the newly consolidated 'Poros Tengah' (Central Axis) has formally nominated Abdurrahman Wahid (Gus Dur, the near-blind cleric who leads the 40-million-strong Nahdlatul Ulama) as its candidate for President of the Republic. While Gus Dur himself had previously expressed sympathy for Megawati, he has accepted the nomination to prevent what the ulama call a destructive polarization between secular nationalists and political Islam.\n\n[color=__CLR_CRIMSON__]Amien Rais has formally consolidated the Islamic parties, absorbing PPP, PKB, and 20 minor Islamic party delegates into the 'Poros Tengah' coalition. Instantly commanding 163 MPR Delegates and transforming into the ultimate kingmaker of the General Session.[/color]",
	"event.ev_central_axis.opt.0.body": "President Habibie's polite welcome for Abdurrahman Wahid's surprise presidential nomination could not mask the cold sweat breaking out inside his campaign headquarters at Patra Kuningan. For months, Habibie's strategists had assumed the Islamic parties would have no choice but to back the founder of ICMI in order to stop Megawati. Now, by nominating Gus Dur, Amien Rais has given Muslim and reformist delegates a viable third door; one that only opens wide if Habibie's Accountability Speech is voted down on October 19.",
	"event.ev_central_axis.opt.0.headline": "HABIBIE SAMBUT PENCALONAN GUS DUR, TAPI POROS TENGAH SIAPKAN SKENARIO TANPA HABIBIE",
	"event.ev_central_axis.opt.0.text": "\"Welcome Gus Dur's nomination graciously as proof of Indonesia's democratic maturity, while reminding the Central Axis that splitting the Muslim and reformist vote risks handing the presidency straight to PDI-P unless we coordinate on the Accountability Vote first.\"",
	"event.ev_central_axis.opt.1.body": "Abdurrahman Wahid needed only one sentence to puncture Bina Graha's latest trial balloon yesterday afternoon. Asked by reporters outside the Ciganjur compound about President Habibie's offer to make him or Hamzah Haz Vice President in exchange for Poros Tengah's 163 votes, the near-blind NU cleric chuckled: 'Why on earth should I apply to be Pak Habibie's assistant when Amien Rais is already working overtime to make me his replacement?' The press corps roared with laughter, though PPP insiders privately admit they are still listening to Palace offers.",
	"event.ev_central_axis.opt.1.headline": "DITAWARI KURSI WAPRES OLEH HABIBIE, GUS DUR BERSeloroh: NGAPAIN JADI WAKIL KALAU BISA JADI PRESIDEN?",
	"event.ev_central_axis.opt.1.text": "\"Meet privately with Gus Dur and Amien Rais to propose a grand power-sharing ticket: support your re-election as President on October 20 with Gus Dur or Hamzah Haz elevated to a constitutionally empowered Vice Presidency.\"",
	"event.ev_central_axis.opt.2.body": "Politics makes strange bedfellows, but watching B.J. Habibie's emissaries knock on Jalan Diponegoro's door to warn Megawati Sukarnoputri about Amien Rais's 'treachery' takes the prize for 1999. While Taufik Kiemas's pragmatic wing inside PDI-P is furious at Gus Dur for abandoning his alliance with Megawati and heard the Palace envoy out, PDI-P's rank-and-file delegates remain adamant that they will never vote to accept Habibie's Accountability Speech just to spite Amien Rais.",
	"event.ev_central_axis.opt.2.headline": "PANIK DIKEPUNG POROS TENGAH, ISTANA COBA MERAYU BANTENG YANG TERLUKA",
	"event.ev_central_axis.opt.2.text": "\"Bypass Amien Rais and send an emergency envoy to Megawati Sukarnoputri and Taufik Kiemas: propose a nationalist-technocratic understanding between Golkar and PDI-P to stop Amien Rais's Central Axis from hijacking the election.\"",
	"event.ev_central_axis.opt.3.body": "Campaign strategists inside Habibie's [i]Tim Sukses[/i] dismissed Gus Dur's nomination by the Central Axis yesterday as 'a paper tiger that will fold before October 20,' vowing instead to steamroll the MPR with Golkar, ABRI, and outer-island delegates. Parliamentary mathematicians in Senayan were less impressed: with PPP, PKB, and PAN now consolidated into a 163-seat bloc under Speaker Amien Rais, snubbing the Central Axis leaves Habibie with zero margin for error if even thirty Golkar delegates defect behind the secret-ballot curtain.",
	"event.ev_central_axis.opt.3.headline": "PALACE DISMISSES CENTRAL AXIS AS BLUFF, BETS THE HOUSE ON GOLKAR AND REGIONAL VOTES",
	"event.ev_central_axis.opt.3.text": "\"Double down on the Banyan Tree and the provinces: ignore the Central Axis's maneuvering and concentrate all Palace resources on locking down Golkar's 120 DPR seats, ABRI's 38 seats, and the 135 Utusan Daerah delegates.\"",
	"event.ev_central_axis.opt.4.body": "Of all the blunders committed by President Habibie's surrogates this year, publicly mocking Abdurrahman Wahid's blindness and stroke recovery as a constitutional disqualification under Article 6 may prove the most suicidal. Within hours, Nahdlatul Ulama boarding schools across East and Central Java erupted in fury, Banser youth brigades burned Habibie campaign banners in Surabaya and Jombang, and wavering PKB and PPP delegates vowed to bury the President's Accountability Speech on October 19.",
	"event.ev_central_axis.opt.4.headline": "HINA FISIK GUS DUR, JUTAAN WARGA NAHDLIYIN DAN BANSER NGAMUK KE ISTANA!",
	"event.ev_central_axis.opt.4.text": "\"Have Palace surrogates publicly question whether a man who has suffered two near-fatal strokes and cannot read a briefing paper with his own eyes is medically fit under Article 6 of the Constitution to serve as President.\"",
	"event.ev_central_axis.title": "The Central Axis Nominates Gus Dur",
	"event.ev_dili_flames.date": "September 4, 1999",
	"event.ev_dili_flames.desc": "At 9:00 AM today in Dili (9:00 PM on September 3 at UN Headquarters in New York), UNAMET Chief Ian Martin and UN Secretary-General Kofi Annan simultaneously announced the certified result of the East Timor consultation: 94,388 voters (21.5%) accepted special autonomy, while 344,580 voters (78.5%) rejected it in favor of independence. Within hours of the announcement, East Timor descended into hell. Pro-integration militias, operating openly alongside territorial soldiers and police, have unleashed 'Operasi Sapu Jagad', systematically torching 70% of Dili's buildings, slaughtering civilians sheltering at the Suai Church compound, firing on Nobel laureate Bishop Carlos Belo's residence, and laying siege to the UNAMET compound where foreign staff and 1,500 terrified Timorese refugees are trapped behind razor wire. Over 250,000 civilians are being herded onto military trucks and ships at gunpoint for forced deportation into West Timor. Kofi Annan is on the telephone from New York demanding immediate action.",
	"event.ev_dili_flames.opt.0.body": "President Habibie's declaration of Martial Law under Keppres No. 107/1999 and the dispatch of Maj. Gen. Kiki Syahnakri have done nothing to stem the scorched-earth rampage consuming East Timor. Even after Syahnakri landed in Dili, eyewitnesses inside the besieged UNAMET compound reported Indonesian soldiers loading looted refrigerators onto military trucks while Aitarak militias burned entire city blocks to the ground. In Washington and New York, diplomats dismissed the martial law decree as 'handing the fire hose to the arsonists,' while in Senayan, PDI-P and Golkar MPs alike are already sharpening their knives over the 78.5 percent humiliation.",
	"event.ev_dili_flames.opt.0.headline": "MARTIAL LAW FAILS TO HALT THE TORCHING OF DILI AS WORLD FURY MOUNTS",
	"event.ev_dili_flames.opt.0.text": "\"Sign Presidential Decree No. 107/1999 declaring Martial Law (Darurat Militer) across East Timor, relieve Col. Tono Suratman and Maj. Gen. Adam Damiri of operational control, and dispatch Maj. Gen. Kiki Syahnakri with fresh Kostrad battalions to restore order within 48 hours.\"",
	"event.ev_dili_flames.opt.1.body": "Less than twenty-four hours after the 78.5 percent referendum defeat was announced, President Habibie has capitulated to Western pressure and invited foreign peacekeepers into East Timor without giving his own armed forces a single day to restore order! While Kofi Annan praised the move from New York, nationalist fury has erupted across Jakarta: retired generals and DPR Commission I legislators accused the President of high treason against the memory of fallen soldiers, and inside Cilangkap, senior commanders are openly declaring that Habibie's political career is finished.",
	"event.ev_dili_flames.opt.1.headline": "HABIBIE ANGKAT BENDERA PUTIH! UNDANG TENTARA ASING MASUK DILI TANPA RESTU DPR",
	"event.ev_dili_flames.opt.1.text": "\"Bypass the generals' stalling entirely: inform Kofi Annan tonight that Indonesia cannot contain its own rogue territorial units in Dili and formally invite an international peacekeeping force to land immediately.\"",
	"event.ev_dili_flames.opt.2.body": "With priests and ratusan of refugees slaughtered inside the Suai Church compound, Bishop Carlos Belo's home burned to the ground, and smoke rising over 70 percent of Dili in full view of satellite cameras, the Habibie government has plumbed new depths of moral bankruptcy by leaving Kodam IX/Udayana's commanders in place and blaming 'Western media fabrications.' The UN Security Council has convened in emergency session to draft Chapter VII sanctions, while the rupiah plunged 8 percent on panic selling in Singapore.",
	"event.ev_dili_flames.opt.2.headline": "BLOODBATH IN SUAI AND DILI AS JAKARTA DENIES THE OBVIOUS",
	"event.ev_dili_flames.opt.2.text": "\"Reject both martial law and foreign peacekeepers: hand absolute security authority to General Wiranto's existing command structure in Kodam IX/Udayana and insist that reports of military complicity are Western media fabrications.\"",
	"event.ev_dili_flames.opt.3.body": "Evacuating Nobel laureate Bishop Carlos Belo and foreign correspondents out of burning Dili on RAAF Hercules flights prevented the massacre of UN staff, but global television networks are broadcasting a devastating image around the clock: terrified Timorese mothers passing their babies over the razor wire of the UNAMET compound as foreign personnel are airlifted out, leaving an entire population behind in the dark with the militias. At home, nationalist politicians attack Habibie for losing the province, while human rights advocates condemn him for failing to stop his own army.",
	"event.ev_dili_flames.opt.3.headline": "SAKSI MATA DIUSIR DARI DILI SAAT OPERASI SAPU JAGAD BERLANSUNG",
	"event.ev_dili_flames.opt.3.text": "\"Order an immediate military escort to evacuate Bishop Carlos Belo, UNAMET personnel, and foreign journalists to Darwin and Baucau, while instructing Komnas HAM's KPP-HAM team to document every atrocity on the ground.\"",
	"event.ev_dili_flames.opt.4.body": "As Dili burns and 250,000 refugees are trucked at gunpoint into West Timor, President Habibie's release of Xanana Gusmão to the British Embassy and his invitation to five UN Security Council ambassadors to inspect East Timor has pleased nobody at home. In Senayan, DPR Commission I members called the UN Security Council visit 'a colonial inspection tour of a defeated nation,' while UN Ambassador Martin Andjaba made clear upon landing at Halim that diplomatic gestures will not save Indonesia from sanctions unless foreign peacekeepers are admitted immediately.",
	"event.ev_dili_flames.opt.4.headline": "XANANA BEBAS KE KEDUBES INGGRIS, TIM DEWAN KEAMANAN PBB DATANG MENGHAKIMI JAKARTA",
	"event.ev_dili_flames.opt.4.text": "\"Release Xanana Gusmão unconditionally from his Salemba house arrest to the British Embassy and invite the UN Security Council delegation led by Ambassador Martin Andjaba to fly into Jakarta and Dili to inspect the situation with General Wiranto.\"",
	"event.ev_dili_flames.title": "Dili in Flames",
	"event.ev_eve_of_vote.date": "October 18, 1999",
	"event.ev_eve_of_vote.desc": "It is the night of October 18, 1999, less than twenty-four hours before the MPR votes by secret ballot to accept or reject your Accountability Speech. Across the eleven MPR factions, four have announced they will accept (Reformasi/PAN-PK, PBB, PDU, and FKKI), four have announced they will reject (PDI-P, PKB, KKI, and PDKB), leaving the entire survival of your presidency hanging on three decisive blocs: Golkar (120 seats), PPP (58 seats), and ABRI (38 seats), alongside the 200 regional and functional delegates. Then, two earthquakes strike within hours of each other: at 3:30 PM today, General Wiranto appeared on television to announce that after consulting the officer corps, he is declining your offer to run as your Vice Presidential candidate; and tonight at the Hotel Mulia, a rebel faction of roughly 40 Golkar delegates led by Akbar Tandjung and Marzuki Darusman ('Golkar Putih') is threatening to defect and vote 'Reject' tomorrow on secret ballot unless you pull their votes back into line at Patra Kuningan tonight.",
	"event.ev_eve_of_vote.opt.0.body": "Tempers exploded past midnight at President Habibie's private residence on Jalan Patra Kuningan as the President and A.A. Baramuli confronted Golkar Chairman Akbar Tandjung and Marzuki Darusman over reports that up to forty 'Golkar Putih' legislators intend to stab Habibie in the back during tomorrow's secret-ballot vote. Witnesses say shouting echoed into the courtyard as Sulawesi loyalists accused Akbar of treason; while Akbar emerged at 2:00 AM promising reporters that 'Golkar's official line remains to accept the speech,' nobody in Jakarta is sure what his lieutenants will actually mark once they step behind the curtain tomorrow.",
	"event.ev_eve_of_vote.opt.0.headline": "MALAM JAHANAM DI PATRA KUNINGAN: HABIBIE BENTAK AKBAR TANDJUNG DI DEPAN KADER GOLKAR",
	"event.ev_eve_of_vote.opt.0.text": "\"Summon Akbar Tandjung, Marzuki Darusman, and the entire Golkar MPR caucus to Patra Kuningan tonight: confront the 'Golkar Putih' defectors face-to-face and demand party discipline under the Banyan Tree for tomorrow's secret ballot.\"",
	"event.ev_eve_of_vote.opt.1.body": "Reeling from General Wiranto's 3:30 PM televised announcement declining to run as his Vice President, President Habibie pivoted in sheer desperation last night, summoning PPP Chairman Hamzah Haz and Central Axis leaders to Patra Kuningan to offer them the vacant number-two slot before tomorrow's vote. While PPP's 58 delegates and Yusril Ihza Mahendra's PBB welcomed the late-night courtship, critics mocked the spectacle of a sitting President peddling the Vice Presidency from door to door at midnight like a last-minute concert ticket.",
	"event.ev_eve_of_vote.opt.1.headline": "DITINGGAL WIRANTO SORE HARI, MALAM HARI HABIBIE TAWARKAN KURSI WAPRES KE POROS TENGAH",
	"event.ev_eve_of_vote.opt.1.text": "\"Pivot immediately after Wiranto's refusal: invite Amien Rais, Hamzah Haz, and Yusril Ihza Mahendra to Patra Kuningan and offer the Vice Presidency directly to the Central Axis and PPP in exchange for their undivided vote tomorrow.\"",
	"event.ev_eve_of_vote.opt.2.body": "Sleep was impossible inside the Hilton, Mulia, and Atlet Century Park hotels last night as operatives from President Habibie's [i]Tim Sukses[/i], led by A.A. Baramuli and Fadel Muhammad, went suite to suite knocking on the doors of outer-island and functional delegates ahead of today's secret ballot. Student monitors from Forum Kota camped in the hotel lobbies accused the Palace brokers of carrying briefcases of cash and project pledges to buy the 351-vote threshold before sunrise.",
	"event.ev_eve_of_vote.opt.2.headline": "OPERASI FAJAR DI HOTEL MULIA DAN HILTON! BROKER ISTANA GERILYA BELI SUARA UTUSAN DAERAH",
	"event.ev_eve_of_vote.opt.2.text": "\"Deploy A.A. Baramuli, Fadel Muhammad, and your floor whips across the hotel suites of the 135 Utusan Daerah and 65 Utusan Golongan delegates tonight to lock down every uncommitted regional and functional vote.\"",
	"event.ev_eve_of_vote.opt.3.body": "General Wiranto's dramatic afternoon press conference declining President Habibie's Vice Presidential offer stunned the Patra Kuningan camp, forcing Habibie into an urgent midnight meeting with Wiranto and ABRI Faction Chairman Lt. Gen. Hari Sabarno. While the generals assured the President that stepping back from the ticket was merely to keep the armed forces neutral and that the 38-seat military bloc will 'respect constitutional continuity' today, Senayan insiders note that Wiranto has carefully untied his own lifeboat from Habibie's hull just hours before the iceberg hits.",
	"event.ev_eve_of_vote.opt.3.headline": "WIRANTO TOLAK PINANGAN WAPRES, FRAKSI TNI/POLRI JADI KUNCI PENENTU NASIB HABIBIE HARI INI",
	"event.ev_eve_of_vote.opt.3.text": "\"Hold an urgent one-on-one meeting with General Wiranto and the ABRI faction leadership under Lt. Gen. Hari Sabarno to ensure that even though Wiranto declined the VP slot, ABRI's 38 delegates vote 'Accept' on your Accountability Speech.\"",
	"event.ev_eve_of_vote.opt.4.body": "While Akbar Tandjung's dissidents, Amien Rais's Central Axis, and Taufik Kiemas's operatives spent the night horse-trading furiously across the hotel suites of Senayan after General Wiranto's afternoon bombshell, President Habibie called off his floor whips and spent a quiet evening praying with his wife Ainun at Patra Kuningan. Even his fiercest critics in the press gallery admitted a grudging respect for his refusal to turn the final night into a cash auction, though in the shark tank of the 1999 MPR, a clear conscience counts for zero votes.",
	"event.ev_eve_of_vote.opt.4.headline": "AS SENAYAN BROKERS TRADE VOTES TILL DAWN, A LONELY PRESIDENT WAITS AT KUNINGAN",
	"event.ev_eve_of_vote.opt.4.text": "\"Reject the midnight hotel horse-trading entirely: spend the evening quietly at Patra Kuningan with Ibu Ainun and your closest family, trusting the 700 delegates of the MPR to judge your 512 days on their honest merits.\"",
	"event.ev_eve_of_vote.title": "Night of the Long Knives",
	"event.ev_imf_ultimatum.date": "August 12, 1999",
	"event.ev_imf_ultimatum.desc": "The Bank Bali scandal has rapidly escalated from a domestic political crisis into an international financial standoff. World Bank Country Director Mark Baird and IMF Asia-Pacific Director Hubert Neiss have formally notified Coordinating Minister Ginandjar Kartasasmita that all remaining bailout disbursements (over $1.4 billion in IMF, World Bank, and Asian Development Bank budgetary support) are suspended indefinitely. Their condition for resuming aid is non-negotiable: the international accounting firm PricewaterhouseCoopers (PwC) must be contracted to conduct an unrestricted forensic audit of the Bank Bali transaction, with full authority to trace every rupiah that flowed out of PT Era Giat Prima into the personal accounts of politicians, ministers, and MPR delegates, and the complete findings must be shared with the DPR and international creditors.",
	"event.ev_imf_ultimatum.opt.0.body": "Held over a barrel by Hubert Neiss and World Bank Director Mark Baird, President Habibie has capitulated unconditionally to Washington's demand for a unrestricted PricewaterhouseCoopers forensic audit of the Bank Bali scandal. While currency traders welcomed the move, domestic politicians across Senayan reacted with a mixture of humiliation and terror: nationalists blasted the government for letting foreign accountants subpoena sovereign central bank servers, while Golkar treasurers implicated in the Rp 546 billion EGP transfers are frantically shredding records before PwC's team walks through the door.",
	"event.ev_imf_ultimatum.opt.0.headline": "DEMI PENCAIRAN DANA IMF, ISTANA SERAHKAN KUNCI BRANKAS BANK INDONESIA KE AUDITOR ASING",
	"event.ev_imf_ultimatum.opt.0.text": "\"Grant PricewaterhouseCoopers unrestricted forensic access to trace the Bank Bali funds wherever they lead, and override any bank-secrecy objections from Bank Indonesia or IBRA. Restoring international financial trust comes before shielding any individual.\"",
	"event.ev_imf_ultimatum.opt.1.body": "Nobody in the diplomatic community is fooled by Bina Graha's clever legal maneuver placing the PricewaterhouseCoopers audit under the formal custody of Supreme Audit Agency (BPK) Chairman Billy Joedono. As DPR Commission VIII legislators pointed out immediately, routing the contract through BPK allows the government to invoke Article 18 of the BPK statute and Banking Secrecy laws the moment PwC's final report names Habibie's inner circle. The IMF's Hubert Neiss warned bluntly yesterday that unless the full, unredacted audit is published, not a single dollar of the frozen $1.4 billion tranche will be released.",
	"event.ev_imf_ultimatum.opt.1.headline": "PALACE HIDES BEHIND BPK SECRECY RULES TO KEEP CONTROL OF PWC AUDIT",
	"event.ev_imf_ultimatum.opt.1.text": "\"Authorize Supreme Audit Agency (BPK) Chairman Billy Joedono to hire PricewaterhouseCoopers under BPK's statutory auspices, granting PwC access to the banking records while keeping legal custody of the final report inside a sovereign Indonesian institution.\"",
	"event.ev_imf_ultimatum.opt.2.body": "Even a primary school student in Jakarta can do the calendar math behind President Habibie's request for a 'sixty-day domestic review' of the Bank Bali scandal: sixty days from August 12 lands conveniently after the October 19 MPR presidential election. International creditors and opposition MPs alike dismissed the proposal as a transparent cover-up designed to shield the President's [i]Tim Sukses[/i] until the ballots are cast. In response, the World Bank and IMF confirmed that the $1.4 billion aid freeze remains locked tight.",
	"event.ev_imf_ultimatum.opt.2.headline": "HABIBIE PLAYS CALENDAR GAMES TO BURY BALIGATE PAST OCTOBER VOTE",
	"event.ev_imf_ultimatum.opt.2.text": "\"Ask Hubert Neiss and Mark Baird for a sixty-day administrative window so BPK and the Attorney General's Office can complete their own domestic audit before any foreign accounting firm is handed subpoena power over Indonesian banks.\"",
	"event.ev_imf_ultimatum.opt.3.body": "Coordinating Minister Ginandjar Kartasasmita returned from Tokyo empty-handed and visibly embarrassed yesterday after Japanese Finance Ministry officials flatly refused to release New Miyazawa Initiative bridge loans to cover the IMF's Bank Bali freeze. Economist Sri Mulyani Indrawati criticized the abortive Tokyo mission as 'humiliating diplomatic panhandling,' noting that instead of cleaning up the Rp 546 billion rot inside his own campaign circle, Habibie sent his chief economic minister abroad to beg for a no-questions-asked bailout and got the door slammed in his face.",
	"event.ev_imf_ultimatum.opt.3.headline": "MENGEMIS KE TOKYO DITOLak MENTAH-MENTAH, JEPANG TUNDUK PADA SYARAT IMF",
	"event.ev_imf_ultimatum.opt.3.text": "\"Send Ginandjar Kartasasmita to Tokyo and the Miyazawa Initiative administrators to seek bilateral Japanese bridge financing, bypassing the IMF's political conditions in Washington.\"",
	"event.ev_imf_ultimatum.opt.4.body": "How convenient that Bina Graha only discovers 'anti-colonial economic sovereignty' when foreign auditors ask to inspect the bank accounts of Golkar's campaign treasurers! President Habibie's chest-thumping refusal to allow PricewaterhouseCoopers into Bank Bali drew loud applause from A.A. Baramuli's cronies in Senayan, but the bill for that bravado arrived on the currency markets within thirty minutes: the IMF and World Bank froze $1.4 billion in budget aid indefinitely, foreign funds dumped Jakarta equities, and ordinary Indonesians are left paying the price for a sovereignty speech designed to hide a Rp 546 billion slush fund.",
	"event.ev_imf_ultimatum.opt.4.headline": "SOK NASIONALIS DEMI TUTUPI KORUPSI! TOLAK AUDIT PWC, RUPIAH LANGSUNG TERJUN BEBAS",
	"event.ev_imf_ultimatum.opt.4.text": "\"Reject the ultimatum publicly. Indonesia is a sovereign republic with its own Supreme Audit Agency (BPK) and central bank; we will not hand private banking records over to foreign auditors as though we were a colonial dependency.\"",
	"event.ev_imf_ultimatum.title": "The IMF & World Bank Ultimatum",
	"event.ev_interfet_lands.date": "September 20, 1999",
	"event.ev_interfet_lands.desc": "Authorized five days ago by UN Security Council Resolution 1264, Australian Major General Peter Cosgrove and Thai Deputy Commander Major General Songkitti Jaggabatara have landed at Dili's Comoro Airport at the head of the first 2,500 troops of the International Force East Timor (INTERFET). Maj. Gen. Kiki Syahnakri's Indonesian forces have begun handing over security sector by sector, though sullen departing soldiers are burning barracks and looting fixtures as their transport ships load in Dili harbor. In Jakarta and Surabaya, television footage of Australian soldiers pointing rifles at disarmed militia members and Indonesian policemen has triggered an explosion of wounded nationalist fury. Demonstrators have fired shots at the Australian Embassy on Jalan Rasuna Said, burned Australian flags in Medan and Yogyakarta, and DPR Commission I members from both PDI-P and Golkar are demanding that you answer for 'humiliating the Red-and-White.'",
	"event.ev_interfet_lands.opt.0.body": "Photographs on every front page this morning showing Australian INTERFET paratroopers standing over hog-tied Timorese militiamen and Indonesian policemen with Steyr rifles have sent a wave of revulsion and fury across the country. When President Habibie's spokesman attempted to describe the handover at Comoro Airport as 'an orderly diplomatic success,' lawmakers in DPR Commission I erupted in jeers. 'Only B.J. Habibie could lose an entire province, watch foreign soldiers humiliate our uniform on global television, and ask for a round of applause,' snapped PDI-P legislator Permadi.",
	"event.ev_interfet_lands.opt.0.headline": "TENTARA KITA DITODONG SEPATU LARS AUSTRALIA, ISTANA MASIH SEBUT SUKSES DIPLOMASI!",
	"event.ev_interfet_lands.opt.0.text": "\"Instruct Maj. Gen. Kiki Syahnakri to execute a disciplined, professional handover to Maj. Gen. Cosgrove and Thai Deputy Commander Maj. Gen. Songkitti, while publicly emphasizing that Indonesia honored its international commitments and saved the nation from economic ruin.\"",
	"event.ev_interfet_lands.opt.1.body": "While East Nusa Tenggara Governor Piet Tallo welcomed Jakarta's emergency disbursement for the quarter-million refugees crammed into squalid camps across Atambua, Belu, and Kupang, reporters on the ground paint a grim picture of where the money is actually going. Armed Aitarak and Besi Merah Putih militiamen who fled across the border ahead of INTERFET have taken control of camp distribution points, intimidating both local NTT residents and Timorese families who were deported at gunpoint and now want to return home.",
	"event.ev_interfet_lands.opt.1.headline": "ATAMBUA DAN KUPANG LUMPUH KEBANJIRAN 250.000 PENGUNGSI, DANA BANTUAN DISUNAT MILISI",
	"event.ev_interfet_lands.opt.1.text": "\"Authorize an immediate humanitarian and resettlement fund through the Ministry of Social Affairs and West Timor Governor Piet Tallo to house and feed the 250,000 displaced persons and civil servants pouring across the border into Atambua and Kupang.\"",
	"event.ev_interfet_lands.opt.2.body": "With nationalist crowds burning Australian flags outside the embassy on Jalan Rasuna Said and taking potshots at diplomatic vehicles, Merdeka Palace has eagerly joined the chorus denouncing Prime Minister John Howard's 'deputy sheriff' arrogance. Yet political analysts in Jakarta note that the anti-Canberra outrage is a transparent diversion: 'John Howard did not sign the January 27 cabinet decision offering a referendum without preparing the military on the ground, B.J. Habibie did,' wrote columnist Christianto Wibisono.",
	"event.ev_interfet_lands.opt.2.headline": "PALACE RIDES ANTI-AUSTRALIAN WAVE TO DEFLECT BLAME FOR TIMOR DEBACLE",
	"event.ev_interfet_lands.opt.2.text": "\"Channel the public anger toward Canberra: formally abrogate the 1995 bilateral defense agreement with Australia, recall our ambassador for consultations, and protest Australian troop conduct at the UN.\"",
	"event.ev_interfet_lands.opt.3.body": "To head off a UN War Crimes Tribunal modeled on Yugoslavia and Rwanda, President Habibie has authorized Komnas HAM to form an independent domestic inquiry (KPP-HAM) featuring some of the military's fiercest critics, including Munir, Albert Hasibuan, and Todung Mulya Lubis. At Cilangkap headquarters, the announcement landed like a bombshell: senior generals whose names are already on KPP-HAM's witness list for the Suai and Dili massacres accuse Habibie of using the officer corps as human shields to save his own international reputation.",
	"event.ev_interfet_lands.opt.3.headline": "KPP-HAM TIMTIM DIBENTUK: PARA JENDERAL TUDING HABIBIE SERAHKAN LEHER TNI KE LSM",
	"event.ev_interfet_lands.opt.3.text": "\"Authorize Komnas HAM to establish the Commission of Inquiry into Human Rights Violations in East Timor (KPP-HAM), led by Albert Hasibuan, Todung Mulya Lubis, and Munir, so Indonesian investigators, rather than a foreign UN tribunal, hold perpetrators accountable.\"",
	"event.ev_interfet_lands.opt.4.body": "As foreign tanks roll through Dili, a city built over twenty-four years with trillions of rupiah in Indonesian tax money and the lives of thousands of soldiers, President Habibie's press office announced yesterday that the Palace has 'moved on' to domestic economic agendas and will take no further questions on East Timor. Cartoonists in this morning's papers depicted the President whistling past a graveyard with his fingers plugged firmly in his ears, while MPR faction leaders promised that East Timor will be Question Number One when he steps to the podium on October 14.",
	"event.ev_interfet_lands.opt.4.headline": "TIMTIM LEPAS, ISTANA PURA-PURA PIKUN!",
	"event.ev_interfet_lands.opt.4.text": "\"Pivot the Palace's public schedule entirely back to domestic economic recovery and the upcoming MPR session, declining all further press questions on East Timor.\"",
	"event.ev_interfet_lands.title": "INTERFET Lands in Dili",
	"event.ev_intl_sanctions.date": "September 10, 1999",
	"event.ev_intl_sanctions.desc": "At the APEC Leaders' Summit in Auckland, which you declined to attend in person, dispatching Coordinating Minister Ginandjar Kartasasmita and Foreign Minister Ali Alatas in your stead, world leaders have turned the summit into an emergency tribunal on East Timor. Yesterday, US President Bill Clinton suspended all US-Indonesian military sales and Pentagon cooperation, warning bluntly that 'if Indonesia does not end the violence, it must invite the international community to assist in restoring security.' Today, the European Union imposed an arms embargo, the IMF froze its scheduled September mission to Jakarta, and UN Secretary-General Kofi Annan gave Jakarta a forty-eight-hour ultimatum to accept an Australian-led multinational force or face binding UN Security Council Chapter VII enforcement and economic isolation. Tomorrow morning, General Wiranto will fly to Dili alongside the five-member UN Security Council delegation led by Ambassador Martin Andjaba.",
	"event.ev_intl_sanctions.opt.0.body": "Walking through the blackened ruins of Dili alongside five furious UN Security Council ambassadors yesterday finally forced General Wiranto to confront the diplomatic abyss facing Indonesia, but the subsequent midnight cabinet session at Merdeka Palace was anything but harmonious. According to two ministers in the room, civilian technocrats warned that Indonesia is forty-eight hours away from an international banking freeze, while military commanders bitterly blamed Habibie's January referendum impulse for putting the armed forces in an impossible position.",
	"event.ev_intl_sanctions.opt.0.headline": "PERTEMUAN TEGANG DI ISTANA USAI KUNJUNGAN DILI: HABIBIE DAN WIRANTO SALING LEMPAR TANGGUNG JAWAB",
	"event.ev_intl_sanctions.opt.0.text": "\"Order General Wiranto to accompany the UN Security Council ambassadors to Dili tomorrow morning so he sees the burned city and the international fury with his own eyes, then convene the full political and security cabinet to force Cilangkap's agreement to peacekeepers.\"",
	"event.ev_intl_sanctions.opt.1.body": "Foreign Minister Ali Alatas's frantic lobbying for Thai, Filipino, and Malaysian contingents to join the incoming East Timor force has given Merdeka Palace a thin diplomatic fig leaf to sell to the domestic public. Yet nobody in Canberra or Senayan is under any illusion about who will actually run the operation: with 4,500 Australian combat troops already staging in Darwin under Maj. Gen. Peter Cosgrove, DPR nationalists mocked the Palace's 'ASEAN peacekeeping' spin as putting a Southeast Asian bumper sticker on an Australian armored column.",
	"event.ev_intl_sanctions.opt.1.headline": "PALACE SCRAMBLES FOR ASEAN FIG LEAF AS AUSTRALIAN TROOPS STAGE IN DARWIN",
	"event.ev_intl_sanctions.opt.1.text": "\"Instruct Ali Alatas in New York to lobby for strong ASEAN participation (Thailand, the Philippines, Malaysia, and Singapore) inside any UN force so the deployment is not purely an Anglo-Australian occupation.\"",
	"event.ev_intl_sanctions.opt.2.body": "Youths from Pemuda Pancasila and nationalist student fronts cheered outside the US and Australian embassies yesterday after President Habibie blasted Western 'hypocrisy' on television. Down at Tanjung Priok port and across Jakarta's banking district, however, the cost of that rhetoric is already devastating: international correspondent banks refused to honor Indonesian letters of credit this morning, container ships diverted to Singapore, and the IMF warned that Jakarta is hurtling toward Yugoslav-style pariah status.",
	"event.ev_intl_sanctions.opt.2.headline": "pidato Konfrontasi HABIBIE DISORAKI PENDEMO, TAPI PELABUHAN DAN PERBANKAN LUMPUH",
	"event.ev_intl_sanctions.opt.2.text": "\"Go before the cameras to denounce Washington and Canberra's hypocrisy, pointing out that Western powers supported Indonesia's annexation in 1975 and have no right to threaten 210 million Indonesians with economic starvation now.\"",
	"event.ev_intl_sanctions.opt.3.body": "For twenty-four years Veteran Foreign Minister Ali Alatas has had to defend Indonesia's East Timor policy before skeptical UN chambers, calling it 'a pebble in Indonesia's shoe.' Yesterday in New York, that pebble became a boulder: Kofi Annan and the Security Council flatly rejected Alatas's plea to give Maj. Gen. Kiki Syahnakri's martial law another week, telling the exhausted minister that Jakarta has until Sunday night to accept international peacekeepers unconditionally or face Chapter VII enforcement.",
	"event.ev_intl_sanctions.opt.3.headline": "MISI MUSTAHIL ALI ALATAS: MENJUAL DARURAT MILITER DI MARKAS PBB YANG MARAH",
	"event.ev_intl_sanctions.opt.3.text": "\"Send Foreign Minister Ali Alatas on an emergency flight to UN Headquarters in New York to plead for another week of Indonesian martial law under Maj. Gen. Kiki Syahnakri before any UN resolution is drafted.\"",
	"event.ev_intl_sanctions.opt.4.body": "Off-the-record briefings by Palace aides to Western wire services claiming that President Habibie is 'a prisoner of his own generals' backfired with devastating force this morning when the quotes were splashed across every front page in Jakarta. Instead of winning sympathy, the leak has made Habibie look pitifully weak to MPR delegates while provoking outrage at Cilangkap, where ABRI spokesman Brig. Gen. Sudrajat barked that 'a Supreme Commander who slanders his own officer corps to foreign reporters has lost the moral authority to lead.'",
	"event.ev_intl_sanctions.opt.4.headline": "PRESIDEN CURHAT KE WARTAWAN ASING TAKUT DIKUDETA: PANGLIMA TERTINGGI MACAM APA?",
	"event.ev_intl_sanctions.opt.4.text": "\"Brief foreign correspondents off the record that civilian leadership wants to invite UN peacekeepers immediately, but is being held hostage by hardline generals threatening a coup if foreign soldiers land.\"",
	"event.ev_intl_sanctions.title": "Sanctions Ultimatum",
	"event.ev_islamic_concessions.date": "Late-July 1999",
	"event.ev_islamic_concessions.desc": "With the KPU vote tally confirming that PDI-P has won 153 seats to Golkar's 120, the parliamentary mathematics for October has crystallized. Neither Megawati nor Golkar can reach the 351-vote threshold in the 700-seat MPR alone. Recognizing this deadlock first, PAN Chairman Amien Rais has begun floating the idea of a 'Poros Tengah' (Central Axis), an alliance of Islamic parties bridging modernist and traditionalist divides, while delegations from Hamzah Haz's PPP (58 seats), Yusril Ihza Mahendra's PBB (13 seats), and Nur Mahmudi Ismail's Justice Party (7 seats) have been arriving at Merdeka Palace with concrete legislative demands.\n\nChief among them are immediate passage of the Hajj Administration Bill (RUU Penyelenggaraan Ibadah Haji) and the Zakat Management Bill (RUU Pengelolaan Zakat), alongside a quiet understanding that ICMI and Muslim parties will hold key portfolios if they block Megawati in October.",
	"event.ev_islamic_concessions.opt.0.body": "While Islamic organizations across the archipelago welcomed the swift passage of Law No. 17/1999 on Hajj Administration and Law No. 38/1999 on Zakat Management, political analysts in Senayan warn that President Habibie is sorely mistaken if he thinks statutory favors will buy him the unconditional loyalty of the emerging Central Axis. Speaking to reporters after Friday prayers, PAN Chairman Amien Rais praised the legislation as overdue, before pointedly adding that 'the Ummah needs a clean new national leadership, not merely a few religious bills signed by a beleaguered incumbent.'",
	"event.ev_islamic_concessions.opt.0.headline": "UU HAJI DAN ZAKAT DISAHKAN, POROS TENGAH TETAP ENGGAN JADI STEMPEL HABIBIE",
	"event.ev_islamic_concessions.opt.0.text": "\"Fast-track the Hajj Administration Act (UU No. 17/1999) and the Zakat Management Act (UU No. 38/1999) through the DPR immediately, delivering concrete reforms for the Ummah without reopening divisive constitutional debates over the Jakarta Charter.\"",
	"event.ev_islamic_concessions.opt.1.body": "Details of a closed-door meeting at Merdeka Palace between President Habibie's inner circle and hardline Islamic party negotiators have sparked outrage across nationalist and minority communities. By dangling ministerial portfolios and tacit support for sectarian fatwas against a female presidency solely to block PDI-P's 34 percent plurality, Habibie is accused of playing with primordial fire. Even Nahdlatul Ulama Chairman Abdurrahman Wahid blasted the maneuver yesterday, warning that politicians who weaponize religion to cling to office are dragging the Republic toward a dangerous sectarian precipice.",
	"event.ev_islamic_concessions.opt.1.headline": "POLITIK DAGANG SAPI SEKTarian DI ISTANA DEMI JEGAL MEGAWATI",
	"event.ev_islamic_concessions.opt.1.text": "\"Go further behind closed doors with PPP and PBB leaders. Signal openness to provincial sharia regulations and promise key religious and economic ministries in October in exchange for an explicit front against Megawati.\"",
	"event.ev_islamic_concessions.opt.2.body": "President Habibie's refusal to entertain concessions to PPP and the modernist Islamic caucus has triggered bitter recriminations among the very ICMI and DDII networks that once championed him as their champion in the Palace. Preachers at Al-Azhar Mosque accused the President of betraying the Ummah to appease Western embassies and secularists; yet PDI-P's leadership on Jalan Diponegoro showed zero gratitude in return, noting that Habibie's sudden embrace of pluralist nationalism is merely the panic of a man watching his coalition math evaporate.",
	"event.ev_islamic_concessions.opt.2.headline": "DITINGGAL KANAN, DITOLAK KIRI: DILEMA HABIBIE USAI TOLAK TUNTUTAN PARTAI ISLAM",
	"event.ev_islamic_concessions.opt.2.text": "\"Some constitutional foundations are not available for horse-trading, whatever the dynamics of the October session looks like. Reaffirm Pancasila as the sole non-sectarian foundation of the state and reach out to both pluralist NU clerics and secular nationalists.\"",
	"event.ev_islamic_concessions.opt.3.body": "Before the newly elected members of parliament have even had their official suits measured, Bina Graha's political brokers are already running a wholesale clearance auction on DPR commission chairmanships! In a transparent bid to bribe Hamzah Haz's PPP and minor Islamic parties away from Amien Rais's Central Axis, Palace emissaries have been promising parliamentary perks using the exact same patronage playbook Suharto used for thirty years. 'They take the perks at noon and still meet Amien Rais at midnight, Habibie is being fleeced by professional politicians,' one senior DPR staffer laughed.",
	"event.ev_islamic_concessions.opt.3.headline": "BELUM APA-APA UDAH BAGI-BAGI KURSI! ISTANA OBROL JABATAN KOMISI DPR",
	"event.ev_islamic_concessions.opt.3.text": "\"Use DPR committee leadership allocations and advisory posts to court PPP and the smaller Islamic parties directly through Golkar's parliamentary whips, keeping them tied to the Palace rather than to Amien Rais's independent axis.\"",
	"event.ev_islamic_concessions.opt.4.body": "An amateurish attempt by Palace operatives to whisper anti-Muhammadiyah warnings to PKB kiai while feeding anti-NU rumors to PAN cadres has blown up spectacularly in the President's face. Appearing side by side before reporters in Ciganjur yesterday, Abdurrahman Wahid and Amien Rais openly mocked the Palace's 'colonial divide-and-rule' intrigue. Far from splitting the traditionalist and modernist camps, the clumsy interference has given Gus Dur and Amien Rais a shared target, accelerating the very Central Axis consolidation Bina Graha feared.",
	"event.ev_islamic_concessions.opt.4.headline": "POLITIK ADU DOMBA ISTANA TERBACA, GUS DUR DAN AMIEN RAIS JUSTRU SEMAKIN RAPAT",
	"event.ev_islamic_concessions.opt.4.text": "\"Play on the deep historical rivalry between traditionalist Nahdlatul Ulama (PKB) and modernist Muhammadiyah (PAN) to prevent Amien Rais and Gus Dur from ever uniting behind a single alternative candidate.\"",
	"event.ev_islamic_concessions.title": "The Islamic Caucus",
	"event.ev_megawati_push.date": "October 13, 1999",
	"event.ev_megawati_push.desc": "Tomorrow night you will stand before the 700 delegates of the MPR to deliver your Pidato Pertanggungjawaban. Outside the Senayan parliamentary complex, the atmosphere has reached a boiling point: over a hundred thousand PDI-P supporters, wearing red headbands and waving Banteng flags, have converged with student coalitions along Jalan Gatot Subroto, pressing against massive coils of razor wire, water cannons, and 30,000 Kostrad, Marines, and Brimob troops deployed by General Wiranto. Meanwhile, inside your own camp at Patra Kuningan, your strategists are urging a bold preemptive move before tomorrow night's speech: formally announce General Wiranto as your running mate for Vice President on the 1999–2004 ticket, locking in ABRI's 38 seats and forcing Golkar's wavering nationalist wing under Akbar Tandjung to stay in line.",
	"event.ev_megawati_push.opt.0.body": "On the eve of his Accountability Speech, President Habibie has played his final trump card by publicly proposing Armed Forces Commander General Wiranto as his Vice Presidential running mate for 1999–2004. Yet while deploying the pink-bereted Marines eased tensions with students along Jalan Gatot Subroto, Wiranto's own response to the marriage proposal was conspicuously frigid: rather than accepting on the spot, the general told reporters he 'needs to consult the officer corps and weigh the national interest first', leaving Habibie hanging in public view like an anxious suitor.",
	"event.ev_megawati_push.opt.0.headline": "LAMARAN TERBUKA HABIBIE KEPADA WIRANTO: MANUVER PUTUS ASA ATAU TIKET PENYELAMAT?",
	"event.ev_megawati_push.opt.0.text": "\"Announce publicly that you have asked General Wiranto to stand as your Vice Presidential running mate for 1999–2004, while instructing the Marines, whom the students respect, to man the front lines at Senayan without live ammunition.\"",
	"event.ev_megawati_push.opt.1.body": "After a late-night visit from Palace emissaries promising an unrigged MPR ballot and dangling a power-sharing cabinet, PDI-P Chairwoman Megawati Sukarnoputri instructed her red-shirted Satgas commanders outside Senayan to pull back from the razor wire and avoid clashes with the Marines. Inside the chamber, however, PDI-P faction leader Dimyati Hartono made clear that peaceful streets will not buy Habibie a single pardon on the floor tomorrow night: 'We will keep our supporters calm outside so the world can watch us reject his speech cleanly inside.'",
	"event.ev_megawati_push.opt.1.headline": "UTUSAN MALAM ISTANA KE KEBAGUSAN: MEGAWATI TENANGKAN MASSA, TAPI TOLAK KOMPROMI PIDATO",
	"event.ev_megawati_push.opt.1.text": "\"Send a personal emissary to Megawati Sukarnoputri and Taufik Kiemas tonight: pledge a clean, democratic vote in the MPR without military intimidation, and offer PDI-P a co-governing coalition if your Accountability Speech is accepted.\"",
	"event.ev_megawati_push.opt.2.body": "Speaking directly into the television cameras last night, President Habibie reminded the nation that tomorrow night's [i]Pidato Pertanggungjawaban[/i] marks the first time since 1955 that an Indonesian head of state will stand before an unscripted parliament that actually has the power to fire him. While civic intellectuals acknowledged the democratic milestone, the sea of red-shirted Banteng supporters and student marchers camped around the Senayan Hilton drowned out the broadcast on giant outdoor screens with deafening chants of [i]'Tolak! Tolak! Tolak!'[/i]",
	"event.ev_megawati_push.opt.2.headline": "HABIBIE PLEADS FOR FAIR HEARING AS 100,000 PROTESTERS RING SENAYAN",
	"event.ev_megawati_push.opt.2.text": "\"Go on national television and radio tonight to address the students and citizens outside Senayan directly, reminding them that you are standing before the MPR tomorrow under truly democratic rules for the first time in 44 years.\"",
	"event.ev_megawati_push.opt.3.body": "Nothing signals a collapsing regime faster than moving the furniture out of the capital. Word that Bina Graha quietly shifted executive secretariat operations fifty kilometers south to Bogor Palace yesterday as 100,000 PDI-P supporters and students surrounded Senayan triggered immediate mockery across the MPR floor. 'Sukarno went to Bogor in March 1966 right before Supersemar, and Suharto wanted to go to Bogor in May 1998; now Habibie is following the exact same exit map,' one Golkar dissident whispered to reporters at the Hotel Mulia.",
	"event.ev_megawati_push.opt.3.headline": "BELUM DISIDANG SUDAH NGUNGSI KE BOGOR! NYALI ISTANA CIUT LIHAT LAUTAN MERAH DI SENAYAN",
	"event.ev_megawati_push.opt.3.text": "\"Move executive cabinet operations temporarily to Bogor Palace for security continuity while General Wiranto's security ring seals off central Jakarta.\"",
	"event.ev_megawati_push.opt.4.body": "Central Jakarta looked like a war zone at dawn today after Brimob riot squads and armored water cannons stormed student and PDI-P encampments along Jalan Gatot Subroto and the Semanggi flyover on orders from the Palace. Over a hundred bloodied demonstrators were carried into Atma Jaya and Jakarta Hospital as tear-gas canisters detonated inside the Hilton Hotel compound where MPR delegates are sleeping, ensuring that when President Habibie walks into the Plenary Hall tonight, the chamber will be waiting for him with pure venom.",
	"event.ev_megawati_push.opt.4.headline": "SENAYAN BANJIR DARAH DAN GAS AIR MATA H-1 PIDATO HABIBIE!",
	"event.ev_megawati_push.opt.4.text": "\"Order Kodam Jaya and Brimob to clear Jalan Gatot Subroto and the Semanggi approaches by force tonight so MPR delegates do not have to pass a single red flag tomorrow morning.\"",
	"event.ev_megawati_push.title": "Barricades at Senayan",
	"event.ev_peacekeeper_decision.date": "September 12, 1999",
	"event.ev_peacekeeper_decision.desc": "It is Sunday evening, September 12, 1999, the single most consequential night of your presidency. The UN Security Council delegation has just met with you at Merdeka Palace after returning from the burned ruins of Dili, and Kofi Annan's forty-eight-hour deadline expires tonight. Across the cabinet table sit General Wiranto, Foreign Minister Ali Alatas, Coordinating Ministers Ginandjar Kartasasmita and Feisal Tanjung, and the service chiefs of the Army, Navy, Air Force, and Police. If you refuse an international peacekeeping force tonight, the UN Security Council will invoke Chapter VII sanctions tomorrow, the IMF will terminate Indonesia's bailout, and the economy will collapse. If you accept unconditionally on live television, nationalist factions across the MPR will brand you the President who lost East Timor and invited foreign boots onto archipelago soil.",
	"event.ev_peacekeeper_decision.opt.0.body": "At 7:30 PM last night at Merdeka Palace, a visibly exhausted President Habibie went before live television cameras to announce that he had telephoned UN Secretary-General Kofi Annan to invite an international peacekeeping force into East Timor immediately. While the decision averts catastrophic economic sanctions, no viewer in Indonesia missed the body language behind the podium: General Wiranto stood stone-faced with his jaw clenched, staring straight ahead without uttering a word. In Senayan this morning, both PDI-P nationalists and Golkar's Akbar Tandjung faction called the broadcast 'the funeral march of Habibie's re-election campaign.'",
	"event.ev_peacekeeper_decision.opt.0.headline": "INDONESIA AKHIRNYA TERIMA PASUKAN PBB: WAJAH KAKU WIRANTO DI BELAKANG HABIBIE BUKA TABIR RETAKNYA ISTANA",
	"event.ev_peacekeeper_decision.opt.0.text": "\"Phone Kofi Annan personally to invite a UN-mandated peacekeeping force, then walk out to the Merdeka Palace microphones at 7:30 PM flanked by General Wiranto and the entire cabinet to announce the decision together on live national television.\"",
	"event.ev_peacekeeper_decision.opt.1.body": "The conspicuous absence of General Wiranto and the military service chiefs from Merdeka Palace during President Habibie's Sunday night broadcast inviting UN peacekeepers into East Timor sent a chill through Jakarta's political establishment. Across Java this morning, nationalist protesters burned effigies of Habibie wearing an Australian slouch hat, while inside the MPR corridors, ABRI and Golkar delegates openly declared that a President who humiliates the armed forces on live television will never survive the October 19 accountability vote.",
	"event.ev_peacekeeper_decision.opt.1.headline": "HABIBIE TAMPIL SENDIRI SERAHKAN TIMTIM KE PBB, PARA JENDERAL BOIKOT SIARAN ISTANA",
	"event.ev_peacekeeper_decision.opt.1.text": "\"Announce the invitation for UN peacekeepers alone from the presidential study as a matter of civilian moral conscience, and order an immediate unilateral withdrawal of all ABRI units from East Timor without waiting for joint handover protocols.\"",
	"event.ev_peacekeeper_decision.opt.2.body": "Tearing up the 1995 bilateral defense treaty with Canberra on the same night Jakarta bowed to the UN Security Council's ultimatum on East Timor may have given wounded nationalists a symbolic bone to chew on, but commentators were quick to point out the hollowness of the gesture. 'Habibie is slamming the door on John Howard right after handing him the keys to Dili airport,' DPR Commission I member Yasril Ananta Baharuddin remarked acidly.",
	"event.ev_peacekeeper_decision.opt.2.headline": "ROBEK PERJANJIAN KEAMANAN DENGAN AUSTRALIA: HIBURAN KECIL DI TENGAH KEHILANGAN PROVINSI KE-27",
	"event.ev_peacekeeper_decision.opt.2.text": "\"Accept the UN peacekeeping force in principle, but pair it with the immediate abrogation of the 1995 Australia-Indonesia Security Agreement and demand that ASEAN commanders share leadership of the incoming force.\"",
	"event.ev_peacekeeper_decision.opt.3.body": "According to multiple cabinet sources, President Habibie only forced the generals' signature on the UN peacekeeping invitation yesterday evening by slamming his fist on the Bina Graha table and threatening to resign on the spot, which under the constitution would have dumped an immediate economic collapse and UN embargo into the lap of the triumvirate of ministers. While the ultimatum forced Wiranto to blink, word that Habibie is already talking about resigning has spread like wildfire through Senayan, convincing wavering Golkar delegates that the President is a lame duck.",
	"event.ev_peacekeeper_decision.opt.3.headline": "ANCAMAN MUNDUR DI MEJA KABINET: SENJATA TERAKHIR PRESIDEN YANG TERKEPUNG",
	"event.ev_peacekeeper_decision.opt.3.text": "\"Threaten across the cabinet table to resign the presidency tonight and hand the collapsing currency and UN sanctions directly to General Wiranto if the armed forces refuse to endorse the peacekeeping deployment.\"",
	"event.ev_peacekeeper_decision.opt.4.body": "President Habibie's Sunday night refusal to admit UN peacekeepers into East Timor has triggered the worst diplomatic and financial catastrophe in modern Indonesian history. At midnight in New York, the UN Security Council began drafting binding Chapter VII economic sanctions; the IMF and World Bank suspended all operations in Jakarta; and the rupiah crashed past Rp 10,000 per dollar at the Monday morning open as panic-stricken citizens queued outside banks to withdraw their savings.",
	"event.ev_peacekeeper_decision.opt.4.headline": "INDONESIA PLUNGES INTO GLOBAL ISOLATION AS HABIBIE DEFIES UN SECURITY COUNCIL",
	"event.ev_peacekeeper_decision.opt.4.text": "\"Defy Kofi Annan's ultimatum: reject foreign peacekeepers outright and order Maj. Gen. Kiki Syahnakri's martial law command to seal East Timor's borders against any unauthorized foreign landing.\"",
	"event.ev_peacekeeper_decision.title": "The September 12 Peacekeeper Decision",
	"event.ev_post_election.date": "June 14, 1999",
	"event.ev_post_election.desc": "It has been a week since the ballots closed, and Jakarta still feels suspended in mid-air. On June 7, more than 105 million citizens turned out at over 300,000 polling stations for the first freely contested parliamentary election since 1955, a logistical triumph conducted by General Rudini's 53-member General Election Commission (KPU) without the widespread bloodshed many had feared. Now the manual counting drags on village by village, kecamatan by kecamatan, while television crews camp outside the KPU headquarters on Jalan Imam Bonjol waiting for numbers that trickle in painfully slowly.\n\nWhat is already unmistakable from the early tallies across Java and Bali is dire for the Palace. Megawati Sukarnoputri's PDI-P is surging toward roughly a third of the national vote, nearly twelve points ahead of Golkar in second place. Red-shirted Banteng crowds are already celebrating along Jalan Thamrin as though the presidency itself has been decided, even though under the 1945 Constitution the street does not elect the president; the 700-member MPR does, four months from now. With small parties in the KPU already threatening to refuse certification over alleged irregularities, your advisors are divided on what signal Merdeka Palace should send.",
	"event.ev_post_election.opt.0.body": "While Merdeka Palace hides behind procedural pieties and promises to let General Rudini's deadlocked commission finish its glacial count, political observers are calling the President's silence by its real name: shell-shock. Even the Palace's hint that it may validate the tally by decree if minor parties refuse to sign has drawn immediate suspicion from Diponegoro, where PDI-P cadres warn that every day of bureaucratic delay at the KPU is another twenty-four hours for Golkar brokers to buy off regional delegates before October.",
	"event.ev_post_election.opt.0.headline": "ISTANA MEMBISU DI TENGAH KEMACETAN KPU, SINYAL KELUMPUHAN POLITIK?",
	"event.ev_post_election.opt.0.text": "\"Patience has served this transition well, and I see no reason to abandon it now. General Rudini's commission deserves the chance to finish its count undisturbed, and if the small parties deadlock the certification later, this office will step in by decree to validate the people's vote.\"",
	"event.ev_post_election.opt.1.body": "Foreign embassies may be applauding President Habibie's hasty congratulations to Megawati Sukarnoputri as 'statesmanlike,' but inside Golkar's Slipi headquarters the gesture is being denounced as an act of political self-harm. Senior regional chairmen who spent months defending the Banyan Tree against street mobs in Java told this newspaper that the President has effectively surrendered the moral mandate to PDI-P before a single MPR seat has been negotiated. Meanwhile, PDI-P Deputy Secretary-General Pramono Anung dismissed the olive branch with cold derision: 'If Pak Habibie truly respects our victory, he can start packing his model airplanes at Patra Kuningan rather than sending flowers.'",
	"event.ev_post_election.opt.1.headline": "HABIBIE MENGALAH SEBELUM BERTANDING",
	"event.ev_post_election.opt.1.text": "\"A leader ought to read a room honestly, even when the reading is uncomfortable. Whatever shape the final district tallies take, PDI-P's plurality at the ballot box is unmistakable, and I would rather congratulate Ibu Megawati on a historic democratic showing now than pretend otherwise.\"",
	"event.ev_post_election.opt.2.body": "Barely a week after 105 million Indonesians stood in the sun to bury the New Order at the ballot box, Pak Habibie has unveiled his newest magic trick! Explaining to the public that elections don't actually choose presidents! By hiding behind the 700-seat MPR (where 238 appointed military, regional, and functional delegates sit waiting to be lobbied), Habibie has signaled that he intends to overturn Megawati's landslide through backroom engineering. 'This is classic Suharto legalism spoken in Aachen terminology,' student leaders from FORKOT declared outside the DPR gates yesterday, warning that if Senayan subverts the popular vote in October, Jakarta will burn hotter than May 1998.",
	"event.ev_post_election.opt.2.headline": "KALAU KALAH YA KALAH SAJA! AKAL-AKALAN KONSTITUSI ALA HABIBIE",
	"event.ev_post_election.opt.2.text": "\"The numbers from the DPR ballot tell you one thing, and the presidency, under the 1945 Constitution this Republic operates by, is decided in October by 700 delegates in the MPR, not by a one-third plurality in June. I would ask everyone to resist premature certainty.\"",
	"event.ev_post_election.opt.3.body": "In the air-conditioned briefing rooms of Bina Graha, the President and his Sulawesi confidant A.A. Baramuli are comforted by maps showing Golkar sweeping 60 percent of the vote across Bone, Parepare, and Kupang. Out on the streets of Java, where two-thirds of the Republic actually lives, that math reads like dangerous delusion. Within forty-eight hours of the Palace's boast that outer-island seats will offset PDI-P's Java landslide, furious crowds in Solo and Surabaya pelted three district Golkar offices with stones. Commentator Andi Mallarangeng noted that pitting outer-island seat weights against Java's popular vote is a reckless gamble with national cohesion purely to salvage one man's job.",
	"event.ev_post_election.opt.3.headline": "MENGHITUNG KURSI DI ATAS POHON BERINGIN YANG RETAK",
	"event.ev_post_election.opt.3.text": "\"Wait for the outer island tallies from Sulawesi, Sumatra, and Nusa Tenggara before allowing Jakarta media networks to crown a winner. Golkar's regional machinery remains the backbone of the archipelago, and the party deserves to hear that confidence from the Palace.\"",
	"event.ev_post_election.opt.4.body": "What was intended as a clandestine midnight overture to Taufik Kiemas at Jalan Kebagusan leaked to the press corps before the Palace envoy's sedan had even cleared South Jakarta. While Kiemas himself heard the emissary out over coffee, PDI-P's nationalist hardliners wasted no time weaponizing the visit as proof that Habibie knows his candidacy is dead on arrival. Worse, word of the secret approach has triggered immediate paranoia inside Golkar Chairman Akbar Tandjung's camp, where senior MPs are asking aloud whether the President is preparing to sell out his own party's speakership ambitions to buy personal clemency from Megawati.",
	"event.ev_post_election.opt.4.headline": "PALACE BACKCHANNEL TO DIPONEGORO EXPOSED AS SIGN OF PANIC",
	"event.ev_post_election.opt.4.text": "\"Before positions calcify into camps neither side can walk back from, send a discreet envoy to Taufik Kiemas and the Diponegoro circle, not a press conference, just an early conversation about how the Republic is governed after October.\"",
	"event.ev_post_election.title": "Post-Election Reality",
	"event.ev_press_freedom.date": "June 28, 1999",
	"event.ev_press_freedom.desc": "Your decision last year to instruct Information Minister Lt. Gen. Muhammad Yunus Yosfiah to abolish the dreaded SIUPP publishing-license revocations, the New Order's favorite garrote against independent journalism, has unleashed an explosion of print and broadcast media that nobody in the bureaucracy knows how to contain. In less than twelve months, the number of licensed publications has rocketed from 289 to over 1,600. Tabloids, investigative weeklies like Tempo (back in print after its 1994 ban), and raucous radio call-in shows now lampoon your voice, your gestures, and your cabinet daily, routinely printing the phrase 'Suharto's lingering shadow' as though it were your official title. More alarmingly for Cilangkap, classified cabinet minutes on state bank recapitalizations and leaked ABRI telegrams on troop deployments in Aceh and East Timor are turning up verbatim on front pages. With the draft Press Bill (RUU Pers) now moving toward the DPR floor, security chiefs are pressing you to reinsert 'national security' licensing controls before press freedom is permanently locked into statute.",
	"event.ev_press_freedom.opt.0.body": "Even as editors across Jakarta welcome the fast-tracking of the Press Bill, which permanently outlaws [i]bredel[/i] (newspaper bans) and strips the Ministry of Information of its licensing whip, few in the press gallery are buying the Palace's sudden conversion to Lockean liberalism at face value. 'A drowning president is throwing lifebuoys to the journalists hoping we will forget he spent twenty years sitting silently in Suharto's cabinet every time Tempo, DeTIK, and Sinar Harapan were being strangled,' wrote columnist Goenawan Mohamad. Meanwhile, senior generals at Cilangkap have privately blasted the bill as an act of institutional disarmament that leaves state secrets defenseless.",
	"event.ev_press_freedom.opt.0.headline": "UU PERS DIKEBUT DEMI SIMPATI OKTOBER: MONUMEN ATAU MANUVER?",
	"event.ev_press_freedom.opt.0.text": "\"Rather than referee newsroom disputes week by week for the rest of my term, let us codify the abolition of censorship once and for all. Push the new Press Bill (UU Pers) through the DPR with a total ban on newspaper closures and an independent Press Council.\"",
	"event.ev_press_freedom.opt.1.body": "Fifteen chief editors were summoned to Bina Graha yesterday for what was billed as an 'informal luncheon,' only to be subjected to a two-hour monologue from the President on the difference between 'responsible freedom' and 'anarchy.' According to three editors in attendance, Habibie's rambling appeal to stop printing leaked military and banking memoranda sounded suspiciously like the old New Order [i]budaya telepon[/i] (telephone censorship), merely translated into polite German-engineered jargon. The Alliance of Independent Journalists (AJI) issued a blistering statement within an hour of dessert, declaring that the press answers to the public, not to Palace dinner invitations.",
	"event.ev_press_freedom.opt.1.headline": "KULIAH DUA JAM DI BINA GRAHA: BUDAYA TELEPON GAYA BARU",
	"event.ev_press_freedom.opt.1.text": "\"I have no interest in reviving the old SIUPP bans, and I want that understood clearly. But there is a difference between freedom and recklessness, and an off-the-record luncheon at Bina Graha with the chief editors might establish some ground rules on classified military cables.\"",
	"event.ev_press_freedom.opt.2.body": "President Habibie's refusal to prosecute newspapers publishing classified ABRI operational cables from Aceh and East Timor has triggered a quiet revolt inside military intelligence. Senior officers at BAIS and Cilangkap headquarters told Forum this week that the Palace is sacrificing operational security on the altar of Western diplomatic applause. Worse, leaving the tabloid press completely unchecked has done nothing to soften their coverage of the President himself. This morning's newsstands still feature caricatures of Habibie as a wind-up toy spinning out of control while his own ministries leak against each other.",
	"event.ev_press_freedom.opt.2.headline": "CILANGKAP GERAH: ISTANA BIARKAN RAHASIA NEGARA DITELANJANGI PERS",
	"event.ev_press_freedom.opt.2.text": "\"Whatever personal discomfort these caricatures bring me, and I will admit there has been plenty, Information Minister Yunus Yosfiah has my full backing to leave the newsrooms completely untouched, even when they print leaked cabinet memos.\"",
	"event.ev_press_freedom.opt.3.body": "Viewers tuning into TVRI's 7:00 PM [i]Dunia Dalam Berita[/i] this week were treated to an eerie blast from the New Order past. Thirty minutes of glowing, uncritical state broadcasts praising the cabinet's rice statistics and legislative output. Far from swaying public opinion, the state media blitz has become the butt of jokes in coffee stalls from Tanah Abang to Glodok. 'We endured thirty-two years of Harmoko telling us the price of chillies was stable while our pockets were empty; now Habibie is playing the same cassette tape,' mocked media watchdog Veven Sp. Wardhana.",
	"event.ev_press_freedom.opt.3.headline": "WARGA BOSAN DONGENG TVRI: HARMOKO GANTI KACAMATA!",
	"event.ev_press_freedom.opt.3.text": "\"Silence has never won an argument in the newspapers. Direct TVRI, RRI, and Antara to launch an aggressive counter-information campaign putting this government's economic and legislative achievements in front of the public every evening.\"",
	"event.ev_press_freedom.opt.4.body": "The reformist mask slipped off Merdeka Palace yesterday afternoon as plainclothes intelligence officers and National Police investigators paid unannounced 'courtesy visits' to three major Jakarta newsrooms, waving colonial-era [i]Haatzai Artikelen[/i] (hate-sowing statutes) and Criminal Code provisions on insulting the head of state. Within hours, hundreds of journalists and UI students blockaded the Ministry of Information on Jalan Medan Merdeka Barat with black ribbons taped over their mouths, chanting a slogan that is now echoing across foreign wire services: 'Habibie is just Suharto with a German doctorate!'",
	"event.ev_press_freedom.opt.4.headline": "ORBA BANGKIT LAGI! INTEL DATANGI REDAKSI, PASAL HINA PRESIDEN DIPAKAI GEBUK PERS",
	"event.ev_press_freedom.opt.4.text": "\"Instruct BAIS and the police to quietly visit the editors printing classified defense telegrams and remind them that Criminal Code provisions on state secrets and defamation of the head of state remain on the books.\"",
	"event.ev_press_freedom.title": "Press Freedom & Law No. 40",
	"event.ev_pwc_audit.date": "September 28, 1999",
	"event.ev_pwc_audit.desc": "Three days before the new MPR is sworn in, the complete 120-page PricewaterhouseCoopers (PwC) long-form forensic audit of the Bank Bali scandal has leaked in full to DPR Commission VIII and the Jakarta press corps. Although Supreme Audit Agency (BPK) Chairman Billy Joedono initially distributed only a sanitized 41-page summary omitting individual names on bank-secrecy grounds, the leaked unredacted PwC report names everyone: it documents indicators of fraud, collusion, and political interference tracing the Rp 546 billion from Bank Bali through Djoko Tjandra and Setya Novanto's PT Era Giat Prima straight to accounts linked to DPA Chairman A.A. Baramuli, State Enterprises Minister Tanri Abeng, IBRA officials, BI Governor Sjahril Sabirin, and your own 'Tim Sukses' re-election operation. DPR Pansus members are holding up copies of the leaked pages for television cameras in Senayan.",
	"event.ev_pwc_audit.opt.0.body": "Only after photocopies of the unredacted 120-page PricewaterhouseCoopers forensic audit were already circulating in every newsroom and embassy in Jakarta did Merdeka Palace finally bow to reality and 'declassify' the report. And what a devastating document it is: page after page traces the Rp 546 billion Bank Bali payout through Setya Novanto and Djoko Tjandra's PT Era Giat Prima straight into the inner sanctum of Habibie's own re-election machine ([i]Tim Sukses[/i]). Inside Golkar, a furious A.A. Baramuli is threatening to drag down everyone with him if prosecuted, while Akbar Tandjung's camp is openly preparing to abandon a presidency drowning in sleaze.",
	"event.ev_pwc_audit.opt.0.headline": "AUDIT PWC BUKA BOROK TIM SUKSES: HABIBIE LEMPAR BARAMULI KE KANDANG SINGA DPR",
	"event.ev_pwc_audit.opt.0.text": "\"Declassify and transmit the full unredacted 120-page PwC audit to the DPR Pansus committee, and instruct the Attorney General and National Police to question every official named in it, including A.A. Baramuli and Setya Novanto.\"",
	"event.ev_pwc_audit.opt.1.body": "Supreme Audit Agency (BPK) Chairman Billy Joedono and Bina Graha turned themselves into a national laughingstock yesterday by solemnly handing DPR members a sanitized 41-page 'summary' of the PwC Bank Bali report with all the politicians' names scrubbed out, at the exact moment street boys at the Kuningan and Slipi traffic lights were hawking bootleg copies of the full 120-page unredacted audit for Rp 10,000 apiece! 'The Palace is trying to hide an elephant behind a handkerchief,' DPR Pansus member Angelina Sondakh's colleagues jeered on the floor.",
	"event.ev_pwc_audit.opt.1.headline": "SENSOR SPIDOL HITAM BPK JADI BAHAN TERTAWAAN! FOTOKOPI AUDIT PWC DIJUAL DI LAMPU MERAH",
	"event.ev_pwc_audit.opt.1.text": "\"Stand behind BPK Chairman Billy Joedono's statutory interpretation: release the 41-page official summary publicly while keeping the raw annexes restricted to law enforcement investigators under Indonesia's banking secrecy statute.\"",
	"event.ev_pwc_audit.opt.2.body": "President Habibie's attempt to pin the blame for the Bank Bali scandal on Bank Indonesia Governor Sjahril Sabirin and IBRA Chairman Glenn Yusuf backfired spectacularly in DPR hearings yesterday afternoon. Protected by the central bank independence statute Habibie himself signed in May, Sabirin flatly refused to resign and instead testified under oath that he only authorized the Rp 904 billion transfer after relentless political pressure and threats from Habibie's closest confidant, DPA Chairman A.A. Baramuli.",
	"event.ev_pwc_audit.opt.2.headline": "DITUDING ISTANA, GUBERNUR BI SJAHRIL SABIRIN MELAWAN DAN BONGKAR TEKANAN BARAMULI",
	"event.ev_pwc_audit.opt.2.text": "\"Call on Bank Indonesia Governor Sjahril Sabirin and IBRA Chairman Glenn Yusuf to accept institutional responsibility for the regulatory failure that allowed the Rp 904 billion interbank claim to be paid out in the first place.\"",
	"event.ev_pwc_audit.opt.3.body": "The Palace's latest legal defense of the Bank Bali scandal, claiming that because the Rp 546 billion was eventually frozen in escrow, 'the state suffered zero loss and therefore no corruption occurred', was shredded by legal scholars and IMF officials alike yesterday. 'By that logic, a bank robber who drops the money bag when surrounded by police at the door commits no crime,' banking analyst Pradjoto told [i]Kompas[/i], noting that the PwC audit proves beyond doubt a premeditated conspiracy to loot state recapitalization funds for the October presidential election.",
	"event.ev_pwc_audit.opt.3.headline": "LOGIKA ABSURD TANPA KERUGIAN NEGARA: PENJARAHAN BANK BALI BUKAN SEKADAR SOAL AKUNTANSI",
	"event.ev_pwc_audit.opt.3.text": "\"Have State Enterprises Minister Tanri Abeng and your legal counsel argue that since the Rp 546 billion has now been frozen in escrow at Bank Indonesia, the state treasury has suffered zero net financial loss.\"",
	"event.ev_pwc_audit.opt.4.body": "In a breathtaking act of political self-destruction just seventy-two hours before the MPR convenes, the Habibie government has sent police investigators into Senayan to hunt down the leakers of the 120-page PwC Bank Bali audit rather than the thieves named inside it. In response, student protesters plastered enlarged pages of the audit showing the transfers to Setya Novanto and Baramuli's network across the walls of the DPR compound, while IMF Director Hubert Neiss announced from Washington that Indonesia's bailout remains frozen solid.",
	"event.ev_pwc_audit.opt.4.headline": "POLICE RAID DPR OFFICES OVER PWC LEAK AS IMF CONDEMNS COVER-UP",
	"event.ev_pwc_audit.opt.4.text": "\"Declare the leaked PwC document a violation of state and banking secrecy laws, and order the police to raid the offices of the newspapers and DPR staffers circulating the unredacted pages.\"",
	"event.ev_pwc_audit.title": "PwC Bank Bali Audit Leaks",
	"event.ev_referendum_countdown.date": "July 22, 1999",
	"event.ev_referendum_countdown.desc": "Despite the militia roadblocks, UNAMET's 400 registration centers are witnessing an extraordinary surge of East Timorese registering to vote ahead of the August 30 consultation. Back in Jakarta, the realization that East Timor might actually vote to leave the Republic has triggered a political firestorm. Recall how this began in January: after receiving Australian Prime Minister John Howard's December letter suggesting a long New Caledonia-style transition followed by a vote decades later, you scribbled a historic note on the margin of the letter to Wiranto and Alatas asking why Indonesia should continue carrying a 'thankless burden' for another ten years when the question could be settled immediately before the MPR session.\n\nNow, PDI-P nationalists and retired generals are accusing you of exceeding a transitional president's mandate by gambling away the '27th province' without parliamentary approval, while Western creditors warn that aborting the August 30 ballot will trigger an immediate financial freeze.",
	"event.ev_referendum_countdown.opt.0.body": "Even President Habibie's closest allies inside Golkar are watching in horror as he lashed his entire political survival to the mast of the August 30 East Timor ballot. At a heated closed-door caucus in Senayan yesterday, legislators from both Golkar and PDI-P questioned by what constitutional right an unelected transitional caretaker gambled away a province where 20,000 Indonesian soldiers died without first asking the MPR. 'He made this decision on an impulse after reading a letter from John Howard, and when East Timor votes to leave next month, that memo will be his political death warrant,' one senior Golkar strategist said.",
	"event.ev_referendum_countdown.opt.0.headline": "HABIBIE PERTARUHKAN NYAWA POLITIKNYA DI KOTAK SUARA TIMTIM",
	"event.ev_referendum_countdown.opt.0.text": "\"A commitment signed in New York in the name of the Republic of Indonesia is binding. We offered Wide-Ranging Autonomy in good faith, and the ballot proceeds on August 30 as scheduled; this government will not be remembered for breaking its word to the world.\"",
	"event.ev_referendum_countdown.opt.1.body": "While wounded veterans of [i]Operasi Seroja[/i] struggle to survive on meager military pensions, Fretilin rebel commander Xanana Gusmão is now receiving foreign diplomats and UN envoys in an air-conditioned state house on Jalan Percetakan Negara VII courtesy of President Habibie! Retired generals led by Try Sutrisno and nationalist MPs from PDI-P erupted in fury yesterday, accusing the Palace of rolling out the red carpet for a separatist leader who is openly preparing his victory lap before the August 30 ballot has even been cast.",
	"event.ev_referendum_countdown.opt.1.headline": "XANANA DISERVIS BAK TAMU AGUNG DI SALEMBA, JENDERAL PENSIUNAN NGAMUK!",
	"event.ev_referendum_countdown.opt.1.text": "\"Release CNRT leader Xanana Gusmão from Cipinang Prison to a special house-arrest residence in Salemba so he can meet directly with UNAMET, Bishop Belo, and pro-integration leaders to calm tensions ahead of August 30.\"",
	"event.ev_referendum_countdown.opt.2.body": "President Habibie's blunt declaration that Indonesia will simply 'part ways as friends' with East Timor if autonomy is rejected on August 30 has stunned constitutional scholars and infuriated nationalists across the spectrum. Editorialists noted that the President spoke of severing a province with the breezy detachment of an aerospace executive closing down an unprofitable subsidiary. 'A head of state is sworn to defend the territorial integrity of the Republic, not to shrug and hold the door open based on a margin note he scribbled in January,' PDI-P theorist Kwik Kian Gie charged yesterday.",
	"event.ev_referendum_countdown.opt.2.headline": "KETIKA PRESIDEN BICARA PELEPASAN WILAYAH BAGAI MEMUTUS KONTRAK DAGANG",
	"event.ev_referendum_countdown.opt.2.text": "\"Make the stakes crystal clear to both Jakarta and Dili, if the East Timorese people reject our offer of Wide-Ranging Autonomy, I will ask the MPR in October to revoke the 1978 integration decree so Indonesia and East Timor can part ways cleanly as neighbors.\"",
	"event.ev_referendum_countdown.opt.3.body": "In a speech that sounded more like a bankruptcy receiver's report than a presidential address, B.J. Habibie lectured the nation yesterday on how East Timor is nothing but 'rocks and pebbles' draining budget subsidies that Jakarta can no longer afford. While IMF economists quietly nodded along, the remarks provoked outrage from both ends of the political spectrum: human rights groups noted that the speech ignored twenty-four years of state violence against the Timorese, while ABRI veterans' associations fumed that the man who poured billions of dollars into failed IPTN airplanes now lectures soldiers about fiscal prudence.",
	"event.ev_referendum_countdown.opt.3.headline": "LOGIKA KALKULATOR HABIBIE: TIMTIM DIANGGAP BEBAN, DARAH PRAJURIT DILUPAKAN",
	"event.ev_referendum_countdown.opt.3.text": "\"Explain the fiscal reality to the Indonesian public that East Timor absorbs billions of rupiah in subsidies every year while costing us crippling diplomatic isolation and IMF friction at a moment when millions of Indonesians need food and jobs.\"",
	"event.ev_referendum_countdown.opt.4.body": "Six months after rejecting Australian Prime Minister John Howard's proposal for a ten-year autonomy transition and insisting on an immediate 1999 referendum, President Habibie has panicked at the eleventh hour and tried to reverse course. The humiliating result is the worst of both worlds: Washington, the UN, and the IMF immediately rejected any retreat from the August 30 ballot, while domestic critics in Senayan pointed out that Habibie's amateurish flip-flopping has exposed Indonesia to global ridicule without saving East Timor.",
	"event.ev_referendum_countdown.opt.4.headline": "ZIGZAG PRESIDENCY: HABIBIE TRIES TO RETREAT FROM HIS OWN TIMOR GAMBLE",
	"event.ev_referendum_countdown.opt.4.text": "\"Pivot back toward John Howard's original December formula. Instruct Ali Alatas to propose suspending the August 30 winner-take-all ballot in favor of a five-to-ten-year interim autonomy period before any final vote is held.\"",
	"event.ev_referendum_countdown.title": "Referendum Countdown",
	"event.ev_rupiah_plummets.date": "August 24, 1999",
	"event.ev_rupiah_plummets.desc": "The convergence of the Bank Bali scandal, the IMF aid freeze, and daily reports of militia gunfire in East Timor has snapped the five-month financial rally you had counted on as the centerpiece of your October Accountability Speech. Having strengthened from Rp 16,800 per US dollar in June 1998 to a post-election peak of Rp 6,600 in late June, the rupiah is now tumbling again on Singapore and Jakarta trading floors, sliding past Rp 8,000 toward Rp 8,500 per dollar in days. Under the newly enacted Bank Indonesia Act (UU No. 23/1999), Governor Sjahril Sabirin holds statutory independence over monetary policy, but with imported rice, wheat, and medicine prices threatening to surge right as the MPR prepares to convene, your economic team at Bina Graha is clashing over how to halt the slide.",
	"event.ev_rupiah_plummets.opt.0.body": "Bank Indonesia's aggressive dollar sales in the spot market yesterday succeeded in dragging the rupiah back below Rp 7,900, but market economists are warning of the steep hidden cost. 'The government is burning through scarce foreign exchange reserves not to fix the underlying political rot of Bank Bali or East Timor, but simply to dress up the exchange rate window for Habibie's October 14 speech before the MPR,' economist Faisal Basri warned, noting that hiking SBI interest rates again will choke off credit to the real sector just as factories were beginning to rehire.",
	"event.ev_rupiah_plummets.opt.0.headline": "BANK INDONESIA BAKAR CADANGAN DEVISA DEMI KOSMETIK PIDATO PERTANGGUNGJAWABAN",
	"event.ev_rupiah_plummets.opt.0.text": "\"Coordinate closely with Bank Indonesia Governor Sjahril Sabirin to deploy targeted foreign exchange sterilization and temporary SBI interest rate hikes, defending the Rp 7,500–8,000 band so inflation remains near zero heading into October.\"",
	"event.ev_rupiah_plummets.opt.1.body": "To stop the rupiah's slide without opening up the Bank Bali books, the Habibie cabinet has signed yet another humiliating commitment with the IMF, this time pledging to accelerate fire-sale auctions of nationalized corporate assets held by the Indonesian Bank Restructuring Agency (IBRA). In Senayan, legislators across both PDI-P and Golkar accused the economic team of auctioning off billions of dollars in Indonesian industrial assets at twenty cents on the dollar to foreign vulture funds purely to buy six weeks of currency calm before the MPR session.",
	"event.ev_rupiah_plummets.opt.1.headline": "OBRAL ASET BPPN KE PEMODAL ASING: HARGA PANIK PEMERINTAHAN HABIBIE",
	"event.ev_rupiah_plummets.opt.1.text": "\"Sign an emergency addendum to the IMF Letter of Intent committing to accelerated IBRA asset sales and bank restructuring milestones, bringing Hubert Neiss back to the table to calm currency traders without burning central bank reserves.\"",
	"event.ev_rupiah_plummets.opt.2.body": "Central bankers and foreign textbook economists may be applauding the Palace for letting the rupiah 'find its market equilibrium' without burning dollar reserves, but at Pasar Senen and Pasar Induk Kramat Jati yesterday, housewives and small traders were in no mood for monetary theory. As the rupiah tumbled past Rp 8,500 to the dollar, wholesalers immediately marked up imported soy, sugar, flour, and prescription medicines. 'Habibie's ministers boast every week that inflation is under control, yet one rumor from Senayan sends our grocery money up in smoke,' a furious vendor told [i]Pos Kota[/i].",
	"event.ev_rupiah_plummets.opt.2.headline": "DOLAR TEMBUS RP 8.500, HARGA SEMBAKO DAN OBAT LANGSUNG MELAMBUNG DI PASAR!",
	"event.ev_rupiah_plummets.opt.2.text": "\"Respect Bank Indonesia's statutory independence under Law No. 23/1999: let the rupiah float freely rather than burning precious foreign reserves, and direct BULOG to release buffer rice stocks to shield poor households from import prices.\"",
	"event.ev_rupiah_plummets.opt.3.body": "While expanding [i]Padat Karya[/i] ditch-clearing and road-sweeping jobs in Jakarta and Surabaya provides welcome daily wages for a fraction of the urban unemployed, financial analysts dismissed the Palace's freeze on ministerial travel and official sedans as theatrical window-dressing. 'Singapore currency desks are not shorting the rupiah because ministers drink too much coffee at Bina Graha; they are shorting it because Rp 546 billion vanished at Bank Bali and Dili is on the verge of war,' INDEF economist Didik J. Rachbini observed sharply.",
	"event.ev_rupiah_plummets.opt.3.headline": "KOSMETIK PENGHEMATAN ISTANA TAK MAMPU OBATI KRISIS KEPERCAYAAN PASAR",
	"event.ev_rupiah_plummets.opt.3.text": "\"Announce an immediate austerity freeze on non-essential ministerial spending, official foreign travel, and state vehicle purchases, redirecting the savings into urban Padat Karya (labor-intensive) public works.\"",
	"event.ev_rupiah_plummets.opt.4.body": "Attempting to imitate Mahathir Mohamad's capital controls without Malaysia's administrative discipline or foreign reserve cushion has blown up in Bina Graha's face within twenty-four hours. The moment rumors of offshore rupiah swap restrictions leaked from the Ministry of Finance, domestic conglomerates and foreign portfolio managers stampeded for the exits, wiring hundreds of millions of dollars to Singapore overnight and driving interbank overnight rates through the roof.",
	"event.ev_rupiah_plummets.opt.4.headline": "JAKARTA'S CLUMSY FLIRTATION WITH CAPITAL CONTROLS SPARKS PANIC EXODUS",
	"event.ev_rupiah_plummets.opt.4.text": "\"Impose temporary Malaysia-style administrative reporting controls on short-term offshore rupiah swaps to punish Singapore currency speculators directly.\"",
	"event.ev_rupiah_plummets.title": "The Rupiah Slides Toward 8,500",
	"event.ev_semanggi_ii.date": "September 24, 1999",
	"event.ev_semanggi_ii.desc": "Yesterday afternoon, in its final days before dissolving, the outgoing DPR rushed through the State of Danger Bill (RUU Penanggulangan Keadaan Bahaya / PKB), a sweeping statute championed by Defense Minister General Wiranto to replace the 1959 emergency law, granting the President and regional military commanders broad powers to declare states of civil or military emergency, ban demonstrations, wiretap communications, and detain suspects. Seeing the bill as the reincarnation of New Order authoritarianism, tens of thousands of university students from UI, Trisakti, and Atma Jaya have occupied Jalan Gatot Subroto and the Semanggi cloverleaf outside the DPR/MPR complex. Over the past twenty-four hours, security forces have fired tear gas and live rounds into the crowds: University of Indonesia engineering student Yap Yun Hap has been shot dead near Semanggi, and violent clashes in Jakarta, Lampung, and Palembang have left eleven dead and over two hundred wounded. With the MPR convening in seven days, the capital is on the verge of exploding.",
	"event.ev_semanggi_ii.opt.0.body": "Why does it always take student corpses on the asphalt of Jalan Sudirman before the Habibie government listens to its own people? That was the bitter question asked by University of Indonesia students weeping over the casket of engineering student Yap Yun Hap at the UI Salemba campus yesterday, hours after the Palace announced it was shelving the hated State of Danger Bill (RUU PKB). While freezing the bill prevented a full-scale insurrection ahead of next week's MPR session, student senates pointed out that Habibie's own ministers drafted and pushed the draconian bill through the DPR in the first place, and inside Cilangkap, General Wiranto's staff are furious at being abandoned mid-stream.",
	"event.ev_semanggi_ii.opt.0.headline": "SETELAH NYAWA YAP YUN HAP MELAYANG, BARU ISTANA TUNDA UU PENANGGULANGAN KEADAAN BAHAYA",
	"event.ev_semanggi_ii.opt.0.text": "\"Refuse to sign the State of Danger Bill (RUU PKB) into law and announce an indefinite postponement of its ratification, depriving the bill of legal force and immediately pulling the fuse out of the student uprising before the MPR convenes.\"",
	"event.ev_semanggi_ii.opt.1.body": "Shelving the RUU PKB and ordering Military Police to arrest the field personnel who fired live ammunition at Semanggi II has cooled the barricades along Jalan Gatot Subroto, but neither the students nor the officer corps are satisfied. At UI Salemba, student leaders noted that the shooters from Trisakti (May 1998) and Semanggi I (November 1998) were similarly 'investigated' while the generals who deployed combat troops with live rounds went untouched; meanwhile, Kodam Jaya and Brimob commanders are fuming that the Palace pushed their men onto the streets to defend a government bill and then threw them to the wolves when bullets flew.",
	"event.ev_semanggi_ii.opt.1.headline": "TUMBAL DI JEMBATAN SEMANGGI: PRAJURIT BAWAHAN DIKORBANKAN, PEMBERI KOMANDO AMAN",
	"event.ev_semanggi_ii.opt.1.text": "\"Postpone the Security Bill AND order Jakarta Military Commander Maj. Gen. Djaja Suparman and National Police Chief Gen. Roesmanhadi to identify and court-martial the personnel who fired live rounds at Yap Yun Hap and the protesters.\"",
	"event.ev_semanggi_ii.opt.2.body": "With eleven protesters dead across Jakarta, Lampung, and Palembang and over two hundred students lying in hospital wards at St. Carolus and Atma Jaya with gunshot wounds and shattered skulls, Merdeka Palace's offer to form a 'joint academic review team' on the State Security Bill was greeted with derision on the streets. Student coalitions from FORKOT, FAMRED, and KB-UI boycotted the Palace invitation outright, burning copies of the RUU PKB at the Semanggi flyover and chanting that they want the law dead, not edited.",
	"event.ev_semanggi_ii.opt.2.headline": "MAHASISWA DITEMBAK PELURU TAJAM, HABIBIE MALAH AJAK BIKIN TIM KAJIAN!",
	"event.ev_semanggi_ii.opt.2.text": "\"Receive a delegation of UI rectorate leaders and student representatives at Merdeka Palace to express condolences to Yap Yun Hap's family and form a joint civilian-student review team on the emergency law.\"",
	"event.ev_semanggi_ii.opt.3.body": "President Habibie's emotional, rambling television address last night, pleading for calm while refusing to explicitly kill the State of Danger Bill that sparked the bloodshed, landed with a thud across the capital. Tens of thousands of mourners marching behind Yap Yun Hap's hearse from Salemba to Tanah Kusir jeered the President's name, pointing out that less than eleven months after Semanggi I, security forces under his command have once again gunned unarmed students down on the exact same stretch of asphalt.",
	"event.ev_semanggi_ii.opt.3.headline": "AIR MATA BUAYA DI LAYAR KACA TAK BISA HIDUPKAN KEMBALI YAP YUN HAP!",
	"event.ev_semanggi_ii.opt.3.text": "\"Deliver an unscripted televised address offering personal prayers for the victims at Semanggi and Lampung while pleading with students to return to their campuses so the MPR General Session can proceed in peace.\"",
	"event.ev_semanggi_ii.opt.4.body": "By signing the despised State of Danger Bill into law on the very day University of Indonesia student Yap Yun Hap was buried, President Habibie has severed his last thread of democratic legitimacy. Over the past twelve hours, central Jakarta has descended into open urban warfare: black smoke billows from burning police posts along Jalan Sudirman, campuses in Yogyakarta, Bandung, and Surabaya have declared a nationwide strike, and Amien Rais warned from Senayan that the President has handed his opponents the ultimate reason to reject his Accountability Speech.",
	"event.ev_semanggi_ii.opt.4.headline": "JAKARTA DARURAT PERANG: HABIBIE TEKEN UU PKB DI ATAS DARAH MAHASISWA SEMANGGI",
	"event.ev_semanggi_ii.opt.4.text": "\"Sign the State of Danger Bill (UU PKB) into law immediately and authorize Maj. Gen. Djaja Suparman to invoke its emergency provisions to clear Jalan Gatot Subroto before the MPR delegates arrive on October 1.\"",
	"event.ev_semanggi_ii.title": "Semanggi II Tragedy",
	"event.ev_suharto_probe.date": "October 11, 1999",
	"event.ev_suharto_probe.desc": "Three days before you are scheduled to step to the MPR podium to deliver your Accountability Speech, Acting Attorney General Ismudjoko, who replaced Lt. Gen. Andi Muhammad Ghalib in June after Indonesia Corruption Watch (ICW) exposed suspicious bank transfers and a leaked wiretap of your private phone call to Ghalib ('Halo Andi...') mocked the anti-corruption probe, has dropped a political grenade. Today, October 11, Ismudjoko formally issued an SP3 (Surat Perintah Penghentian Penyidikan / Order to Terminate Investigation) shutting down the state corruption investigation into former President Suharto and his seven charitable foundations (Dakab, Supersemar, Dharmais), citing 'insufficient legal evidence of state losses' and Suharto's recent hospitalization at Pertamina Central Hospital. Within hours of the announcement, thousands of furious students have marched toward Jalan Cendana and the Attorney General's Office in Blok M, chanting that your entire 17-month presidency was a calculated charade to pardon your old mentor.",
	"event.ev_suharto_probe.opt.0.body": "Terrified that Acting Attorney General Ismudjoko's October 11 termination of the Suharto corruption probe would ignite a student revolution on the eve of his Accountability Speech, President Habibie scrambled yesterday to annul the SP3 order and seize the Cendana foundations. While anti-corruption activists welcomed the reversal, nobody in Senayan missed the opportunism of the timing: for sixteen months Habibie slow-walked the probe, even getting caught on a wiretap coaching Andi Ghalib, only to discover anti-Suharto zeal seventy-two hours before the MPR votes on his job. Meanwhile, Jalan Cendana's financiers have declared total war on Habibie's candidacy.",
	"event.ev_suharto_probe.opt.0.headline": "PANIK DIKEPUNG MAHASISWA, HABIBIE BATALKAN SP3 SOEHARTO H-3 PIDATO PERTANGGUNGJAWABAN",
	"event.ev_suharto_probe.opt.0.text": "\"Override Acting Attorney General Ismudjoko immediately: annul the SP3 order, place Suharto's seven foundation accounts under full state receivership, and pledge before the MPR that the corruption probe will continue under an independent special prosecutor.\"",
	"event.ev_suharto_probe.opt.1.body": "The charade that began with the leaked [i]'Halo, Andi? Apa kabar?'[/i] wiretap in February reached its cynical climax yesterday afternoon as Acting Attorney General Ismudjoko, with President Habibie's full blessing, issued an SP3 order dropping all corruption charges against former President Suharto just three days before the MPR Accountability Speech! Molotov cocktails rained down on the gates of the Attorney General's Office in Blok M last night as thousands of students clashed with riot police, chanting that the man who once called Suharto 'Super Genius' was installed in May 1998 for one purpose only: to wash his master's sins clean.",
	"event.ev_suharto_probe.opt.1.headline": "MURID BAKTI PADA SANG GURU! HABIBIE RESMIKAN SP3 SOEHARTO, REFORMASI DIKHIANATI",
	"event.ev_suharto_probe.opt.1.text": "\"Uphold the Attorney General's SP3 order on legal and humanitarian grounds, reminding the nation that Suharto has already transferred Rp 4 trillion in foundation assets to the state under Keppres No. 133/1998 and is gravely ill.\"",
	"event.ev_suharto_probe.opt.2.body": "Justice Minister Muladi spent two hours yesterday trying to convince a skeptical press corps that terminating the Suharto corruption investigation via an SP3 on October 11 is merely a 'reversible procedural pause' while the former strongman rests at Pertamina Central Hospital. Legal Aid Foundation (YLBHI) chairman Bambang Widjojanto called the explanation 'insulting legal gymnastics designed to placate Cendana cronies inside Golkar while anesthetizing the students until next week's MPR vote is over.'",
	"event.ev_suharto_probe.opt.2.headline": "AKROBAT HUKUM MULADI: SP3 DISEBUT SEMENTARA, SOEHARTO TETAP LENGGANG KANGKUNG",
	"event.ev_suharto_probe.opt.2.text": "\"Clarify through Justice Minister Muladi that an SP3 is only a provisional suspension while Suharto is hospitalized at Pertamina Hospital, and sign an instruction keeping the travel ban on Tommy Suharto and the Cendana family strictly in force.\"",
	"event.ev_suharto_probe.opt.3.body": "President Habibie's pious claim yesterday that he 'cannot interfere with the independent legal judgment of Acting Attorney General Ismudjoko' on the Suharto SP3 was greeted with derisive laughter across Senayan. Every newspaper reader in Indonesia still remembers the verbatim transcript of Habibie's private telephone call to former Attorney General Andi Ghalib earlier this year, in which the President choreographed the three-hour questioning of Suharto down to the minute. Pretending to be a bystander now fools not a single soul.",
	"event.ev_suharto_probe.opt.3.headline": "MENDADAK HORMATI INDEPENDENSI KEJAKSAAN SETELAH REKAMAN TELEPON ANDI GHALIB",
	"event.ev_suharto_probe.opt.3.text": "\"Insist on strict judicial non-interference: state that under a rule-of-law republic the President cannot order the Attorney General to indict or drop charges against any citizen, and leave the SP3 to judicial pre-trial review.\"",
	"event.ev_suharto_probe.opt.4.body": "To deflect public outrage over the Attorney General's SP3 order dropping the Suharto probe, Bina Graha announced yesterday that soldiers have been posted around No. 8 Jalan Cendana and the family's foundation accounts frozen for MPR review. [i]Pos Kota[/i] photographers stationed on Jalan Cendana all afternoon observed a rather different reality: the guards snapped to attention and saluted every time Tutut and Bambang Trihatmodjo's tinted Mercedes convoys glided in and out of the compound.",
	"event.ev_suharto_probe.opt.4.headline": "SANDIWARA JAGA JALAN CENDANA: TENTARA SENYUM HORMAT SAAT MOBIL KELUARGA CENDANA LEWAT!",
	"event.ev_suharto_probe.opt.4.text": "\"Order security forces to place Jalan Cendana under visible 24-hour protective custody and freeze the remaining Supersemar and Dakab foundation disbursements pending an MPR special committee review.\"",
	"event.ev_suharto_probe.title": "Suharto SP3 Order",
	"event.ev_the_speech.date": "October 14, 1999",
	"event.ev_the_speech.desc": "Just after nightfall on October 14, 1999, you walk to the rostrum of the Plenary Hall of the People's Consultative Assembly as MPR Speaker Amien Rais bangs the gavel for order. Before you sit 700 delegates, and tens of millions of Indonesians watching live on television, for your [i]Pidato Pertanggungjawaban[/i], the constitutional accounting of your 512 days in office. Unlike the choreographed unanimous ovations of Suharto's six terms, you are greeted by a chorus of 'Huuuu!' jeers and floor interruptions from PDI-P and student-aligned delegates before you even read your first page.\n\nFor nearly three hours, and again in your formal reply ([i]Jawaban Presiden[/i]) after all eleven MPR factions deliver their sharp critiques over October 15–17, you must frame the overarching narrative of your presidency. Will you anchor your defense in the macroeconomic miracle of rescuing the rupiah from Rp 16,800 to the 7,000s and crushing inflation from 77% to 2%? Will you champion the democratic revolution of freeing political prisoners, unleashing a free press, enacting regional autonomy, and holding the June 1999 election? Or will you confront your two greatest vulnerabilities, East Timor and Bank Bali, head-on?\n\n[color=__STAT_PC__]Your speech tonight grants an immediate burst of Political Capital and sets the tone for the final forty-eight hours of backroom caucuses (Turns 21–22), where all Final Faction Appeals are now unlocked before the October 19 roll call.[/color]",
	"event.ev_the_speech.opt.0.body": "Standing for nearly three hours beneath the glare of the television lights as PDI-P delegates repeatedly interrupted him with cries of [i]'Huuuu!'[/i], President Habibie marshaled a barrage of macroeconomic charts and legislative statistics, reminding the 700 delegates that his 512-day administration passed 39 laws, cut inflation from 77 percent to single digits, and brought the dollar down from Rp 16,800. Yet when the eleven MPR factions rose one by one to deliver their formal [i]Pemandangan Umum[/i] replies, even Golkar's own spokesman slammed the speech for glossing over East Timor, Bank Bali, and the SP3 for Suharto, warning that statistics alone will not save him on October 19.",
	"event.ev_the_speech.opt.0.headline": "TIGA JAM DI PODIUM MPR: ANGKA STATISTIK HABIBIE DIHADANG HUJATAN TIMTIM DAN BANK BALI",
	"event.ev_the_speech.opt.0.text": "\"Lead with the undeniable record of Reformasi and macroeconomic rescue: remind the Assembly that in 512 days we brought the rupiah back from Rp 16,800, broke inflation from 77%, freed political prisoners, enacted Laws No. 22 & 25 on Regional Autonomy, liberated the press, and delivered the freest election since 1955.\"",
	"event.ev_the_speech.opt.1.body": "In a dramatic departure from three decades of presidential infallibility, B.J. Habibie bowed his head from the MPR rostrum during his [i]Jawaban Presiden[/i] reply to apologize directly to the Indonesian people for the shortcomings of his seventeen-month transition, while defending the East Timor referendum as the only way to free Indonesia from a twenty-four-year international pariah trap. The humility noticeably quieted the jeering benches of PKB and the functional groups, though nationalist hardliners in PDI-P and ABRI immediately attacked the apology as an admission of guilt that warrants rejecting his mandate.",
	"event.ev_the_speech.opt.1.headline": "PERMINTAAN MAAF DI TENGAH MALAM: KETULUSAN NEGARAWAN ATAU TAKTIK MEREDAM PALU SIDANG?",
	"event.ev_the_speech.opt.1.text": "\"Confront East Timor and Bank Bali with candor and humility: apologize to the nation for the shortcomings of your transitional cabinet, explain that East Timor was never recognized by the UN and had become a bleeding wound, and pledge full prosecution of anyone implicated in Bank Bali.\"",
	"event.ev_the_speech.opt.2.body": "Dropping all pretense of a neutral constitutional accounting, President Habibie turned his three-hour address before the MPR into a combative campaign rally aimed squarely at outer-island delegates, Golkar stalwarts, and the Islamic parties of the Central Axis. While his loyalists from Sulawesi and the PBB benches cheered every line, secular nationalists and independent commentators accused the President of polarizing the chamber along regional and religious fault lines in a desperate bid to scrape together 351 votes.",
	"event.ev_the_speech.opt.2.headline": "PIDATO PERTANGGUNGJAWABAN RASA KAMPANYE: HABIBIE GALANG SENTIMEN KEDAERAHAN DAN ISLAM",
	"event.ev_the_speech.opt.2.text": "\"Deliver a fiery appeal to the Golkar family, the outer islands, and the Islamic caucus: warn the Assembly that rejecting your speech is a backdoor coup designed to erase everything ICMI, the regions, and reformist Muslims have built since May 1998.\"",
	"event.ev_the_speech.opt.3.body": "Facing eleven factions sharpening their blades for the October 19 accountability vote, President Habibie used his address at the MPR podium to dangle the ultimate prize before every party boss in the hall: a proportional 'National Unity Rainbow Cabinet' where PDI-P, Poros Tengah, Golkar, and the military all get a slice of executive power if his speech is accepted. In the Senayan coffee lounges afterward, opposition MPs smiled cynically: 'Why take a slice of Habibie's rainbow cake when we can reject his speech tomorrow and take the whole bakery?'",
	"event.ev_the_speech.opt.3.headline": "JANJI KABINET PELANGI DARI PODIUM MPR: RAYUAN TERAKHIR SEBELUM KOTAK SUARA DIBUKA",
	"event.ev_the_speech.opt.3.text": "\"Extend a constitutional olive branch to the entire Assembly: present your 17 months as a bridge to full democracy and pledge that a 1999–2004 cabinet will be a National Unity Rainbow Cabinet shared proportionally across PDI-P, the Central Axis, Golkar, and ABRI.\"",
	"event.ev_the_speech.title": "Pidato Pertanggungjawaban",
	"event.ev_timor_militia.date": "July 15, 1999",
	"event.ev_timor_militia.desc": "Under the tripartite New York Agreement signed on May 5 by Foreign Minister Ali Alatas, Portuguese Foreign Minister Jaime Gama, and UN Secretary-General Kofi Annan, Ian Martin's United Nations Mission in East Timor (UNAMET) is scheduled to open voter registration tomorrow across all thirteen districts of East Timor. Instead of an orderly administrative process, pro-integration militias (Eurico Guterres's Aitarak in Dili, Besi Merah Putih in Liquiça, and Mahidi in Ainaro) are waging a campaign of arson and terror, having already attacked UN offices in Maliana and Viqueque.\n\nEvery credible diplomatic cable reaching your desk confirms what UN monitors are saying openly: the militias are being armed, funded, and directed by elements of Kodam IX/Udayana (Maj. Gen. Adam Damiri) and Korem 164/Wira Dharma (Col. Tono Suratman) alongside Kopassus veterans. Kofi Annan has already delayed voter registration by three days and warned Jakarta that the entire consultation is in jeopardy unless Indonesia fulfills its May 5 obligation to maintain peace.",
	"event.ev_timor_militia.opt.0.body": "President Habibie's much-hyped dispatch of General Wiranto, Foreign Minister Ali Alatas, and a dozen cabinet ministers to Dili yesterday lasted barely four hours on the tarmac and convinced not a single diplomat on the ground. While Wiranto promised UNAMET chief Ian Martin 'strict neutrality,' foreign television crews filmed Indonesian territorial troops standing idly by less than two kilometers away as armed Aitarak militiamen manned roadblocks in broad daylight. Western ambassadors in Jakarta privately described the ministerial fly-in as pathetic proof that Habibie can command air force VIP jets, but cannot command a single infantry colonel on the ground in Dili.",
	"event.ev_timor_militia.opt.0.headline": "FIFTEEN MINISTERS FLY TO DILI FOR FOUR-HOUR CHARADE",
	"event.ev_timor_militia.opt.0.text": "\"Order General Wiranto and a senior delegation of fifteen cabinet ministers, including Ali Alatas and Muladi, to fly directly to Dili this week, inspect UNAMET's security personally, and put Korem 164 on notice that the eyes of the cabinet are on them.\"",
	"event.ev_timor_militia.opt.1.body": "While Western capitals applauded President Habibie's order removing Korem 164 commander Col. Tono Suratman ahead of UNAMET voter registration, insiders at Cilangkap are laughing at the Palace's naivety. Far from facing court-martial over militia attacks in Liquiça and Maliana, Suratman is already slated for promotion to brigadier general and a prestigious desk at ABRI headquarters. Meanwhile, the ABRI faction in Senayan is seething at Habibie's public humiliation of field officers who claim they were merely executing orders to defend integration, vowing that the President will pay for his disloyalty when the MPR votes in October.",
	"event.ev_timor_militia.opt.1.headline": "DICOPOT DI DILI, NAIK PANGKAT DI JAKARTA: SANDIWARA MUTASI TIMTIM",
	"event.ev_timor_militia.opt.1.text": "\"Issue a direct presidential order relieving Col. Tono Suratman of command in Dili and warning every territorial officer in Kodam IX/Udayana that anyone caught supplying weapons to Aitarak or Besi Merah Putih will face immediate court-martial.\"",
	"event.ev_timor_militia.opt.2.body": "Nothing illustrates the impotence of civilian authority in Jakarta more vividly than the fate of President Habibie's special monitoring team in Dili this week. Sent to bypass biased military intelligence reports, the Pejambon diplomats and Komnas HAM monitors have been virtually barricaded inside the Mahkota Hotel by Eurico Guterres's Aitarak militia, while local police claim they lack the fuel to escort them to Maliana.",
	"event.ev_timor_militia.opt.2.headline": "PALACE CIVILIAN ENVOYS PINNED DOWN IN DILI HOTELS BY GUNMEN",
	"event.ev_timor_militia.opt.2.text": "\"Dispatch a permanent civilian task force from Jakarta (diplomats from Pejambon, Komnas HAM monitors, and Political Affairs Envoy Dino Patti Djalal) to embed in Dili and report militia violations directly to Merdeka Palace, bypassing military intelligence filters.\"",
	"event.ev_timor_militia.opt.3.body": "Foreign Minister Ali Alatas's plea for another delay in the East Timor consultation calendar was met with icy contempt in New York and Lisbon this week. While Kofi Annan conceded a brief technical postponement to August 30 to allow UNAMET to secure its registration posts, UN officials publicly blasted Jakarta for using militia terror of its own making as an excuse to stall the vote. Back home, neither camp is happy: ABRI generals complain that a two-week delay changes nothing, while reformists accuse Habibie of dithering over a crisis he recklessly started himself.",
	"event.ev_timor_militia.opt.3.headline": "JAKARTA'S CLUMSY FOOT-DRAGGING FOOLS NOBODY AT THE UN",
	"event.ev_timor_militia.opt.3.text": "\"Instruct Foreign Minister Ali Alatas to quietly request that Kofi Annan push voter registration and the August ballot back by several weeks, giving Bishop Belo, Xanana Gusmão, and the pro-integration leaders time to implement the June Dare II peace talks.\"",
	"event.ev_timor_militia.opt.4.body": "By parroting Cilangkap's threadbare claim that the slaughter in Liquiça and the attacks on UN offices in Maliana are merely 'spontaneous tribal clashes' provoked by biased UNAMET staff, Merdeka Palace has torched what little international credibility it had left. Foreign correspondents in Dili have already published photographs of Besi Merah Putih militiamen drawing rations and ammunition directly from district military commands. 'Listening to Habibie's spokesmen blame the UN for militia violence is like watching an arsonist sue the fire brigade for water damage,' human rights lawyer Todung Mulya Lubis said yesterday.",
	"event.ev_timor_militia.opt.4.headline": "DIPLOMASI KEPALA DI DALAM PASIR: DUNIA TAK PERCAYA DONGENG KONFLIK HORIZONTAL",
	"event.ev_timor_militia.opt.4.text": "\"Reject the bias in the foreign press. Instruct the Foreign Ministry to state plainly that the clashes in Liquiça and Maliana are horizontal communal disputes between pro-integration and pro-independence Timorese factions, and that UNAMET's own local hires are tilting the field.\"",
	"event.ev_timor_militia.title": "Militia Terror in East Timor",
	"event.ev_timor_votes.date": "August 30, 1999",
	"event.ev_timor_votes.desc": "Defying months of militia intimidation, burned villages, and armed roadblocks, an astonishing 98.6% of the 451,792 registered East Timorese voters queued before dawn today at 850 polling stations across East Timor and diaspora centers to cast their ballots in the UN-administered popular consultation. UNAMET chief Ian Martin and international parliamentary observers describe scenes of extraordinary quiet determination as voters dressed in their Sunday best waited hours to mark their choice between accepting or rejecting special autonomy within Indonesia. Yet as the ballot boxes are sealed and transported under UN police escort to the Dili museum counting center, ominous reports are already pouring in: four local UNAMET staff members have been murdered in Ermera as the polls closed, and BAIS intelligence reports indicate that Eurico Guterres's militias and Korem 164 units have pre-positioned fuel drums and trucks across Dili for 'Operasi Sapu Jagad' the moment an independence vote is confirmed.",
	"event.ev_timor_votes.opt.0.body": "Up until the polls closed at 4:00 PM yesterday, military intelligence chiefs and Foreign Ministry officials had solemnly assured President Habibie that a 'silent majority' of East Timorese would vote to retain the red-and-white flag. Now, as every field report from Dili to Baucau points toward an overwhelming landslide for independence, the President's televised pledge to respect the outcome has triggered an earthquake inside the Indonesian establishment. In officers' messes across Cilangkap and Kupang, furious commanders accuse Habibie of walking blindly into a historic national humiliation on the strength of wishful thinking.",
	"event.ev_timor_votes.opt.0.headline": "TERTIPU LAPORAN ASAL BAPAK SENANG: ISTANA TERPANA MELIHAT ANTREAN 98,6 PERSEN",
	"event.ev_timor_votes.opt.0.text": "\"Go on national television tonight to commend the peaceful 98.6% turnout and state unequivocally that whatever verdict the UN certifies from those ballot boxes, the Republic of Indonesia will honor its signature on the May 5 Agreement.\"",
	"event.ev_timor_votes.opt.1.body": "While Jakarta's envoys staged one more round of handshakes for the cameras in Dili yesterday between CNRT representatives and pro-integration figures, the reality outside the conference room doors made a mockery of the proceedings. Eurico Guterres's Aitarak gunmen openly boycotted the afternoon session, and UN police reported military trucks unloading drums of gasoline and automatic weapons in Becora and Ermera. 'Jakarta is organizing cocktail-party reconciliation committees while its own security forces prepare to burn the house down,' one Western diplomat in Dili said bitterly.",
	"event.ev_timor_votes.opt.1.headline": "PEACE CEREMONIES IN DILI AS MILITIAS STOCKPILE GASOLINE CANS",
	"event.ev_timor_votes.opt.1.text": "\"Convene an urgent reconciliation council in Dili bringing together Bishop Carlos Filipe Ximenes Belo, Xanana Gusmão's CNRT representatives, and pro-integration leaders under the Peace and Stability Commission before the count is announced.\"",
	"event.ev_timor_votes.opt.2.body": "Word that Merdeka Palace has quietly instructed Pelni passenger ships and Navy LSTs to stand by for a mass evacuation of Indonesian civil servants and teachers leaked across Dili within hours yesterday, confirming to pro-integration militias that Jakarta already knows autonomy has been crushed at the polls. Far from ensuring an orderly transition, the leaked withdrawal order has sent armed militia gangs into a frenzy of betrayal, with Aitarak commanders vowing over local radio to reduce Dili to cinders before handing it over to Fretilin.",
	"event.ev_timor_votes.opt.2.headline": "BOCORNYA PERINTAH EVAKUASI PICU KEPANIKAN DAN AMUK MILISI DI DILI",
	"event.ev_timor_votes.opt.2.text": "\"Issue quiet contingency orders to General Wiranto and National Police Chief Gen. Roesmanhadi to prepare sea and airlift transport for an orderly evacuation of civil servants, teachers, and security units if autonomy is rejected.\"",
	"event.ev_timor_votes.opt.3.body": "As the world's television networks broadcast images of 98.6 percent of East Timorese defying death threats to vote, followed immediately by the murder of four local UN staffers in Ermera as the polls closed, Merdeka Palace has pulled down the shutters and refused to utter a single word. Reporters camped outside Bina Graha until midnight saw ministers slip out through side gates without taking questions, leaving the impression of a caretaker government paralyzed by the realization that its own referendum gamble has blown up.",
	"event.ev_timor_votes.opt.3.headline": "ISTANA BUNGKAM SERIBU BAHASA SAAT EMPAT STAF LOKAL UNAMET TEWAS DI ERMERA",
	"event.ev_timor_votes.opt.3.text": "\"Keep the cabinet in continuous closed session at Merdeka Palace and decline all public comment until Kofi Annan and Ian Martin formally certify the final count.\"",
	"event.ev_timor_votes.opt.4.body": "Having failed to intimidate the East Timorese electorate into staying home through months of militia terror, Jakarta is now attempting the equally absurd tactic of claiming that UNAMET rigged a vote witnessed by hundreds of international parliamentary observers. UN Secretary-General Kofi Annan dismissed the Indonesian complaint out of hand last night, while even Jakarta's own independent election monitors (KIPP) noted that blaming UN translators for an impending four-to-one defeat makes the Habibie government look both dishonest and delusional.",
	"event.ev_timor_votes.opt.4.headline": "SORE LOSERS IN JAKARTA CRY FOUL OVER 98.6% TURNOUT",
	"event.ev_timor_votes.opt.4.text": "\"Have the Foreign Ministry file formal complaints accusing UNAMET local staff of systemic pro-independence bias during the ballot, laying the groundwork to challenge the legitimacy of the count if autonomy loses.\"",
	"event.ev_timor_votes.title": "East Timor Votes",
	"event.ev_timtim_merdeka.date": "October 19, 1999",
	"event.ev_timtim_merdeka.desc": "Twenty-one years ago, in July 1978, a New Order MPR enacted Decree No. VI (TAP MPR No. VI/MPR/1978), formally incorporating the former Portuguese colony of East Timor into the Republic of Indonesia as its 27th province, an annexation the United Nations never recognized. Today, October 19, 1999, as its final act before bringing the wooden ballot boxes onto the floor to vote by secret ballot on your Accountability Speech (TAP MPR No. III/MPR/1999), the People's Consultative Assembly takes up TAP MPR No. V/MPR/1999 on the East Timor Referendum.\n\nWith remarkably little floor resistance, the Assembly formally revokes TAP MPR No. VI/1978, constitutionally recognizing the August 30 referendum result in which 78.5% of East Timorese voters chose independence, and clearing the legal path for the United Nations Transitional Administration in East Timor (UNTAET) to assume authority over the territory. As MPR Speaker Amien Rais prepares to call the 700 delegates forward one by one to cast their secret ballots on your presidency, you issue your final word on the close of the East Timor chapter.",
	"event.ev_timtim_merdeka.opt.0.body": "In a bitter historical irony, the very same MPR factions that spent the past week savaging President Habibie for 'losing the 27th province' voted unanimously this afternoon to pass TAP MPR No. V/MPR/1999, formally revoking the 1978 integration decree and letting East Timor go without a single dissenting vote. Having used East Timor to bludgeon Habibie's reputation to pieces, the 700 delegates have now washed their own hands of the territory just in time to unlock the wooden ballot boxes and pass judgment on the man who dared to hold the referendum.",
	"event.ev_timtim_merdeka.opt.0.headline": "MPR CABUT TAP INTEGRASI TIMTIM, KINI 700 ANGGOTA DEWAN SIAP HAKIMI NASIB HABIBIE",
	"event.ev_timtim_merdeka.opt.0.text": "\"This twenty-four-year chapter closes today with constitutional dignity rather than endless war. Indonesia's obligations under the May 5 Agreement are honorably discharged, may Indonesia and an independent Timor Lorosa'e live side by side in peace.\"",
	"event.ev_timtim_merdeka.opt.1.body": "With the stroke of Amien Rais's gavel ratifying TAP MPR No. V/MPR/1999, twenty-four years of blood, international isolation, and broken promises in East Timor came to a formal constitutional end this afternoon in Senayan. Yet as diplomats in the gallery applauded President Habibie's parting words on democratic honor, the floor below was already clearing for the main event: the secret-ballot roll call on his Accountability Speech has begun, and every politician in the hall is ready to collect their pound of flesh.",
	"event.ev_timtim_merdeka.opt.1.headline": "BABAK TERAKHIR TIMOR TIMUR DITUTUP, PALU AMIEN RAIS MEMBUKA MALAM PENENTUAN",
	"event.ev_timtim_merdeka.opt.1.text": "\"I will not pretend this was the outcome I hoped for when we offered Wide-Ranging Autonomy, but a Republic that honors the free vote of the ballot box, even when the result hurts, proves to the world and to itself that Reformasi is real.\"",
	"event.ev_timtim_merdeka.title": "TAP MPR No. V/1999",
	"faction.abri.biography": "Born in Yogyakarta in 1947 and commissioned from the National Military Academy (AMN) in Magelang in 1968, General Wiranto rose steadily through the Army's territorial and strategic commands after serving four pivotal years as President Suharto's personal adjutant (1989–1993). Appointed Commander of Kodam Jaya, Commander of Kostrad, Army Chief of Staff, and finally Commander of the Armed Forces (Pangab) in February 1998, he stood at the fulcrum of state power when Jakarta burned in May 1998. Rather than seizing power at the head of a junta or ordering a bloodbath on the steps of the occupied parliament complex, Wiranto nudged Suharto into stepping aside, guaranteed the physical safety and dignity of the Cendana household, and underwrote your constitutional succession—before promptly stripping his fiery rival, Lt. Gen. Prabowo Subianto, of command over Kostrad barely twenty-four hours later.\n\nServing concurrently as Armed Forces Commander and Minister of Defense and Security (Menhankam) in your Development Reform Cabinet, Wiranto views himself as the custodian of the Republic's survival rather than your personal subordinate. Besieged by student fury over the Trisakti and Semanggi shootings, the Tim Mawar kidnappings, and international condemnation over army-backed militias in East Timor, his overriding loyalty belongs to the cohesion and honor of the [color=__FAC_ABRI__][b]TNI officer corps[/b][/color]. Polished, Javanese, and fond of crooning ballads at officer receptions while keeping his political cards close to his chest, he will hold the barracks behind your government only for as long as you respect Cilangkap's institutional red lines.",
	"faction.abri.deal.tni_business_interests.alert": "Word of the audit triggers immediate fury across the regional Kodam commands. Wiranto stonewalls the BPK auditors at every turn, delivering a blunt warning to the Palace that threatening the military's off-budget autonomy crosses a dangerous red line.",
	"faction.abri.deal.tni_business_interests.desc": "Less than a third of Indonesian defense spending comes from the official state budget; the rest flows through an opaque empire of military foundations (yayasan), Kalimantan logging concessions, and regional protection rackets. Authorizing Supreme Audit Agency (BPK) investigators to inspect those books will electrify Reformasi advocates and the IMF—but strikes directly at Cilangkap's financial lifeblood and pushes the generals' patience toward the breaking point.",
	"faction.abri.deal.tni_business_interests.text": "Order BPK auditors to open the books on ABRI's off-budget foundations and timber concessions",
	"faction.abri.deal.tni_civilian_posts_withdrawal.alert": "Thousands of seconded officers across the archipelago are forced to choose between their military stars and their civilian desks. Civil-society groups hail the dismantling of Kekaryaan as a milestone for civilian supremacy, though middle-ranking colonels grumble bitterly over the lost sinecures.",
	"faction.abri.deal.tni_civilian_posts_withdrawal.desc": "Under the New Order's [i]Dwifungsi[/i] ('Dual Function') doctrine, roughly 6,800 active-duty officers sit in lucrative civilian posts as provincial governors, district regents ([i]bupati[/i]), and ministry secretaries-general. Instruct General Wiranto to enforce a strict ultimatum starting April 1999: retire from active military commission ([i]pensiun dini[/i]) or vacate civilian office immediately. Wears down the generals' patience with Cilangkap's territorial colonels.",
	"faction.abri.deal.tni_civilian_posts_withdrawal.text": "Enforce the end of active-duty military secondments to the civilian bureaucracy (Kekaryaan)",
	"faction.abri.deal.tni_east_timor_security.alert": "The brass in Cilangkap welcomes your defense of Indonesian military honor over the twenty-seventh province. In Dili, Liquiça, and Suai, however, UNAMET observers immediately warn that army-backed Aitarak and Besi Merah Putih militias are intimidating voters with total impunity.",
	"faction.abri.deal.tni_east_timor_security.desc": "Reject United Nations and Western appeals for an armed international peacekeeping deployment ahead of the August 30 popular consultation in East Timor, leaving security under the May 5 New York Agreement entirely in the hands of General Wiranto and Maj. Gen. Adam Damiri's Kodam IX/Udayana. Places the high command deeply in your debt for defending national sovereignty, while alarming human rights advocates and foreign chancelleries.",
	"faction.abri.deal.tni_east_timor_security.text": "Entrust Kodam IX/Udayana with exclusive security authority over the East Timor ballot",
	"faction.abri.deal.tni_final_appeal.alert": "General Wiranto listens in measured silence, salutes crisply, and assures you that Fraksi TNI/Polri will cast its ballots in the highest interest of national stability when the roll is called.",
	"faction.abri.deal.tni_final_appeal.desc": "Unlike the fractious civilian parties trading envelopes in hotel suites around Senayan, [color=__FAC_ABRI__][b]Fraksi TNI/Polri's 38 delegates[/b][/color] march into the Plenary chamber under direct military orders. Sit down with General Wiranto one final time before the ballot boxes open to call in every institutional guarantee you have extended to the armed forces. Redeems every political obligation and institutional favor Cilangkap owes the Palace.",
	"faction.abri.deal.tni_final_appeal.text": "Hold a midnight consultation with General Wiranto on the eve of the MPR roll call",
	"faction.abri.deal.tni_golkar_withdrawal.alert": "Cilangkap formally declares that ABRI now stands 'at an equal distance from all political parties.' Opposition leaders and election monitors applaud the announcement, while Akbar Tandjung's provincial chairmen complain that the Banyan Tree has been left to fend for itself.",
	"faction.abri.deal.tni_golkar_withdrawal.desc": "For three decades, the armed forces formed the 'Jalur A' pillar of the [color=__FAC_ABRI__][b]ABG (ABRI–Birokrasi–Golkar)[/b][/color] triad that guaranteed [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]Golkar's[/b][/color] electoral hegemony from the capital down to the village Koramil post. Urge General Wiranto to formally sever [color=__FAC_ABRI__][b]ABRI's[/b][/color] ties to [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]DPP Slipi[/b][/color] and pledge strict military neutrality across all forty-eight contesting parties. Angers Akbar Tandjung's regional Golkar apparatus.",
	"faction.abri.deal.tni_golkar_withdrawal.text": "Press Wiranto to sever ABRI's thirty-year institutional alliance with Golkar",
	"faction.abri.deal.tni_imf_funds.alert": "Cilangkap's financial managers quietly receive their allocation of state recapitalization bonds. Regional Kodam commanders express rare warmth toward Bina Graha for rescuing the officer welfare funds, though Ministry of Finance auditors wince at the balance-sheet cost.",
	"faction.abri.deal.tni_imf_funds.desc": "The Army's sprawling network of command foundations—led by Yayasan Kartika Eka Paksi, Bank Artha Graha, and regional Kodam ventures—suffered heavy losses during the banking collapse. Quietly fold their distressed commercial arms into the government's recapitalization bond scheme alongside civilian banks. Secures a major institutional obligation from Cilangkap's generals, at a heavy cost to the state balance sheet and your reformist reputation.",
	"faction.abri.deal.tni_imf_funds.text": "Fold ABRI's commercial banks and welfare foundations into the state recapitalization umbrella",
	"faction.abri.deal.tni_intel.alert": "Working from wiretaps and informant tips, BAIS operatives quietly detain several key paymasters and seize caches of envelopes and incendiary materials in Jakarta's outskirts, disrupting Cendana's latest attempt to set the capital alight.",
	"faction.abri.deal.tni_intel.desc": "Shadowy networks of paid agitators ([i]preman bayaran[/i]) and Jalan Cendana fixers have been busing in provocateurs to turn peaceful rallies and neighborhood disputes into arson attacks. Order the Strategic Intelligence Agency (BAIS) to intercept their couriers and raid their safe houses before the next riot can be staged. Blunts Cendana's street-level sabotage and steadies public order.",
	"faction.abri.deal.tni_intel.text": "Direct BAIS military intelligence to roll up Cendana-financed provocateur rings",
	"faction.abri.deal.tni_logistics.alert": "Convoys of olive-drab Reo military trucks bypass bottlenecked wholesalers and unload subsidized Bulog rice and cooking oil directly at district markets, easing food inflation and winning grateful praise from working families.",
	"faction.abri.deal.tni_logistics.desc": "With private distribution networks crippled by credit freezes, ethnic pogroms, and panic hoarding, task the Army's Kodam and Korem logistics battalions with trucking Bulog rice, cooking oil, sugar, and kerosene ([i]Sembako[/i]) directly from Tanjung Priok and Tanjung Perak into provincial markets. Relieves acute shortages and steadies working-class neighborhoods across the archipelago.",
	"faction.abri.deal.tni_logistics.text": "Mobilize ABRI's territorial command trucks for emergency Sembako distribution",
	"faction.abri.deal.tni_new_paradigm.alert": "Unveiled with full ceremonial honors on Armed Forces Day, the 'New Paradigm' wins praise from moderate civilian reformers and foreign defense attachés alike, while reassuring Cilangkap that institutional reform will remain securely in military hands.",
	"faction.abri.deal.tni_new_paradigm.desc": "Publicly champion the intellectual architects of military reform at [color=__FAC_ABRI__][b]Mabes TNI[/b][/color]—Lt. Gen. Susilo Bambang Yudhoyono, Lt. Gen. Agus Widjojo, and General Wiranto—by endorsing their [i]Paradigma Baru[/i] ('New Paradigm') doctrine alongside ICRC rules of engagement. Allowing Cilangkap to reform itself at its own pace earns a lasting debt of gratitude from the high command without threatening the territorial structure.",
	"faction.abri.deal.tni_new_paradigm.text": "Co-sponsor Cilangkap's 'Paradigma Baru' doctrine and ICRC crowd-control protocols",
	"faction.abri.deal.tni_parliamentary_reduction.alert": "After icy negotiations in Bina Graha, the high command agrees in principle to a timetable phasing out reserved legislative seats. Wiranto privately warns you that the officer corps feels increasingly cornered and humiliated by civilian politicians.",
	"faction.abri.deal.tni_parliamentary_reduction.desc": "Although [color=__FAC_ABRI__][b]Fraksi ABRI's[/b][/color] legislative bloc was already halved from 75 to 38 seats under the January election laws, student coalitions and [color=__CLR_MUTED__][b]Utusan Golongan[/b][/color] reformers are demanding an explicit timetable to abolish unelected military representation in parliament altogether. Press Wiranto to accept a binding phase-out schedule. Severely wears down General Wiranto's patience.",
	"faction.abri.deal.tni_parliamentary_reduction.text": "Press Cilangkap to commit to a complete phase-out of ABRI's unelected MPR seats",
	"faction.abri.deal.tni_riot_control.alert": "Panser armored carriers and razor-wire barricades take up positions along Jalan Sudirman, Medan Merdeka, and the Semanggi cloverleaf, dispersing unruly crowds before nightfall. Commuters and shopkeepers breathe a sigh of relief at the return of order, even as campus senates condemn the deployment.",
	"faction.abri.deal.tni_riot_control.desc": "When street demonstrations and sectarian flashpoints threaten to paralyze Jakarta, authorize General Wiranto and Kodam Jaya to position Kostrad mechanized infantry and Brimob riot police around key ministries, Glodok commercial hubs, and the Senayan parliamentary complex. Restores calm to the streets of the capital, though student activists will denounce the show of force as a return to New Order repression.",
	"faction.abri.deal.tni_riot_control.text": "Deploy Kostrad and Brimob battalions to secure the capital's thoroughfares",
	"faction.abri.mood.0": "Supporting Habibie",
	"faction.abri.mood.1": "Accommodating",
	"faction.abri.mood.2": "Guarded",
	"faction.abri.mood.3": "Alienated",
	"faction.abri.name": "Fraksi TNI/POLRI",
	"faction.abri.portrait_name": "Fraksi TNI/POLRI",
	"faction.abri.short": "Wiranto",
	"faction.abri.summary": "Under the command of General Wiranto, [color=__FAC_ABRI__][b]Fraksi ABRI (TNI/Polri)[/b][/color] controls 38 unelected seats in the MPR—cut in half from the 75 seats the military held prior to the January 1999 political laws, yet still voting with iron barrack discipline whenever Mabes Cilangkap issues an order. In April 1999, Inpres No. 2 Tahun 1999 formally separated the National Police (Polri) from the armed forces chain of command, and the high command unveiled its [i]Paradigma Baru[/i] ('New Paradigm'): a calculated institutional retreat from front-line [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]Golkar[/b][/color] party politics designed to preserve the Army's Kodam territorial network, protect its off-budget foundations, and shield senior generals from human rights tribunals.\n\nFor now, General Wiranto's accommodation with Bina Graha is the pragmatic shield keeping your government standing amidst the daily tempests of [i]Reformasi[/i]. So long as General Wiranto's patience with Cilangkap lasts, the officer corps will not openly desert the Palace: Kostrad and Brimob battalions will clear riot-torn boulevards in an afternoon, territorial trucks will move Bulog rice when civilian ports jam, and BAIS intelligence operatives will quietly roll up Cendana-financed provocateurs before they strike.\n\nThat protection is a conditional loan, not a blank check. Push too aggressively against the generals' legal immunity, their sprawling commercial empire, or their counter-insurgency campaigns in East Timor and Aceh, and the generals' patience will run out and turn to anger—and an angry Cilangkap is slow to forgive, drags down every deal you strike with the other factions, and leaves all 38 military and police delegates free to abandon you on the Assembly floor.",
	"faction.already_engaged": "You have already engaged with a faction this turn.",
	"faction.bio_alt": "$NAME$ Biography",
	"faction.btn_info": "Faction Dossier",
	"faction.burned_note": "[i]Relations with this bloc have been permanently severed.[/i]",
	"faction.cooldown": "ON COOLDOWN: $TURNS$ TURN(S)",
	"faction.default_alert": "Negotiation completed.",
	"faction.dulled": " (diminished)",
	"faction.favor_many": "$COUNT$",
	"faction.favor_none": "None",
	"faction.favor_one": "1",
	"faction.favor_redeemed": "Past political commitments were redeemed during negotiations.",
	"faction.golkar_akbar.biography": "Born in Sibolga, North Sumatra, Djandji Akbar Zahiruddin Tandjung honed his political instincts chairing the Islamic Students' Association (HMI) from 1972 to 1974, where he forged the lifelong 'Green' alumni network that now staffs the upper tiers of the Indonesian state. After co-founding the state youth umbrella KNPI and entering the DPR through [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]Golkar[/b][/color] in 1977, he earned Suharto's trust through disciplined coalition-building, serving as Minister of Youth and Sports (1988–1993) and Minister of Public Housing (1993–1998). When Suharto fell in May 1998, you appointed Akbar Minister/State Secretary. Two months later, at [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]Golkar's[/b][/color] turbulent July 1998 Extraordinary National Congress ([i]Munaslub[/i]) at Hotel Indonesia, your allies and General Wiranto's regional commanders backed Akbar to defeat retired General Edi Sudradjat by seventeen provincial delegations to ten.\n\nFrom [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]DPP Slipi[/b][/color], Akbar abolished the Advisory Board ([i]Dewan Pembina[/i]) that once gave Jalan Cendana veto power over the party and unveiled his [i]Paradigma Baru[/i] ('New Paradigm'). While Sudradjat's defeated secular-military wing walked out to form the Justice and Unity Party ([i]PKP[/i]), Akbar held the Banyan Tree's provincial bastions together through the June 1999 campaign, enduring rocks and jeers on Java's hustings to secure second place. Behind his soft voice and unhurried smile sits the sharpest tactician in Senayan. He nurses no ideological attachment to you or your reform agenda; his sole aim is keeping [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]Golkar[/b][/color] at the center of power. Whether as the core of your second term or as the kingmaker that crowns your replacement.",
	"faction.golkar_akbar.deal.golkar_bumn.alert": "You sign the commissioner decrees without fanfare, and Golkar's regional barons welcome the appointments as proof that the old spoils system endures. Market analysts and IMF monitors, watching party operatives take seats atop fragile state corporations, downgrade their outlook on Jakarta.",
	"faction.golkar_akbar.deal.golkar_bumn.desc": "The supervisory boards of Indonesia's flagship State-Owned Enterprises (BUMN)—from Pertamina and Telkom to state banks on BLBI liquidity support—hold lucrative commissioner seats overseen by Minister Tanri Abeng. Sign decrees filling those vacancies with the slate of regional bosses Akbar Tandjung's provincial chapters have pressed on the State Secretariat for months. Undermines state enterprise reform and Reformasi credibility, while placing DPP Slipi in your debt.",
	"faction.golkar_akbar.deal.golkar_bumn.text": "Appoint Golkar's provincial powerbrokers to state-owned enterprise (BUMN) commissioner boards",
	"faction.golkar_akbar.deal.golkar_congress.alert": "Word from the Palace cements Akbar's grip over the central board and quashes talk of a pre-session leadership coup. In Makassar and across the ICMI network, however, your loyalists fume that you fortified the one party leader most prepared to sell you out.",
	"faction.golkar_akbar.deal.golkar_congress.desc": "[color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]Golkar's[/b][/color] internal hierarchy remains fractured between Akbar Tandjung's HMI-rooted apparatus at [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]Slipi[/b][/color] and your own Sulawesi and ICMI partisans in A.A. Baramuli's [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_H__][b][i]Irama Suka Nusantara[/i][/b][/color] caucus, who want to unseat Akbar before the General Session. Instruct Bina Graha to affirm Akbar's authority over the central party board, curbing your loyalists' insurgency to buy peace with the [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]Slipi[/b][/color] machine. Antagonizes Baramuli's Loyalist Golkar bloc.",
	"faction.golkar_akbar.deal.golkar_congress.text": "Back Akbar Tandjung's authority over the central board against your own outer-island loyalists",
	"faction.golkar_akbar.deal.golkar_final_appeal.alert": "Akbar Tandjung promised to whip the Slipi delegates until dawn while betraying nothing of his late-night conversations with Amien Rais and Gus Dur at the Hotel Mulia.",
	"faction.golkar_akbar.deal.golkar_final_appeal.desc": "Every BUMN board seat, every impounded audit dossier, and every regional concession you have granted [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]DPP Slipi[/b][/color] over the past four months comes down to tonight's secret ballot in Senayan. Summon Akbar Tandjung to Bina Graha and demand he enforce iron discipline across his eighty delegates when the assembly clerk calls the roll. Calls in every political debt and backroom obligation DPP Slipi owes the Palace.",
	"faction.golkar_akbar.deal.golkar_final_appeal.text": "Summon Akbar Tandjung before the roll call and demand DPP Slipi hold the line",
	"faction.golkar_akbar.deal.golkar_own_nomination.alert": "After a tense all-night session at Slipi, the Rapimnas ratifies a binding resolution affirming you as Golkar's sole presidential nominee. Baramuli's loyalists hail the vote as an ironclad mandate, though Akbar's floor managers keep their backchannels to Amien Rais and Gus Dur open.",
	"faction.golkar_akbar.deal.golkar_own_nomination.desc": "Wait-and-see chapters inside Akbar Tandjung's camp have floated nominating Akbar himself—or General Wiranto—should your standing falter in October, challenging the May 1999 resolution. Demand that [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]Golkar's[/b][/color] National Leadership Meeting ([i]Rapimnas[/i]) bind all 120 [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]Fraksi Karya Pembangunan[/b][/color] delegates to your candidacy under threat of party recall, tying the Banyan Tree's survival to your own before rival brokers split the caucus. Locks in a formal political commitment from DPP Slipi.",
	"faction.golkar_akbar.deal.golkar_own_nomination.text": "Compel Golkar's Rapimnas to bind all 120 F-KP delegates to your sole candidacy",
	"faction.golkar_akbar.deal.golkar_patronage.alert": "Akbar Tandjung receives the guarantee with satisfaction, and Golkar's provincial chairmen fall back into line across the archipelago. When details of the allocation leak to the Jakarta press, student leaders and opposition lawmakers denounce the arrangement as proof that KKN has just changed its letterhead.",
	"faction.golkar_akbar.deal.golkar_patronage.desc": "For three decades, chairing a [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]Golkar[/b][/color] provincial chapter ([i]DPD Tingkat I[/i]) carried privileged access to public works contracts, forestry concessions, and regional development bank ([i]BPD[/i]) credit lines—an ecosystem local party bosses regard as the natural order of government. Dispatch couriers from Bina Graha to [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]DPP Slipi[/b][/color] with a binding guarantee that your administration will keep those regional spigots open. Tarnishes your reformist credentials and alienates the opposition, but binds Akbar Tandjung's provincial chairmen with a concrete political obligation.",
	"faction.golkar_akbar.deal.golkar_patronage.text": "Guarantee Golkar's provincial chairmen continued access to state tenders and regional credit",
	"faction.golkar_akbar.deal.golkar_pwc_shelve.alert": "The administrative embargo at the BPK buys Golkar's treasury the cover it needed, and Akbar logs the debt at DPP Slipi. Inside Senayan, PDI Perjuangan's Commission IX investigators denounce the cover-up, while IMF directors warn that suppressing the audit threatens the next bailout tranche.",
	"faction.golkar_akbar.deal.golkar_pwc_shelve.desc": "The full PwC forensic audit into PT Era Giat Prima's Rp 546 billion fee names [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]Golkar[/b][/color] treasurers and campaign financiers whom [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]DPP Slipi[/b][/color] wants kept out of televised DPR hearings. Invoke statutory secrecy protocols at the Supreme Audit Agency (BPK) to withhold the unredacted annex from parliament. Forecloses any move to surrender the full Bank Bali files to PDI Perjuangan's Pansus investigators, while securing a major political debt from Akbar Tandjung's leadership.",
	"faction.golkar_akbar.deal.golkar_pwc_shelve.text": "Impound the unredacted PricewaterhouseCoopers Bank Bali annex before it reaches Senayan",
	"faction.golkar_akbar.deal.golkar_threaten.alert": "The message lands at DPP Slipi as intended. Akbar's lieutenants mute their public sniping before the morning papers go to press, and the Cendana-linked operators exposed by the Bank Bali paper trail back away from opposition whip counts.",
	"faction.golkar_akbar.deal.golkar_threaten.desc": "The forensic audit by PricewaterhouseCoopers (PwC) into the Bank Bali cessie transfer—alongside Attorney General's Office files implicating [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]Golkar[/b][/color] deputy treasurer Setya Novanto and off-budget campaign accounts—remains under Palace seal. Let Akbar Tandjung and Marzuki Darusman understand, without crude threats, that executive discretion over which dossiers stay locked in the vault depends on the discipline of their eighty delegates.",
	"faction.golkar_akbar.deal.golkar_threaten.text": "Remind DPP Slipi of the unredacted financial dossiers sitting on the Attorney General's desk",
	"faction.golkar_akbar.mood.0": "Standing Behind Habibie",
	"faction.golkar_akbar.mood.1": "Backing Habibie, For Now",
	"faction.golkar_akbar.mood.2": "Weighing Habibie's Odds",
	"faction.golkar_akbar.mood.3": "Hedging Bets at Slipi",
	"faction.golkar_akbar.mood.4": "Looking Past Habibie",
	"faction.golkar_akbar.mood.5": "Preparing to Defect",
	"faction.golkar_akbar.mood.6": "Cutting Habibie Loose",
	"faction.golkar_akbar.name": "Fraksi Karya Pembangunan (DPP Slipi)",
	"faction.golkar_akbar.portrait_name": "Fraksi Karya Pembangunan\n(DPP Slipi)",
	"faction.golkar_akbar.short": "Tanjung",
	"faction.golkar_akbar.summary": "From the party's central headquarters at [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]DPP Slipi[/b][/color], Akbar Tandjung commands the organizational spine of [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]Golongan Karya (Golkar)[/b][/color]: the provincial governors, regency bosses, KORPRI mandarins, and rural patronage networks forged under the New Order. For three decades, the Banyan Tree operated as the civilian pillar of Suharto's three-stream [i]Jalur A-B-G[/i] edifice—binding the armed forces ([color=__FAC_ABRI__][b]ABRI[/b][/color]), the civil service bureaucracy, and functional groups into an electoral juggernaut that enforced civil-service [i]monoloyalitas[/i] from Jakarta ministries down to the village hall. Capturing 22.44% of the popular vote—23.7 million ballots and 120 parliamentary seats—in June 1999 gave Akbar proof that his cautious rebranding rescued the party from the dissolution student demonstrators demanded a year ago.\n\nUnlike your Sulawesi and ICMI partisans in the [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_H__][b][i]Irama Suka Nusantara[/i][/b][/color] caucus, [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]Akbar's Slipi apparatus[/b][/color] acknowledges no personal debt to you. Their allegiance belongs to the party machine itself: guarding its hold over state-owned enterprises (BUMN), shielding regional treasurers from KKN indictments, and claiming a share of executive power after October. In their view, you are a temporary tenant in Bina Graha whom [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]Golkar[/b][/color] backs for as long as the association yields returns. A steady rupiah, protected patronage arteries, and insulation from Jalan Cendana's fallout persuade these operators more than any sermon on democratic renewal. Should floor counts convince the provincial chairmen ([i]DPD Tingkat I[/i]) that your presidency is sinking, Akbar and parliamentary whip Marzuki Darusman will trade your mandate away behind the voting curtain without hesitation.",
	"faction.golkar_habibie.biography": "For twenty years before May 1998, you built an archipelago of laboratories, shipyards, and aircraft hangars under the umbrella of the Agency for the Assessment and Application of Technology (BPPT) and the Strategic Industries Management Agency (BPIS). In December 1990, with Suharto's blessing at a symposium in Malang, you added a political engine to that technocratic base by founding the Association of Indonesian Muslim Intellectuals (ICMI). Through its think tank CIDES and the daily [i]Republika[/i], figures like Adi Sasono, Jimly Asshiddiqie, and Wardiman Djojonegoro challenged the dominance of secular-nationalist generals and CSIS technocrats who had shaped New Order policy since 1966.\n\nWhen Suharto stepped down on May 21, 1998, your ascension marked the triumph of the ICMI intelligentsia, the BPPT engineering corps, and eastern Indonesian powerbrokers led by Supreme Advisory Council chair A.A. Baramuli and Gorontalo entrepreneur Fadel Muhammad. Yet their grip on state power remains precarious. Resented by Cilangkap's officer corps, distrusted by Megawati's secular nationalists, and outmaneuvered inside [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]Golkar's[/b][/color] central board by Akbar Tandjung's HMI network, your inner circle knows that if your accountability speech fails in Senayan, their decade-long march through Indonesia's institutions ends that same night.",
	"faction.golkar_habibie.deal.loyalist_bppt.alert": "The disbursement keeps the laboratories open and spares hundreds of aerospace and maritime engineers from pink slips. Inside BPPT and BPIS, your veteran directors greet the lifeline with palpable relief, even as IMF mission chiefs in Jakarta flag the off-budget transfer as a breach of the Letter of Intent.",
	"faction.golkar_habibie.deal.loyalist_bppt.desc": "Ever since IMF Managing Director Michel Camdessus stood over Suharto in January 1998, Fund auditors have targeted the strategic industries you spent two decades building—IPTN in Bandung, PT PAL in Surabaya, and PT Pindad—as wasteful prestige projects. Instruct the Finance Ministry to route emergency bridge funds through research endowments to keep your BPPT and BPIS engineering teams on the payroll. Binds your technocratic inner circle with a lasting debt of gratitude, though IMF monitors and foreign creditors will penalize the fiscal sleight of hand.",
	"faction.golkar_habibie.deal.loyalist_bppt.text": "Carve out off-budget bridge financing to shield BPIS and BPPT laboratories from IMF austerity",
	"faction.golkar_habibie.deal.loyalist_final_stand.alert": "After a quiet prayer led by your ICMI scholars in the Patra Kuningan living room, Baramuli and Marwah Daud embrace you at the door. Whatever happens behind the voting curtains at Senayan tomorrow, these forty delegates will fight for every ballot until the final gavel falls.",
	"faction.golkar_habibie.deal.loyalist_final_stand.desc": "Tomorrow the MPR decides whether your presidency lives or dies. Summon A.A. Baramuli, Marwah Daud Ibrahim, Fadel Muhammad, Adi Sasono, and the IPTN pioneers back to Patra Kuningan one final time—not to haggle over portfolios, but to stand shoulder to shoulder before entering the cauldron at Senayan. Calls in every personal bond and past commitment you have forged with your loyalist core.",
	"faction.golkar_habibie.deal.loyalist_final_stand.text": "Summon the Irama Suka Nusantara and ICMI inner circle to Patra Kuningan on the eve of the vote",
	"faction.golkar_habibie.deal.loyalist_icmi.alert": "Word of the evening colloquium travels through campus mosques, ministry corridors, and the newsroom at Republika. Because several ICMI scholars in attendance also advise Amien Rais and Hamzah Haz, the goodwill generated in the room ripples beyond your own caucus into the modernist Islamic parties.",
	"faction.golkar_habibie.deal.loyalist_icmi.desc": "The intellectual network you assembled at Malang in 1990 through the Association of Indonesian Muslim Intellectuals (ICMI) now spans cabinet ministries, university rectorates, and the editorial board of [i]Republika[/i]—though several of its brightest minds have drifted toward [color=__FAC_AXIS__][b]Amien Rais's PAN[/b][/color] and [color=__FAC_PPP__][b]PPP[/b][/color]. Gather ICMI's senior council and CIDES researchers for a closed-door colloquium to reaffirm that Bina Graha remains the home of modernist Muslim governance.",
	"faction.golkar_habibie.deal.loyalist_icmi.text": "Convene ICMI scholars and CIDES fellows for an evening colloquium on modernist Muslim statecraft",
	"faction.golkar_habibie.deal.loyalist_n250.alert": "Cheers echo across the hangars at Husein Sastranegara Airport in Bandung when news of the presidential authorization arrives. For the engineers who built the Gatotkaca from scratch, your signature salvages their life's work—even as Finance Ministry auditors and IMF inspectors warn that Indonesia cannot afford prestige aviation amidst a sovereign debt crisis.",
	"faction.golkar_habibie.deal.loyalist_n250.desc": "To the engineers who followed you home from Aachen and Hamburg, August 10, 1995—the day the fly-by-wire N-250 Gatotkaca lifted off the tarmac in Bandung—remains the proudest hour of the Republic's industrial history. Defy the IMF's structural adjustment ban on aerospace subsidies and sign a presidential authorization releasing state funds to keep the N-250 flight-test program alive. Earns an enduring personal debt from the IPTN and BPPT old guard, at the cost of straining the state budget and provoking Washington and the IMF.",
	"faction.golkar_habibie.deal.loyalist_n250.text": "Authorize prototype continuation funding for IPTN's N-250 Gatotkaca turboprop in Bandung",
	"faction.golkar_habibie.deal.loyalist_rally.alert": "Sitting around the dining table at Patra Kuningan until three in the morning, your oldest comrades rediscover the conviction that carried them from the hangars of Bandung to Istana Merdeka. Doubts that had begun to fester in the corridors of Senayan evaporate by dawn.",
	"faction.golkar_habibie.deal.loyalist_rally.desc": "Your private residence at Patra Kuningan has served as the nerve center for this circle since the early years at IPTN and the tense nights of May 1998 when Suharto cut you loose. Summon A.A. Baramuli, Adi Sasono, Marwah Daud Ibrahim, and your senior BPPT deputies to the house after midnight—no press, no State Secretariat stenographers, just strong Makassar coffee and a candid reckoning of what hangs in the balance.",
	"faction.golkar_habibie.deal.loyalist_rally.text": "Host an off-the-record midnight strategy session at the Patra Kuningan residence",
	"faction.golkar_habibie.deal.loyalist_technocrat_defense.alert": "Several economic ministers who had drafted resignation letters return them to their desk drawers after watching your press conference. Foreign bondholders and Jakarta's financial press welcome the display of cabinet solidarity, and morale across your technocratic wing rebounds.",
	"faction.golkar_habibie.deal.loyalist_technocrat_defense.desc": "Your economic team—Coordinating Minister Ginandjar Kartasasmita, Finance Minister Bambang Subianto, and Bappenas chief Boediono—faces daily broadsides in the press over bank closures, subsidy cuts, and food prices. Rather than letting your technocrats absorb the street's anger alone while the Palace keeps its distance, step before the microphones at Bina Graha and claim full presidential ownership of their stabilization program.",
	"faction.golkar_habibie.deal.loyalist_technocrat_defense.text": "Defend your economic technocrats in public against populist attacks over IMF structural adjustments",
	"faction.golkar_habibie.mood.0": "Ride or Die",
	"faction.golkar_habibie.mood.1": "Faithful",
	"faction.golkar_habibie.mood.2": "Nervous",
	"faction.golkar_habibie.mood.3": "Worried",
	"faction.golkar_habibie.mood.4": "Losing Confidence",
	"faction.golkar_habibie.mood.5": "Panicking",
	"faction.golkar_habibie.mood.6": "Jumping Ship",
	"faction.golkar_habibie.name": "Fraksi Karya Pembangunan (Irama Suka Nusantara)",
	"faction.golkar_habibie.portrait_name": "Fraksi Karya Pembangunan\n(Irama Suka Nusantara)",
	"faction.golkar_habibie.short": "Loyalists",
	"faction.golkar_habibie.summary": "Spearheaded by Sulawesi kingmaker Ahmad Arnold Baramuli and fiery parliamentarian Marwah Daud Ibrahim, the [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_H__][b][i]Irama Suka Nusantara[/i][/b][/color] or the [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_H__][b][i]Iramasuka Group[/i][/b][/color] caucus—mocked in the Jakarta press as [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_H__][b][i]Irama Tersedak[/i][/b][/color] ('Choked Rhythm')—forms your palace guard inside [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]Golkar[/b][/color]. This forty-seat bloc unites outer-island barons from Sulawesi, Kalimantan, and Nusa Tenggara with modernist Muslim scholars from ICMI and state engineers who climbed the ranks beside you at BPPT and the IPTN aircraft works in Bandung. Where Akbar Tandjung's [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]DPP Slipi[/b][/color] operators calculate coalition odds, these men and women treat your presidency as a personal crusade: proof that Indonesia's eastern islands and civilian technocrats can govern the Republic without asking permission from Java's military brass or Jalan Cendana.\n\nUnlike [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]Slipi's[/b][/color] machine politicians, Baramuli's partisans have nowhere else to go. Their cabinet portfolios, their BPIS research budgets, and their protection from Bank Bali subpoenas hang on keeping you in Istana Merdeka past October. Sustaining reformist momentum, reviving economic confidence, and maintaining Indonesia's standing abroad keep this caucus energized and sharpen your leverage over them, though forty loyalists alone cannot carry the MPR floor if the larger blocs turn against you.",
	"faction.golkar_pillars.a.desc": "The armed forces are too entrenched in the state. Territorial commands from Kodam down to Koramil shadow every level of civilian government, and the officer corps sits inside the legislatures, the cabinet and the regional governorships.",
	"faction.golkar_pillars.a.effect": "While it stands, [color=__CLR_GOLD__]Golkar[/color] resists your influence permanently. Every gain with a Golkar bloc is cut by [b][color=__CLR_DARK_RED__]$RESIST$%[/color][/b].",
	"faction.golkar_pillars.a.name": "ABRI",
	"faction.golkar_pillars.abri.desc": "The armed forces are too entrenched in the state. Territorial commands from Kodam down to Koramil shadow every level of civilian government, and the officer corps sits inside the legislatures, the cabinet and the regional governorships.",
	"faction.golkar_pillars.abri.effect": "While it stands, [color=__CLR_GOLD__]Golkar[/color] resists your influence permanently. Every gain with a Golkar bloc is cut by [b][color=__CLR_DARK_RED__]$RESIST$%[/color][/b].",
	"faction.golkar_pillars.abri.name": "ABRI",
	"faction.golkar_pillars.b.desc": "The civil service is staffed by Golkar loyalists and old guards. Every ministry and regional office is run by officials who came up through KORPRI and owe their careers to the party, and they vote as they are told.",
	"faction.golkar_pillars.b.effect": "While it stands, the bureaucracy slow-walks your orders. You earn [b][color=__CLR_DARK_RED__]$PCMALUS$%[/color][/b] less [b][color=__STAT_PC__]Political Capital[/color][/b] from every source.",
	"faction.golkar_pillars.b.name": "Bureaucracy",
	"faction.golkar_pillars.birokrasi.desc": "The civil service is staffed by Golkar loyalists and old guards. Every ministry and regional office is run by officials who came up through KORPRI and owe their careers to the party, and they vote as they are told.",
	"faction.golkar_pillars.birokrasi.effect": "While it stands, the bureaucracy slow-walks your orders. You earn [b][color=__CLR_DARK_RED__]$PCMALUS$%[/color][/b] less [b][color=__STAT_PC__]Political Capital[/color][/b] from every source.",
	"faction.golkar_pillars.birokrasi.name": "Bureaucracy",
	"faction.golkar_pillars.broken": "[b]Broken.[/b] $DECREE$ is in force.",
	"faction.golkar_pillars.effect_lifted": "[b]Its penalty no longer applies.[/b]",
	"faction.golkar_pillars.g.desc": "The Functional Groups: not a party in name, but an electoral machine that fused patronage, business money and the state. It has won every election since 1971 by pooling the loyalty of the other two pillars.",
	"faction.golkar_pillars.g.effect": "While it stands, the party machine keeps propping up the Cendana network. [b][color=__STAT_CENDANA__]Cendana Influence[/color][/b] creeps back up by [b][color=__CLR_DARK_RED__]$DRIFT$[/color][/b] at the end of every turn.",
	"faction.golkar_pillars.g.name": "Golkar",
	"faction.golkar_pillars.golkar.desc": "The Functional Groups: not a party in name, but an electoral machine that fused patronage, business money and the state. It has won every election since 1971 by pooling the loyalty of the other two pillars.",
	"faction.golkar_pillars.golkar.effect": "While it stands, the party machine keeps propping up the Cendana network. [b][color=__STAT_CENDANA__]Cendana Influence[/color][/b] creeps back up by [b][color=__CLR_DARK_RED__]$DRIFT$[/color][/b] at the end of every turn.",
	"faction.golkar_pillars.golkar.name": "Golkar",
	"faction.golkar_pillars.label": "The three pillars of Golkar: ABRI, Bureaucracy and Golkar",
	"faction.golkar_pillars.prereq": "To break this pillar, enact [b]$DECREE$[/b].",
	"faction.golkar_pillars.req": "Break the $PILLAR$ pillar: enact $DECREE$",
	"faction.golkar_pillars.unlock_note": "Until all three pillars are broken, the decrees that abolish Golkar's seats stay locked.",
	"faction.insufficient_pc": "Insufficient Political Capital.",
	"faction.interact_title": "Interact with $NAME$",
	"faction.label.delegates": "Seats Held:",
	"faction.label.favor": "Favor:",
	"faction.label.leverage": "Palace Bargaining Hand:",
	"faction.label.stance": "Current Disposition:",
	"faction.leverage_blunt": "Negotiating from weakness left our overture tepidly received.",
	"faction.leverage_boost": "Our position allowed Palace negotiators to extract far greater goodwill!",
	"faction.no_interactions": "No formal negotiations are currently available with this faction at this time.",
	"faction.not_started": "Start the game first.",
	"faction.other_parties.biography": "When the Ministry of Justice opened party registration in 1998, Indonesia's historical political streams ([i]aliran[/i])—suppressed since Suharto's forced party fusion ([i]fusi partai[/i]) of 1973—resurfaced overnight. More than a hundred movements formed; forty-eight passed verification under Team Eleven to appear on the June 7, 1999 ballot, reviving the ideological pluralism last seen in the 1955 parliamentary election.\n\nWithin the Islamic stream, [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]Yusril Ihza Mahendra's Crescent Star Party (PBB)[/b][/color] claimed the heritage of Mohammad Natsir's Masyumi to win thirteen seats, while [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]Nur Mahmudi Ismail's Justice Party (PK)[/b][/color] mobilized urban university mosque networks ([i]Lembaga Dakwah Kampus[/i]) to capture seven seats and anchor the [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]Daulatul Ummah (F-PDU)[/b][/color] caucus alongside [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]K.H. Syukron Ma'mun's PNU[/b][/color] and Adi Sasono's cooperative-backed [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]PDR[/b][/color]. Across the aisle, retired General Edi Sudradjat—defeated by Akbar Tandjung at [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]Golkar's[/b][/color] 1998 congress—led his [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]Justice and Unity Party (PKP)[/b][/color] into the [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]F-KKI[/b][/color] bloc alongside minor nationalist splinters, while sociologist [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]Manasse Malo's PDKB[/b][/color] organized Christian intellectuals. On its own, each party holds a sliver of the chamber; together, their forty-six ballots can tip the October roll call. Winning them requires tailoring the pitch: constitutional prestige for [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]PBB[/b][/color], clean-governance pledges for [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]PK[/b][/color], minority guarantees for [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]PDKB[/b][/color], and campaign stipends for the cash-strapped micro-parties.",
	"faction.other_parties.deal.others_bribe.alert": "Working out of hotel suites around Senayan, the chairmen of the smallest parliamentary splinters accept the operational stipends without hesitation and commit their delegates to the Palace column.",
	"faction.other_parties.deal.others_bribe.desc": "Campaigning across twenty-seven provinces exhausted the treasuries of the micro-parties sitting in [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]F-KKI[/b][/color] and [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]F-PDU[/b][/color]—splinters holding one or two seats apiece, from the [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]People's Sovereignty Party (PDR)[/b][/color] to [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]IPKI[/b][/color] and the rump 1996 PDI. Dispatch Bina Graha couriers to clear their post-election campaign debts in exchange for signed pledges backing your accountability speech.",
	"faction.other_parties.deal.others_bribe.text": "Disburse off-budget operational stipends to cash-strapped splinter party chairmen",
	"faction.other_parties.deal.others_committee_seats.alert": "Seated on the dais of Senayan's hearing rooms for the first time, the minor-party vice-chairmen relish their elevated stature and credit Bina Graha's floor whips for breaking the big-party monopoly.",
	"faction.other_parties.deal.others_committee_seats.desc": "Under Senayan's standing rules, the giant caucuses—[color=__FAC_PDIP__][b]PDI Perjuangan[/b][/color] and [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]Golkar[/b][/color]—expect to monopolize the gavels of the DPR's nine permanent commissions. Instruct your floor managers to break that duopoly and back nominees from [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]F-PBB[/b][/color], [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]F-PDU[/b][/color], and [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]F-KKI[/b][/color] for vice-chair posts across key budget and legal commissions. Places the minor party caucuses in the Palace's debt.",
	"faction.other_parties.deal.others_committee_seats.text": "Allocate DPR commission vice-chairmanships to the F-KKI, F-PDU, and F-PBB caucuses",
	"faction.other_parties.deal.others_final_appeal.alert": "Flattered by direct midnight calls from the President of the Republic, the chairmen of the minor blocs affirm their commitments one by one and dispatch their whips to hold their delegates in line when the ballot boxes open.",
	"faction.other_parties.deal.others_final_appeal.desc": "With the MPR split down the middle, the scattered delegates of [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]F-PBB[/b][/color], [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]F-PDU[/b][/color], [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]F-KKI[/b][/color], and [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]F-PDKB[/b][/color] hold the margin between survival and defeat. Spend the final hours before the plenary roll call on the telephone from Bina Graha, speaking chairman to chairman with Yusril Ihza Mahendra, Nur Mahmudi Ismail, Manasse Malo, and Edi Sudradjat's deputies. Redeems every political obligation and parliamentary favor the minor blocs owe the Palace.",
	"faction.other_parties.deal.others_final_appeal.text": "Work the telephones through the night to lock in the minor party chairmen before the ballot",
	"faction.other_parties.deal.others_pbb_counsel.alert": "Yusril Ihza Mahendra accepts the brief with characteristic self-assurance. Within days, his legal team refines the Palace's legislative drafts, and PBB's thirteen delegates warm toward your administration.",
	"faction.other_parties.deal.others_pbb_counsel.desc": "[color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]Crescent Star Party (PBB)[/b][/color] chairman Yusril Ihza Mahendra—a sharp University of Indonesia constitutional law professor who drafted speeches at the State Secretariat for Suharto and wrote the text of his May 1998 resignation—commands thirteen modernist Muslim delegates and harbors presidential ambitions of his own. Bring Yusril into Bina Graha's legal drafting circle to co-author your upcoming constitutional reform bills. Secures a binding political debt from PBB's leadership.",
	"faction.other_parties.deal.others_pbb_counsel.text": "Appoint Crescent Star Party (PBB) Chairman Yusril Ihza Mahendra as special constitutional counsel",
	"faction.other_parties.deal.others_pdkb_courtship.alert": "Manasse Malo and the Christian delegates of PDKB and F-KKI welcome the presidential guarantee. Reassured that Bina Graha will not trade away minority rights to appease hardline factions, their caucus softens its stance toward your government.",
	"faction.other_parties.deal.others_pdkb_courtship.desc": "Christian-pluralist parties inside this bloc—led by sociologist [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]Manasse Malo's Love the Nation Democratic Party (PDKB)[/b][/color] and Catholic and Protestant delegates within [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]F-KKI[/b][/color]—watch the sectarian bloodshed in Ambon and calls in Senayan to revive the Jakarta Charter with mounting alarm. Receive their church and parliamentary leaders at Istana Merdeka and issue a public guarantee safeguarding minority worship and Pancasila pluralism.",
	"faction.other_parties.deal.others_pdkb_courtship.text": "Pledge constitutional protection for religious minorities to Manasse Malo's PDKB and F-KKI",
	"faction.other_parties.deal.others_pk_outreach.alert": "Nur Mahmudi Ismail and the Justice Party's Shura Council welcome the overture after careful deliberation. Unlike the transactional brokers in the lobby, PK's seven lawmakers respond to clean-governance commitments rather than cash.",
	"faction.other_parties.deal.others_pk_outreach.desc": "Forged out of university mosque movement networks ([i]Usrah[/i] and [i]Tarbiyah[/i]) and chaired by Texas A&M-trained food scientist Nur Mahmudi Ismail alongside Hidayat Nur Wahid, the [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]Justice Party (Partai Keadilan)[/b][/color] enforces strict internal discipline that renders its seven delegates immune to patronage envelopes. Address their inaugural national gathering and pledge an uncompromising purge of KKN across the ministries.",
	"faction.other_parties.deal.others_pk_outreach.text": "Court Nur Mahmudi Ismail and the campus dakwah cadres of the Justice Party (PK)",
	"faction.other_parties.mood.0": "Secured",
	"faction.other_parties.mood.1": "Favorable",
	"faction.other_parties.mood.2": "Fragmented",
	"faction.other_parties.mood.3": "Weighing Offers",
	"faction.other_parties.mood.4": "Skeptical",
	"faction.other_parties.mood.5": "Defecting",
	"faction.other_parties.mood.6": "Hostile",
	"faction.other_parties.name": "F-KKI, F-PDU & Minor Blocs",
	"faction.other_parties.portrait_name": "F-KKI, F-PDU & Minor Blocs",
	"faction.other_parties.short": "Others",
	"faction.other_parties.summary": "After Law No. 2/1999 dismantled the New Order's three-party straitjacket—which since 1973 had confined electoral politics to [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]Golkar[/b][/color], [color=__FAC_PPP__][b]PPP[/b][/color], and PDI—forty-eight parties contested the June 1999 general election. Outside the five major parliamentary powers, eighteen smaller parties won representation in Senayan, pooling their forty-six mandates into composite caucuses: the modernist Islamic [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]Crescent Star Party (F-PBB)[/b][/color] and [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]Daulatul Ummah Coalition (F-PDU)[/b][/color], the nationalist [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]Indonesian National Unity Faction (F-KKI)[/b][/color], and the Christian-pluralist [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]Love the Nation Democratic Party (F-PDKB)[/b][/color].\n\nSharing no unified doctrine, this mosaic spans Neo-Masyumi constitutionalists under Yusril Ihza Mahendra, campus [i]Tarbiyah[/i] cadres in [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]Nur Mahmudi Ismail's Justice Party (PK)[/b][/color], secular Siliwangi veterans in [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]Edi Sudradjat's PKP[/b][/color], and Protestant scholars led by Manasse Malo. Because none of these splinter blocs can command the floor alone, their chairmen treat the MPR General Session as an auction for cabinet seats, commission gavels, and statutory protection. Even as Amien Rais courts the Islamic splinter parties into his [color=__FAC_AXIS__][b]Central Axis[/b][/color], dozens of unbound mandates remain in play. Maintaining public approval and preserving calm in the streets give the Palace strong leverage over these minor caucuses, whose leaders shrink from backing an embattled president if riots threaten to engulf Jakarta.",
	"faction.pdip.biography": "Diah Permata Megawati Setiawati Sukarnoputri is the eldest daughter of Indonesia's founding president, Sukarno, and spent her formative years watching the New Order systematically dismantle her father's name, confine him to house arrest at Wisma Yaso until his death in 1970, and consign his family to the political wilderness. Entering the legislature quietly in 1987 to revive the moribund Indonesian Democratic Party (PDI), she shattered the regime's carefully managed consensus in December 1993 when grassroots delegates at an extraordinary congress ([i]Munaslub[/i]) in Surabaya defied military intimidation to elect her party chairwoman. Almost overnight, she became the living vessel for every grievance Suharto's thirty-two-year rule could no longer contain.\n\nAlarmed by the prospect of a Sukarno challenging the presidency in 1998, Cendana and [color=__FAC_ABRI__][b]ABRI[/b][/color]orchestrated a rival party congress in Medan in June 1996 under Commander-in-Chief Feisal Tanjung and Socio-Political Chief Syarwan Hamid to reinstall the pliant Soerjadi. When Megawati's loyalists refused to vacate the central headquarters at Jalan Diponegoro No. 58 and held nightly free-speech forums ([i]Mimbar Bebas[/i]), trucks of state-backed thugs and security forces under Jakarta military commander Sutiyoso stormed the compound at dawn on July 27, 1996. The Kudatuli assault left at least five dead, 149 wounded, and twenty-three activists missing, sparking the worst Jakarta riots in two decades. Yet the crackdown backfired: Megawati's quiet refusal to bend turned a factional dispute into a sacred martyrdom. Rechristening her movement [color=__FAC_PDIP__][b]PDI Perjuangan[/b][/color] after May 1998 and adopting the defiant circular white-muzzled bull emblem at the October 1998 Bali Congress, she rode a tidal wave of popular devotion to first place in June 1999. Now, from her residence in Kebagusan, she waits with characteristic silence for the MPR to ratify what her millions of followers consider her birthright.",
	"faction.pdip.deal.pdip_cabinet.alert": "Kwik Kian Gie and Laksamana Sukardi weigh the proposal with cool detachment, well aware of how dangerous an open pact with Bina Graha looks to the red-shirted street. Still, the promise of real authority over economic restructuring is too substantive to dismiss out of hand. PDI Perjuangan's spokesmen noticeably dial back their daily broadsides, while Akbar Tandjung's camp in Golkar fumes at being sidelined.",
	"faction.pdip.deal.pdip_cabinet.desc": "For thirty-two years, the New Order treated PDI as decorative opposition, locking its intellectuals out of executive governance. Yet Megawati's advisory board ([i]Litbang[/i])—figures like Kwik Kian Gie and Laksamana Sukardi—are serious economists and bankers eager to dismantle the old crony monopolies. Send word through Taufik Kiemas that if your administration survives October, first-rank economic and legal ministries in a national unity cabinet will be theirs to name. Secures a lasting political obligation from Diponegoro's leadership, though Golkar's old guard and Cilangkap will view the offer as a betrayal.",
	"faction.pdip.deal.pdip_cabinet.text": "Quietly guarantee PDI Perjuangan's technocrats key economic and legal portfolios in a unity cabinet",
	"faction.pdip.deal.pdip_final_appeal.alert": "In the quiet parlor of her Kebagusan home, surrounded by portraits of Bung Karno, Megawati hears you out in her trademark, inscrutable silence before offering a measured nod. Taufik Kiemas escorts you to your car at the gate. Every ounce of goodwill you have painstakingly built with the Banteng camp over the past four months will now be weighed on the Plenary floor.",
	"faction.pdip.deal.pdip_final_appeal.desc": "The time for emissaries, legislative signals, and quiet dinners with Taufik Kiemas has run out. With the MPR Plenary preparing to cast its ballots on your [i]Pidato Pertanggungjawaban[/i], travel personally to Megawati's residence in Kebagusan, sit across from Sukarno's daughter, and ask plainly what it will take for the 153 delegates of [color=__FAC_PDIP__][b]Fraksi PDI Perjuangan[/b][/color] to refrain from bringing down your government tonight. Redeems every political obligation and goodwill gesture you have banked with Diponegoro.",
	"faction.pdip.deal.pdip_final_appeal.text": "Seek a private eleventh-hour audience with Megawati at Kebagusan ahead of the roll call",
	"faction.pdip.deal.pdip_kiemas.alert": "Over a late dinner of Palembang pempek and clove cigarettes far from the television cameras at Senayan, Taufik Kiemas listens with genial, worldly pragmatism. He makes no promises on his wife's behalf, but agrees to keep hotheads in the parliamentary faction from burning every bridge to the Palace.",
	"faction.pdip.deal.pdip_kiemas.desc": "Where Megawati treats politics as a matter of principle, silence, and filial destiny, her husband Taufik Kiemas—a fellow former GMNI activist from South Sumatra who endured New Order prison cells—operates as the pragmatic broker of the Kebagusan household. Bypass the ideological hardliners on the party board and route a quiet overture through Kiemas to keep communication lines open between Bina Graha and Teuku Umar.",
	"faction.pdip.deal.pdip_kiemas.text": "Dispatch an envoy to dine privately with Taufik Kiemas",
	"faction.pdip.deal.pdip_kudatuli.alert": "Wreaths are laid outside the scarred walls of Jalan Diponegoro No. 58 as the Palace's formal acknowledgment is read aloud. Megawati's cadres treat the restitution as long-delayed justice rather than presidential charity, yet the emotional weight of the gesture is unmistakable. Across town, retired New Order generals and Golkar holdovers implicated in the Medan Congress and the July 27 raid react with cold fury.",
	"faction.pdip.deal.pdip_kudatuli.desc": "For Megawati's rank and file, the dawn raid on Jalan Diponegoro No. 58 on July 27, 1996—Peristiwa Kudatuli—remains an open, unavenged wound. While New Order courts blamed the radical PRD and jailed victims' families, the generals and Soerjadi operatives who organized the storming walked free. Issue a formal state apology, return the seized Diponegoro property titles, and authorize a joint fact-finding team ([i]TGPF[/i]) into the assault. Binds PDI Perjuangan's leadership with a deep debt of honor, at the cost of infuriating Golkar's old guard and the Cilangkap brass implicated in the 1996 crackdown.",
	"faction.pdip.deal.pdip_kudatuli.text": "Establish a state inquiry and restitution fund for the July 27, 1996 Kudatuli assault",
	"faction.pdip.deal.pdip_pansus_bankbali.alert": "Cardboard boxes of unredacted clearing slips from Bank Indonesia and BPPN are wheeled directly into the Pansus hearing room at Senayan. PDI Perjuangan's lawmakers hail the disclosure as a triumph of parliamentary oversight, warming considerably toward your office even as Golkar treasurers implicated in the paper trail scramble for legal cover.",
	"faction.pdip.deal.pdip_pansus_bankbali.desc": "The DPR's Special Committee ([i]Pansus Hak Angket Bank Bali[/i]) has spent weeks demanding the unredacted fund-transfer trails connecting PT Era Giat Prima's Rp 546 billion fee to insiders around [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]Golkar[/b][/color] and your own re-election team. [color=__FAC_PDIP__][b]PDI Perjuangan's[/b][/color] investigators on Commission IX have led the charge. Override the bureaucracy and order every ministry, IBRA, and the central bank to hand the full dossier to the committee. Forecloses any backroom attempt to help Golkar bury the audit, while earning a major political obligation from PDI Perjuangan's parliamentary whip.",
	"faction.pdip.deal.pdip_pansus_bankbali.text": "Order Bank Indonesia and IBRA to surrender unredacted Bank Bali files to the DPR Pansus",
	"faction.pdip.deal.pdip_regional.alert": "Once the directive from Bina Graha lands on the Director-General's desk at Depdagri, the stalled regional decrees are signed within forty-eight hours. Secretary-General Alex Litaay and Sutjipto register the gesture without public applause—it is, in their view, merely the Palace returning what was already won at the ballot box—but the friction between regional PDI Perjuangan chapters and Jakarta eases.",
	"faction.pdip.deal.pdip_regional.desc": "Alongside the parliamentary vote, provincial and regency legislatures ([i]DPRD Tingkat I & II[/i]) across Java, Bali, and North Sumatra swept [color=__FAC_PDIP__][b]PDI Perjuangan[/b][/color] into local majorities. Holdover [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]Golkar[/b][/color] bureaucrats inside the Ministry of Home Affairs ([i]Depdagri[/i]), habituated to decades of Yogi S. Memet's administrative manipulation, have been quietly slow-walking the swearing-in of Banteng regional speakers and regents. Instruct Syarwan Hamid's ministry to certify the local results immediately.",
	"faction.pdip.deal.pdip_regional.text": "Order Depdagri to halt bureaucratic obstruction of PDI Perjuangan's local DPRD majorities",
	"faction.pdip.deal.pdip_sukarno_memorial.alert": "The state ceremony honoring Bung Karno draws emotional crowds in Jakarta and at his gravesite in Blitar. Within Kebagusan, where filial devotion to the founding father defines political life, the gesture resonates deeply—even as aging New Order ideologues within Golkar mutter darkly about the return of the Old Order.",
	"faction.pdip.deal.pdip_sukarno_memorial.desc": "For three decades under Suharto, official historiography Downplayed Sukarno's role in founding the Republic, sanitized his teachings on [i]Marhaenisme[/i], and cast a shadow of suspicion over his final years under MPRS Decree No. XXXIII/1967. To Megawati and her followers, the slight against [i]Bung Karno[/i] is deeply personal. Lend the full weight of the presidency to a state-sponsored commemorative program and monument elevating the Proklamator's legacy in Jakarta and Blitar.",
	"faction.pdip.deal.pdip_sukarno_memorial.text": "sponsor a state rehabilitation and monument honoring Bung Karno as Proklamator",
	"faction.pdip.mood.0": "Reluctant Partner",
	"faction.pdip.mood.1": "Open to Dialogue",
	"faction.pdip.mood.2": "Ambivalent",
	"faction.pdip.mood.3": "Guarded",
	"faction.pdip.mood.4": "Skeptical",
	"faction.pdip.mood.5": "Belligerent",
	"faction.pdip.mood.6": "Implacably Hostile",
	"faction.pdip.name": "Fraksi PDI Perjuangan (Megawati)",
	"faction.pdip.portrait_name": "Fraksi PDI Perjuangan\n(Megawati)",
	"faction.pdip.short": "Megawati",
	"faction.pdip.summary": "[color=__FAC_PDIP__][b]The Indonesian Democratic Party of Struggle (PDI Perjuangan)[/b][/color], led by the stoic Megawati Sukarnoputri, commands the single largest bloc in parliament and the undisputed loyalty of the secular-nationalist street. Having captured 33.74% of the national vote—more than 35.6 million ballots—and 153 seats in the June 1999 general election, the Banteng Moncong Putih finished nearly twelve points ahead of [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]Golkar[/b][/color] in second place. To her inner circle on Jalan Kebagusan and the millions of [i]wong cilik[/i] (common folk) who manned neighborhood [i]Posko Gotong Royong[/i] command posts across Java and Bali, the election was not merely a legislative tally; it was a plebiscite on who should sit in Istana Merdeka. Their logic is simple, visceral, and almost impossible to argue against in public: the people voted, [color=__FAC_PDIP__][b]PDI Perjuangan[/b][/color] won, and every week you remain in Bina Graha is a week stolen from a mandate you never earned at the ballot box.\n\nTo Diponegoro's cadres, your administration is an illegitimate remnant of the New Order—a caretaker presidency handed down through Suharto's unilateral resignation rather than popular sovereignty—and no sheaf of reformist decrees erases that original sin. Worse for the Palace, Megawati's red-shirted Satgas paramilitaries and [i]arus bawah[/i] grassroots give the party street-level muscle no other faction can match, a volatile force already massing at the gates of Senayan and the Semanggi cloverleaf whenever rumours of backroom [i]rekayasa politik[/i] (political engineering) surface. Courting this caucus through ordinary Senayan horse-trading is largely futile while the street smells blood. Only if your popular standing and reformist credibility become undeniable in the public eye will their pragmatic operators dare temper their hostility—and even then, they will never forget that they finished first in June and you did not. Short of that, [i]best leave the bull alone.[/i]",
	"faction.pkb.biography": "Formed in July 1998 immediately following the collapse of the New Order, [color=__FAC_PKB__][b]PKB[/b][/color] gave Nahdlatul Ulama's clergy their first legal political vehicle since Suharto's forced 1973 party fusion ([i]fusi[/i]) drove NU into [color=__FAC_PPP__][b]PPP[/b][/color]. Gus Dur—then recovering from a severe stroke that left him visually impaired—envisioned [color=__FAC_PKB__][b]PKB[/b][/color] as an inclusive, nationalist home for traditionalist Islam that contextualized Koranic and Hadith interpretation for a modern democratic society.\n\nInitial assumptions that [color=__FAC_PKB__][b]PKB[/b][/color] would form an automatic coalition with [color=__FAC_PDIP__][b]Megawati Sukarnoputri's PDI Perjuangan[/b][/color]—grounded in Gus Dur and Megawati's long-standing personal friendship—dissolved as Gus Dur began playing the major factions against one another to position himself as the master kingmaker of the transition. Fusing traditional Javanese political intuition with deep theological authority, he moves through Jakarta's corridors as the pivotal figure capable of bridging the secular-religious chasm threatening the Republic.",
	"faction.pkb.deal.pkb_ansor.alert": "The security coordination functions without friction, allowing Banser units to quell potential sectarian flashpoints across Central and East Java without deploying territorial troops. Cilangkap generals, watching a civilian administration parley directly with religious militias, grumble behind closed doors.",
	"faction.pkb.deal.pkb_ansor.desc": "Nahdlatul Ulama's youth wing (GP Ansor) maintains its own uniformed security corps (Banser) across Java, mobilizing hundreds of thousands of young men for crowd control and defense of religious sites. Rather than relying solely on [color=__FAC_ABRI__][b]ABRI[/b][/color] detachments in traditionalist strongholds, open a direct liaison channel to Banser's command staff to maintain public order.",
	"faction.pkb.deal.pkb_ansor.text": "Coordinate security in NU strongholds directly with GP Ansor and Banser militia units",
	"faction.pkb.deal.pkb_fund.alert": "Gus Dur sends his wry, unpredictable regards through an intermediary at Bina Graha, acknowledging the gesture with characteristic dry amusement. In Jombang and the East Java countryside, the rural clerics whose influence drives PKB's turnout register the support with satisfaction.",
	"faction.pkb.deal.pkb_fund.desc": "The rural pesantren networks across East Java—specifically around Jombang and the Tebuireng madrasah founded by Gus Dur's grandfather, Hasyim Asy'ari—form the organizational bedrock beneath [color=__FAC_PKB__][b]PKB's[/b][/color] parliamentary seats. Route a discreet infusion of state agricultural and educational funds directly into those rural districts.",
	"faction.pkb.deal.pkb_fund.text": "Direct state development funds toward the pesantren heartland of East Java",
	"faction.pkb.deal.pkb_gusdur_health.alert": "The assistance is accepted with characteristic dry wit rather than conventional deference. Those closest to Gus Dur note the gesture, recognizing that the Palace extended a humanitarian hand when politics hung in the balance.",
	"faction.pkb.deal.pkb_gusdur_health.desc": "Abdurrahman Wahid's failing vision and chronic health complications require expert neurological attention abroad. Coordinate through a secure private channel—bypassing the public health bureaucracy—to fly specialist physicians to Jakarta or arrange treatment in Europe. Secures a vital political obligation from Gus Dur's inner circle that carries forward into the Central Axis.",
	"faction.pkb.deal.pkb_gusdur_health.text": "Arrange confidential international medical evacuation and specialist care for Gus Dur",
	"faction.pkb.deal.pkb_matori_role.alert": "Matori Abdul Djalil accepts the portfolio with evident pleasure, cementing an institutional bridge between PKB's parliamentary caucus and Bina Graha as the MPR General Session approaches.",
	"faction.pkb.deal.pkb_matori_role.desc": "While Gus Dur holds spiritual command over the party, Matori Abdul Djalil manages [color=__FAC_PKB__][b]PKB's[/b][/color] legislative machinery in Senayan. Elevate Matori to a major cabinet post to anchor the party's institutional wing firmly to your administration ahead of October. Secures a lasting political debt from PKB's parliamentary leadership.",
	"faction.pkb.deal.pkb_matori_role.text": "Appoint PKB Chairman Matori Abdul Djalil to a senior cabinet portfolio",
	"faction.pkb.deal.pkb_nu_congress.alert": "NU's executive board accepts the state contribution with deep appreciation, and news of the presidential backing travels through traditionalist networks across Java within days.",
	"faction.pkb.deal.pkb_nu_congress.desc": "The upcoming national congress of Nahdlatul Ulama and the upkeep of thousands of affiliated boarding schools across the archipelago require substantial financial backing. Authorize a direct state grant to support the proceedings.",
	"faction.pkb.deal.pkb_nu_congress.text": "Subsidize Nahdlatul Ulama's national congress and affiliated regional madrasahs",
	"faction.pkb.mood.0": "Aligned with Gus Dur",
	"faction.pkb.mood.1": "Supportive",
	"faction.pkb.mood.2": "Pragmatic",
	"faction.pkb.mood.3": "Unpredictable",
	"faction.pkb.mood.4": "Distant",
	"faction.pkb.mood.5": "Opposed",
	"faction.pkb.mood.6": "Hostile",
	"faction.pkb.name": "Fraksi Kebangkitan Bangsa (Gus Dur)",
	"faction.pkb.portrait_name": "Fraksi Kebangkitan Bangsa\n(Gus Dur)",
	"faction.pkb.short": "PKB",
	"faction.pkb.summary": "The [color=__FAC_PKB__][b]National Awakening Party (PKB)[/b][/color] functions as the electoral wing of Nahdlatul Ulama (NU), Indonesia's largest traditionalist Islamic organization with over thirty million adherents. While Matori Abdul Djalil holds the chairmanship in Senayan, the party's spiritual and tactical direction obeys Abdurrahman Wahid—[i]Gus Dur[/i]. Winning fifty-one seats in June 1999, [color=__FAC_PKB__][b]PKB[/b][/color] anchors a vast, rural voting bloc concentrated across East and Central Java, where NU's network of ulama, boarding schools ([i]pesantren[/i]), and village shrines outlasts any secular party machine.\n\nTheologically pluralist and fiercely opposed to enforcing Islamic law through the state, [color=__FAC_PKB__][b]PKB[/b][/color] rejects the sectarian rigidities championed by conservative factions. Yet Gus Dur's mercurial political artistry keeps his caucus open to alignment with whoever serves his overarching strategy. Rooted in neo-modernist Islamic discourse, his brand of pluralism harmonizes Islamic jurisprudence with Indonesian nationalism. Financial support for rural pesantren, medical diplomacy, and respect for traditionalist networks secure this bloc's cooperation, though Gus Dur holds ultimate ambition for the presidency himself.",
	"faction.poros_tengah.biography": "Born in Surakarta on April 26, 1944, into a devout Muhammadiyah family, Mohammad Amien Rais wrote his doctoral dissertation at the University of Chicago on the Muslim Brotherhood before returning to teach international relations at Yogyakarta's Gadjah Mada University ([i]UGM[/i]). In 1993, at a time when mentioning presidential succession remained taboo, he broke the silence by floating the issue of [i]suksesi kepemimpinan nasional[/i] in public. Elected chairman of Muhammadiyah—Indonesia's twenty-eight-million-strong modernist Islamic movement—at its 1995 Banda Aceh congress, healso chaired the Council of Experts ([i]Dewan Pakar[/i]) inside your own ICMI until February 1997, when Suharto forced you to oust him after he denounced foreign plunder at the Freeport copper-gold mine in Irian Jaya and the Busang (Bre-X) gold swindle.\n\nThroughout the spring of 1998, Amien lent the campus protest movement nationwide organizational cover, culminating on May 20 when he called off a million-person march at the National Monument ([i]Monas[/i]) after [color=__FAC_ABRI__][b]ABRI[/b][/color] ringed Medan Merdeka with barbed wire and armor—warning that he refused to hand the generals a Tiananmen Square. Hours later, Suharto resigned. Founding [color=__FAC_AXIS__][b]PAN[/b][/color] in August 1998 as an inclusive reform party, Amien suffered a bruising disappointment when Muhammadiyah voters split their ballots in June 1999. Undeterred by fifth place, he now prowls the suites of Senayan, determined to weld Indonesia's fractured Islamic parties into a bloc strong enough to dictate the October succession.",
	"faction.poros_tengah.deal.rais_diplomatic.alert": "The appointments clear the State Secretariat without fanfare. With several of his closest academic colleagues now seated on state advisory boards and embassy rosters, Amien Rais tempers his morning broadsides against Bina Graha.",
	"faction.poros_tengah.deal.rais_diplomatic.desc": "When Amien Rais co-founded the People's Mandate Council (MARA) in May 1998 and launched [color=__FAC_AXIS__][b]PAN[/b][/color] three months later, dozens of reformist academics, economists like Bambang Sudibyo, and engineers like Hatta Rajasa staked their careers on the new party. Open a slate of diplomatic postings abroad and economic advisory seats to nominees Amien's executive board puts forward.",
	"faction.poros_tengah.deal.rais_diplomatic.text": "Appoint MARA intellectuals and PAN cadres to ambassadorships and state advisory councils",
	"faction.poros_tengah.deal.rais_freeport.alert": "Amien Rais savors the mandate as personal vindication for his 1997 ouster from ICMI, praising your willingness to confront New Order resource contracts. Within hours, however, the US Embassy and foreign mining executives wire urgent protests to the Ministry of Mines and Energy.",
	"faction.poros_tengah.deal.rais_freeport.desc": "In February 1997, Suharto forced you to remove Amien Rais as head of ICMI's Council of Experts after he attacked the revenue-sharing terms of PT Freeport Indonesia's Grasberg mine in Irian Jaya and the Busang gold scandal involving Cendana cronies. Settle that old score between you by granting [color=__FAC_AXIS__][b]Fraksi Reformasi[/b][/color] a mandate to audit foreign mining Contracts of Work ([i]Kontrak Karya[/i]). Secures a personal political obligation from Amien Rais, though Wall Street investors and Washington diplomats will bristle at the contract review.",
	"faction.poros_tengah.deal.rais_freeport.text": "Authorize a parliamentary review of Freeport-McMoRan's Contract of Work and New Order mining concessions",
	"faction.poros_tengah.deal.rais_islamic_law.alert": "Amien Rais welcomes the overture as a breakthrough for regional self-determination, and modernist lawmakers across PAN and PPP rally behind the framework. At Jalan Diponegoro, however, Megawati's deputies condemn the pledge as a backdoor assault on the unitary Pancasila state.",
	"faction.poros_tengah.deal.rais_islamic_law.desc": "Since campaigning in Banda Aceh and West Sumatra, Amien Rais has championed asymmetric decentralization—arguing that provinces with deep Islamic traditions should receive statutory authority to implement religious law in education, family courts, and public custom without reviving a nationwide constitutional fight over the Jakarta Charter. Signal through Bina Graha that your administration backs provincial religious autonomy. Binds Fraksi Reformasi's leadership with a lasting political debt, while provoking fierce pushback from PDI Perjuangan's secular nationalists.",
	"faction.poros_tengah.deal.rais_islamic_law.text": "Endorse statutory autonomy for provincial implementation of Islamic legal frameworks",
	"faction.poros_tengah.deal.rais_muhammadiyah.alert": "From Yogyakarta to Padang, Muhammadiyah's regional boards welcome the grants as vital relief for schools and clinics battered by inflation. Word of the Palace's generosity reaches Amien Rais through Syafii Maarif before the week is out.",
	"faction.poros_tengah.deal.rais_muhammadiyah.desc": "Although Amien Rais handed the chairmanship of Muhammadiyah to Ahmad Syafii Maarif when he founded [color=__FAC_AXIS__][b]PAN[/b][/color], the organization's sprawling network of schools, universities, and PKU hospitals remains his spiritual home—and a bridge to your own Minister of Religious Affairs, Malik Fadjar. Release a tranche of state social-safety-net funds to subsidize Muhammadiyah's urban clinics and colleges.",
	"faction.poros_tengah.deal.rais_muhammadiyah.text": "Direct state health and education grants to Muhammadiyah's universities and PKU clinics",
	"faction.poros_tengah.deal.rais_reformasi_credit.alert": "The tribute costs the treasury nothing and flatters Amien Rais's acute sense of historical destiny. Campus activist networks who marched behind him in May 1998 welcome the speech as overdue candor from the Palace.",
	"faction.poros_tengah.deal.rais_reformasi_credit.desc": "Inside [color=__FAC_AXIS__][b]PAN's[/b][/color] headquarters, resentment lingers that your cabinet claimed the institutional fruits of Suharto's resignation while Amien Rais—who risked arrest rallying students and defused a bloodbath at Monas on May 20, 1998—was left on the outside. Use a televised address from Istana Negara to salute Amien by name as the foremost catalyst of Indonesia's democratic awakening.",
	"faction.poros_tengah.deal.rais_reformasi_credit.text": "Hail Amien Rais in a state address as the moral architect of the May 1998 Reformasi movement",
	"faction.poros_tengah.merged.biography": "For half a century, rivalry between urban modernist Muslims in Muhammadiyah and rural traditionalist clerics in Nahdlatul Ulama divided Indonesian Islam, a fracture dating back to NU's 1952 break from Masyumi. Yet as the summer of 1999 wore on and the prospect of a polarized showdown between your embattled administration and [color=__FAC_PDIP__][b]Megawati Sukarnoputri's PDI Perjuangan[/b][/color] loomed over Jakarta, Amien Rais executed the boldest maneuver of the transition.\n\nShuttle-diplomacy between Gus Dur's headquarters in Ciganjur, Hamzah Haz's offices at [color=__FAC_PPP__][b]PPP[/b][/color], and the modernist leaders of [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]PBB[/b][/color] and Partai Keadilan produced the [color=__FAC_AXIS__][b]Poros Tengah[/b][/color]. Having captured the MPR Speakership with backing from across the Islamic spectrum, Amien Rais now holds the gavel of the General Session while Gus Dur waits in the wings as the coalition's dark-horse presidential contender. To survive the accountability vote, you must convince Amien, Gus Dur, and Hamzah Haz that keeping you in Istana Merdeka serves the Islamic caucus better than claiming the crown for themselves.",
	"faction.poros_tengah.merged.deal.axis_cabinet.alert": "Behind closed doors at Senayan, the power-sharing offer shifts the calculus inside the Central Axis, drawing PPP and PAN negotiators toward your column. At PDI Perjuangan's headquarters, word of the compact sparks outrage as Megawati's strategists realize they are being boxed out of the coalition math.",
	"faction.poros_tengah.merged.deal.axis_cabinet.desc": "Since the [color=__FAC_AXIS__][b]Poros Tengah[/b][/color] coalesced, its brokers have made clear the price of keeping Gus Dur from challenging you on the floor: the Vice Presidency and control over key economic and welfare portfolios for [color=__FAC_AXIS__][b]PAN[/b][/color], [color=__FAC_PPP__][b]PPP[/b][/color], and [color=__FAC_PKB__][b]PKB[/b][/color]. Put the power-sharing compact on the table in exchange for whip instructions backing your accountability speech across all 163 Axis delegates. Secures a binding coalition obligation from the Central Axis, while infuriating PDI Perjuangan.",
	"faction.poros_tengah.merged.deal.axis_cabinet.text": "Pledge the Vice Presidency and senior economic ministries to the Central Axis leadership",
	"faction.poros_tengah.merged.deal.axis_education.alert": "Ulama and school directors across both Nahdlatul Ulama and Muhammadiyah hail the directive, noting that no administration in the Republic's history has expanded the religious education budget on such a scale.",
	"faction.poros_tengah.merged.deal.axis_education.desc": "Both wings of the [color=__FAC_AXIS__][b]Central Axis[/b][/color]—traditionalist NU kiai and modernist Muhammadiyah educators—depend on funding administered by Minister of Religious Affairs Malik Fadjar. Sign an executive directive doubling state educational subsidies for rural [i]madrasah[/i], [i]pesantren[/i], and Islamic universities before the plenary vote. Places the clerical leadership of the Central Axis in your debt.",
	"faction.poros_tengah.merged.deal.axis_education.text": "Double Ministry of Religious Affairs budget allocations for NU pesantren and Muhammadiyah schools",
	"faction.poros_tengah.merged.deal.axis_final_deal.alert": "After hours of hard-nosed bargaining over tea in a guarded suite at the Hotel Mulia, Amien Rais, Gus Dur, and Hamzah Haz rise to shake your hand. Every political debt you banked with PAN, PKB, and PPP has been laid on the table before the morning session gavels in.",
	"faction.poros_tengah.merged.deal.axis_final_deal.desc": "Commanding 163 ballots on the plenary floor, the [color=__FAC_AXIS__][b]Central Axis[/b][/color] holds the fate of your presidency in its hands. Sit down behind closed doors at the Hotel Mulia with Amien Rais, Abdurrahman Wahid, Hamzah Haz, and Yusril Ihza Mahendra to call in every promise, subsidy, and political debt you have accumulated across [color=__FAC_AXIS__][b]PAN[/b][/color], [color=__FAC_PKB__][b]PKB[/b][/color], and [color=__FAC_PPP__][b]PPP[/b][/color]. Redeems every political obligation the Central Axis and its constituent parties owe the Palace.",
	"faction.poros_tengah.merged.deal.axis_final_deal.text": "Convene a midnight summit with Amien Rais, Gus Dur, and Hamzah Haz before the ballot boxes open",
	"faction.poros_tengah.merged.deal.axis_hajj_quota.alert": "News of the revised Hajj quota allocations spreads through provincial religious offices and KBIH travel boards within hours, giving the Central Axis's regional operators a tangible stake in your survival.",
	"faction.poros_tengah.merged.deal.axis_hajj_quota.desc": "The Ministry of Religious Affairs oversees Indonesia's two-hundred-thousand-pilgrim annual Hajj quota and the lucrative Ongkos Naik Haji (ONH) guidance foundations ([i]KBIH[/i]). Revise this year's allocation formula to favor regional pilgrimage foundations tied to [color=__FAC_PPP__][b]PPP[/b][/color], NU, and Muhammadiyah chapters inside the [color=__FAC_AXIS__][b]Central Axis[/b][/color].",
	"faction.poros_tengah.merged.deal.axis_hajj_quota.text": "Reallocate provincial Hajj pilgrimage quotas and ONH travel charters to Axis-affiliated foundations",
	"faction.poros_tengah.merged.deal.axis_ppp_courtship.alert": "Hamzah Haz accepts the prominent drafting role with practiced parliamentary poise, and PPP's fifty-eight delegates inside the Central Axis soften their rhetoric toward your accountability report.",
	"faction.poros_tengah.merged.deal.axis_ppp_courtship.desc": "Within the [color=__FAC_AXIS__][b]Central Axis[/b][/color], [color=__FAC_PPP__][b]United Development Party (PPP)[/b][/color] chairman Hamzah Haz—who served in your cabinet as Minister of Investment before stepping down to lead his fifty-eight-seat caucus—commands the single largest party bloc. Elevate Hamzah Haz as the Palace's chief partner in drafting the 1999–2004 Broad Outlines of State Policy ([i]GBHN[/i]).",
	"faction.poros_tengah.merged.deal.axis_ppp_courtship.text": "Recognize PPP Chairman Hamzah Haz as lead co-author of the MPR's State Policy Guidelines (GBHN)",
	"faction.poros_tengah.merged.deal.axis_speaker_deference.alert": "Amien Rais registers the Palace's deference from the Speaker's podium with a satisfied nod, smoothing procedural friction between Bina Graha's floor managers and the MPR leadership ahead of the accountability vote.",
	"faction.poros_tengah.merged.deal.axis_speaker_deference.desc": "From the rostrum of the MPR General Session, Speaker Amien Rais controls the procedural clock, the rules of order ([i]Tata Tertib[/i]), and the mechanism for tallying ballots on your accountability report. Instruct your floor managers in [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]Golkar[/b][/color] to defer to Amien's rulings from the chair rather than contesting his gavel on the floor.",
	"faction.poros_tengah.merged.deal.axis_speaker_deference.text": "Defer to MPR Speaker Amien Rais on plenary rules and commission scheduling",
	"faction.poros_tengah.merged.mood.0": "Standing with Habibie",
	"faction.poros_tengah.merged.mood.1": "Leaning Toward Habibie",
	"faction.poros_tengah.merged.mood.2": "Weighing Options",
	"faction.poros_tengah.merged.mood.3": "Skeptical",
	"faction.poros_tengah.merged.mood.4": "Preparing Gus Dur's Bid",
	"faction.poros_tengah.merged.mood.5": "United Against Habibie",
	"faction.poros_tengah.merged.mood.6": "Mobilized to Unseat Habibie",
	"faction.poros_tengah.merged.name": "Poros Tengah (Amien Rais & Abdurrahman Wahid)",
	"faction.poros_tengah.merged.portrait_name": "Poros Tengah\n(Amien Rais & Abdurrahman Wahid)",
	"faction.poros_tengah.merged.summary": "Orchestrated by Amien Rais alongside [color=__FAC_PPP__][b]PPP's Hamzah Haz[/b][/color] and [color=__FAC_PKB__][b]PKB's Abdurrahman Wahid (Gus Dur)[/b][/color], the [color=__FAC_AXIS__][b]Central Axis (Poros Tengah)[/b][/color] has upended the arithmetic of the 1999 General Session overnight. By welding together [color=__FAC_AXIS__][b]Fraksi Reformasi (PAN & PK)[/b][/color], [color=__FAC_PPP__][b]PPP[/b][/color], [color=__FAC_PKB__][b]PKB[/b][/color], [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]Yusril Ihza Mahendra's PBB[/b][/color], and the [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]Daulatul Ummah[/b][/color] splinters under the banner of Islamic fraternity ([i]Ukhuwah Islamiyah[/i]), Amien has assembled a 163-seat coalition that outnumbers both [color=__FAC_PDIP__][b]PDI Perjuangan[/b][/color] and [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]Golkar[/b][/color].\n\nBeneath the surface, the [color=__FAC_AXIS__][b]Central Axis[/b][/color] remains a marriage of convenience between lifelong rivals: Muhammadiyah modernists and Nahdlatul Ulama traditionalists, campus [i]Tarbiyah[/i] purists in [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]PK[/b][/color] and seasoned New Order survivors in [color=__FAC_PPP__][b]PPP[/b][/color]. What holds them together is a shared refusal to surrender the Republic to Megawati's secular-nationalist camp—and Amien's gambit of floating Gus Dur as an alternative presidential nominee should your candidacy falter. Strong reformist credibility and public standing remain essential to bargaining with this bloc, for neither Bina Graha nor Diponegoro can reach 351 votes in Senayan without winning over—or splitting—the Axis.",
	"faction.poros_tengah.mood.0": "Supportive",
	"faction.poros_tengah.mood.1": "Intrigued",
	"faction.poros_tengah.mood.2": "Observing",
	"faction.poros_tengah.mood.3": "Skeptical",
	"faction.poros_tengah.mood.4": "Critical",
	"faction.poros_tengah.mood.5": "Condemnatory",
	"faction.poros_tengah.mood.6": "Fierce Opponent",
	"faction.poros_tengah.name": "Fraksi Reformasi (Amien Rais)",
	"faction.poros_tengah.portrait_name": "Fraksi Reformasi\n(Amien Rais)",
	"faction.poros_tengah.short": "A. Rais",
	"faction.poros_tengah.summary": "Chairman of the [color=__FAC_AXIS__][b]National Mandate Party (PAN)[/b][/color] and standard-bearer of the 1998 student uprising, Amien Rais commands a parliamentary footprint far smaller than his national stature suggests. After [color=__FAC_AXIS__][b]PAN[/b][/color] captured 7.12% of the June 1999 vote—thirty-four seats in Senayan, pooled with the seven lawmakers of the [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]Justice Party (PK)[/b][/color] to form [color=__FAC_AXIS__][b]Fraksi Reformasi[/b][/color]—the Yogyakarta political scientist lacks the raw ballot numbers to claim the presidency on his own. What he wields instead is moral authority and tactical audacity. Having stared down Suharto's generals in May 1998, Amien dominates television studios and newspaper front pages, operating as an agile political sniper who watches [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]Golkar[/b][/color] and [color=__FAC_PDIP__][b]PDI Perjuangan[/b][/color] batter each other while he brokers a third path behind closed doors.\n\nInside [color=__FAC_AXIS__][b]Fraksi Reformasi[/b][/color], urban Muhammadiyah modernists sit beside secular-pluralist intellectuals from the People's Mandate Council (MARA) and former political prisoners like A.M. Fatwa. None of them trust the New Order holdovers crowding your cabinet, yet they harbor equal dread of a Megawati presidency hostile to political Islam. Demonstrating genuine reformist credentials and sustaining public support give the Palace strong leverage over Amien's caucus, though the man Jakarta's press dubs the Kingmaker never stops calculating his next move.",
	"faction.post_speech_note": "Routine pre-session overtures are closed; only Last-Minute Appeals remain open.",
	"faction.ppp.biography": "Born in Ketapang, West Kalimantan, on February 15, 1940, Hamzah Haz taught school, edited a Pontianak newspaper, and chaired rural banking cooperatives before entering the West Kalimantan provincial legislature in 1968 under the banner of Nahdlatul Ulama. Moving to Senayan in 1971, he absorbed the shock of January 5, 1973, when the New Order forced NU, Parmusi, PSII, and PERTI to fuse into [color=__FAC_PPP__][b]PPP[/b][/color]. Over the next quarter-century—even after NU withdrew from formal party politics in 1984 and Suharto's [i]Asas Tunggal[/i] laws stripped [color=__FAC_PPP__][b]PPP[/b][/color] of its Islamic foundation and Ka'bah emblem—Hamzah stayed inside parliament, mastering the state ledger on the DPR Budget Commission (Komisi APBN).\n\nYou brought him into the Development Reform Cabinet as Minister of Investment in May 1998. Six months later, at [color=__FAC_PPP__][b]PPP's[/b][/color] Fourth National Congress ([i]Muktamar IV[/i]) at Pondok Gede, delegates restored Islam as the party's ideological foundation, brought back the Ka'bah symbol, and elected Hamzah Haz party chairman over A.M. Saefuddin. When [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]Golkar[/b][/color] demanded that ministers from rival parties resign ahead of the June 1999 campaign, Hamzah surrendered his portfolio without rancor and steered [color=__FAC_PPP__][b]PPP[/b][/color] to fifty-eight seats. An understated accountant by training and temperament, he weighs your accountability report like a balance sheet—ready to extend credit if your government stays solvent, or call in his markers with Amien Rais and Gus Dur if the Palace faces bankruptcy.",
	"faction.ppp.deal.ppp_fusion_history.alert": "Veteran Ka'bah lawmakers who endured decades of state surveillance and forced leadership coups under the New Order greet your statement with visible emotion, while old-guard Golkar operatives bristle at the indictment of Suharto's political architecture.",
	"faction.ppp.deal.ppp_fusion_history.desc": "For veterans of [color=__FAC_PPP__][b]PPP[/b][/color] like Hamzah Haz, Bachtiar Chamsyah, and Aisyah Aminy, the trauma of Suharto's 1973 party fusion—followed by intelligence operative Ali Moertopo's meddling and the 1984 law that outlawed the Ka'bah emblem—remains a bitter memory. Deliver a formal speech acknowledging that the New Order's subjugation of [color=__FAC_PPP__][b]PPP[/b][/color] was an abuse of state power.",
	"faction.ppp.deal.ppp_fusion_history.text": "Repudiate the New Order's 1973 forced party fusion and Asas Tunggal coercion on the record",
	"faction.ppp.deal.ppp_gender_debate.alert": "Tracts and Friday sermons debating female leadership multiply across West Java, Madura, and South Kalimantan, hardening the theological barrier between PPP's fifty-eight delegates and Megawati's camp while provoking outrage from PDI Perjuangan and civil-society feminists.",
	"faction.ppp.deal.ppp_gender_debate.desc": "Since the November 1998 Congress of the Indonesian Muslim Community ([i]KUII[/i]) and fiery statements by [color=__FAC_PPP__][b]PPP[/b][/color] minister A.M. Saefuddin, conservative ulama inside [color=__FAC_PPP__][b]PPP's[/b][/color] Majelis Syariah have argued that Islamic jurisprudence forbids a woman from serving as head of state—a ruling aimed straight at Megawati Sukarnoputri. Use state-linked Islamic publications and Friday pulpit networks to give those clerical rulings wider circulation.",
	"faction.ppp.deal.ppp_gender_debate.text": "Amplify the clerical fiqh debate over female executive leadership",
	"faction.ppp.deal.ppp_hamzah_role.alert": "Hamzah Haz receives the offer with his trademark understated composure. Having spent decades mastering state budgets from the opposition benches, the prospect of helming Indonesia's entire economic cabinet softens his caucus's posture toward the Palace.",
	"faction.ppp.deal.ppp_hamzah_role.desc": "Hamzah Haz spent a year running the Investment Coordinating Board (BKPM) in your cabinet before [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]Golkar[/b][/color] forced party chairmen to vacate their ministerial posts in May 1999. Promise him that if your administration wins a full mandate in October, he will return to the cabinet room promoted to Coordinating Minister for Economy, Finance, and Industry ([i]Menko Ekuin[/i]). Binds PPP's leadership with a lasting political obligation that carries forward into the Central Axis.",
	"faction.ppp.deal.ppp_hamzah_role.text": "Pledge the Coordinating Ministry for Economy and Finance (Menko Ekuin) to Hamzah Haz",
	"faction.ppp.deal.ppp_pesantren_visit.alert": "Photographs of you kneeling beside the senior kiai of Madura and Rembang run across the front pages of the Islamic press. The elders of PPP's Majelis Syariah send warm word to Hamzah Haz in Jakarta.",
	"faction.ppp.deal.ppp_pesantren_visit.desc": "Even after Gus Dur launched [color=__FAC_PKB__][b]PKB[/b][/color], revered traditionalist kiai like K.H. Alawy Muhammad in Sampang, Madura, and K.H. Maimun Zubair at Pesantren Al-Anwar in Sarang, Rembang, kept their flocks loyal to the Ka'bah. Travel by presidential helicopter to pay homage at their boarding schools,wearing a peci and joining the santri in afternoon prayer.",
	"faction.ppp.deal.ppp_pesantren_visit.text": "Pay a state visit to PPP's flagship pesantren strongholds in Madura and Rembang",
	"faction.ppp.deal.ppp_subsidies.alert": "As a veteran of the DPR Budget Commission, Hamzah Haz inspects the revised Depag budget tables himself before nodding in approval. With their rural madrasah funding protected from the IMF's scalpel, PPP's lawmakers warm toward Bina Graha.",
	"faction.ppp.deal.ppp_subsidies.desc": "Structural adjustment targets drafted by the IMF call for across-the-board reductions in social spending, threatening the Ministry of Religious Affairs (Depag) grant lines that sustain the [i]Madrasah Diniyah[/i] and rural [i]pesantren[/i] networks anchoring [color=__FAC_PPP__][b]PPP's[/b][/color] electorate. Give Hamzah Haz and parliamentary whip Zarkasih Nur a written guarantee that religious schooling funds remain untouched. Secures a binding political debt from PPP's leadership that carries forward into the Central Axis.",
	"faction.ppp.deal.ppp_subsidies.text": "Ring-fence Ministry of Religious Affairs madrasah subsidies against IMF austerity cuts",
	"faction.ppp.mood.0": "Aligned",
	"faction.ppp.mood.1": "Favorable",
	"faction.ppp.mood.2": "Neutral",
	"faction.ppp.mood.3": "Cautious",
	"faction.ppp.mood.4": "Distanced",
	"faction.ppp.mood.5": "Opposed",
	"faction.ppp.mood.6": "Irreconcilable",
	"faction.ppp.name": "Fraksi PPP (Hamzah Haz)",
	"faction.ppp.portrait_name": "Fraksi PPP\n(Hamzah Haz)",
	"faction.ppp.short": "H. Haz",
	"faction.ppp.summary": "Chaired by the measured budget veteran Hamzah Haz, the [color=__FAC_PPP__][b]United Development Party (PPP)[/b][/color] stands as the oldest surviving Islamic party in the Republic. Born out of Suharto's forced 1973 merger of four Muslim parties, the Ka'bah party defied predictions that new rivals like [color=__FAC_PKB__][b]PKB[/b][/color] and [color=__FAC_AXIS__][b]PAN[/b][/color] would hollow out its base, capturing 10.71% of the national ballot—11.3 million votes and fifty-eight parliamentary seats—to finish third in June 1999. That resilience rests on a quarter-century of parish-level organizing across Aceh, West Java, South Kalimantan, West Sumatra, and Madura, where loyal ulama and rural boarding schools ([i]pesantren[/i]) rallied to the restored Ka'bah banner.\n\nThough Hamzah Haz served a full year inside your cabinet as State Minister of Investment (BKPM) before stepping down in May 1999 to lead [color=__FAC_PPP__][b]PPP's[/b][/color] campaign, thirty years of surviving New Order parliaments have trained him never to lash his party to a sinking hull. [color=__FAC_PPP__][b]PPP's[/b][/color] clerical council rejects secularization and invokes classical [i]fiqh[/i] doctrine to oppose a female president, erecting an ideological wall between Hamzah Haz and Megawati Sukarnoputri. Yet Hamzah knows every skeleton in your administration's closet and keeps his caucus positioned to pivot toward [color=__FAC_AXIS__][b]Amien Rais's Central Axis[/b][/color] if your numbers falter. Preserving public order across the provinces and commanding broad popular approval give the Palace strong leverage over PPP's cautious lawmakers, who dread street upheaval and shrink from backing an isolated president.",
	"faction.resolve_first": "Resolve the current crisis before interacting with the factions.",
	"faction.session_closed": "The MPR General Session has already convened. Only Final Appeals may be used now.",
	"faction.surcharge_note": "Faction engagements already held this turn: $COUNT$. Every interaction here carries a surcharge of $SURCHARGE$ PC.",
	"faction.utusan_daerah.biography": "Across the archipelago beyond Jakarta's ring roads, the fall of Suharto unleashed thirty years of pent-up regional grievance against Java-centric rule. Under the Law No. 5/1974 system, the Ministry of Home Affairs (Depdagri) treated governors as Jakarta's viceroys while Jalan Cendana conglomerates carved up outer-island timber, mining, and plantation concessions.\n\nSelected by the newlyseated 1999 provincial assemblies rather than handpicked by Suharto's interior ministry, this cohort of [color=__CLR_MUTED__][b]Utusan Daerah[/b][/color] mixes sitting governors, regional chamber-of-commerce bosses like West Kalimantan's Oesman Sapta Odang and West Sumatra's Irman Gusman, university rectors, and traditional aristocrats. While your administration won praise in the outer islands by tasking Ryaas Rasyid's team with drafting the landmark 1999 Regional Autonomy statutes, separatist flashpoints in Aceh, East Timor, and Irian Jaya alongside communal bloodshed in Maluku and West Kalimantan keep these delegates on edge. In the October session, their 135 ballots represent the largest unaligned prize on the floor.",
	"faction.utusan_daerah.deal.daerah_aceh_papua.alert": "Civic and provincial delegates from Banda Aceh and Jayapura welcome the Special Autonomy framework as the first serious alternative to armed conflict in a generation, though Cilangkap officers and PDI Perjuangan nationalists warn that asymmetric concessions invite the breakup of the unitary state.",
	"faction.utusan_daerah.deal.daerah_aceh_papua.desc": "At opposite ends of the archipelago, Aceh and Irian Jaya teeter on the brink of secession after decades of [color=__FAC_ABRI__][b]ABRI[/b][/color] counter-insurgency operations and resource extraction. Put a formal Special Autonomy ([i]Otonomi Khusus[/i]) framework on the table for both provinces—granting Banda Aceh authority over religious, educational, and customary affairs while returning mineral royalties and cultural recognition to Jayapura.",
	"faction.utusan_daerah.deal.daerah_aceh_papua.text": "Offer asymmetric Special Autonomy charters to the delegations from Aceh and Irian Jaya",
	"faction.utusan_daerah.deal.daerah_final_appeal.alert": "The switchboard at Bina Graha stays lit past dawn as governors from Makassar, Pekanbaru, Samarinda, and Padang pledge their five-member delegations to the first non-Javanese President of the Republic.",
	"faction.utusan_daerah.deal.daerah_final_appeal.desc": "Spread across twenty-seven provincial delegations from Sabang to Merauke, the 135 seats of [color=__CLR_MUTED__][b]Fraksi Utusan Daerah[/b][/color] form the third-largest voting bloc in the MPR. Spend the final night before the ballot boxes open calling the governors and delegation chairs across all three Indonesian time zones to remind them that you—a son of Parepare, South Sulawesi, and the architect of [i]Otonomi Daerah[/i]—are the outer islands' champion in Jakarta. Calls in every decentralization pledge and political debt the regional delegations owe the Palace.",
	"faction.utusan_daerah.deal.daerah_final_appeal.text": "Work the telephones across all twenty-seven provincial capitals on the eve of the roll call",
	"faction.utusan_daerah.deal.daerah_infra.alert": "Bulldozers and road crews return to work across a dozen provinces within weeks of the disbursement. Grateful for tangible projects they can showcase at home, the regional governors instruct their MPR delegations to back Bina Graha.",
	"faction.utusan_daerah.deal.daerah_infra.desc": "The 1997–1998 monetary collapse froze public works from Sumatra's trans-highway to inter-island ferry terminals in Maluku and Nusa Tenggara. Authorize an immediate tranche of block grants through the National Development Planning Agency (Bappenas) so provincial governors can restart stalled bridge, port, and irrigation projects before the MPR convenes.",
	"faction.utusan_daerah.deal.daerah_infra.text": "Release emergency General Allocation Funds (DAU) for provincial roads, ports, and irrigation",
	"faction.utusan_daerah.deal.daerah_otonomi_law.alert": "By overriding the central bureaucracy and signing the implementing regulations on the spot, you convince skeptical provincial leaders that Otonomi Daerah is law in practice, not just on paper.",
	"faction.utusan_daerah.deal.daerah_otonomi_law.desc": "Although parliament passed Law No. 22/1999 on regional government and Law No. 25/1999 on central-regional fiscal balance in May, career mandarins in Jakarta's ministries have slow-walked the implementing government regulations ([i]Peraturan Pemerintah[/i]) needed to transfer authority to the provinces and regencies. Back Director-General Ryaas Rasyid and sign the implementing decrees ahead of the statutory deadline. Secures a binding political debt from the Regional Delegates Faction.",
	"faction.utusan_daerah.deal.daerah_otonomi_law.text": "Accelerate Ryaas Rasyid's implementing decrees for Laws No. 22 and No. 25 on Regional Autonomy",
	"faction.utusan_daerah.deal.daerah_revenue_formula.alert": "Governors and DPRD speakers from Riau, East Kalimantan, and Irian Jaya hail the revised royalty split as a historic correction of New Order fiscal plunder. Their delegates in Senayan shift toward the Palace column, even as central treasury officials and PDI Perjuangan lawmakers protest the drain on Jakarta's coffers.",
	"faction.utusan_daerah.deal.daerah_revenue_formula.desc": "Resource-rich provinces—Riau, East Kalimantan, Aceh, and Irian Jaya—have watched Pertamina and Jakarta ministries pocket the lion's share of their oil, gas, timber, and mineral royalties for three decades, fueling talk of a Free Riau ([i]Riau Merdeka[/i]) in Pekanbaru and federalist demands in Samarinda. Instruct the Ministry of Finance to expand the regional revenue-sharing allocation ([i]Dana Bagi Hasil[/i]) for producing provinces ahead of statutory schedule. Binds the outer-island delegations to the Palace with a major political obligation, though central budget reserves and PDI Perjuangan's unitary nationalists will absorb the blow.",
	"faction.utusan_daerah.deal.daerah_revenue_formula.text": "Revise the oil, gas, and forestry revenue-sharing formula in favor of resource-producing provinces",
	"faction.utusan_daerah.deal.daerah_sultan.alert": "Sultan Hamengkubuwono X receives you inside the Kraton pavilion with classic Javanese grace. Television footage of the cordial audience reassures undecided provincial delegates across Java and the outer islands that the Palace respects regional dignity.",
	"faction.utusan_daerah.deal.daerah_sultan.desc": "Sri Sultan Hamengkubuwono X—who stood before a million citizens at the May 1998 [i]Pisowanan Agung[/i] in Yogyakarta to back peaceful reform and joined the Ciganjur quartet alongside Megawati, Gus Dur, and Amien Rais—commands unmatched moral authority among Indonesia's governors and traditional rulers. Travel to the Yogyakarta Kraton to endorse his formal confirmation as Governor and seek his counsel on healing the Republic.",
	"faction.utusan_daerah.deal.daerah_sultan.text": "Pay a state visit to Kraton Ngayogyakarta and consult Sultan Hamengkubuwono X",
	"faction.utusan_daerah.mood.0": "Secured",
	"faction.utusan_daerah.mood.1": "Content",
	"faction.utusan_daerah.mood.2": "Split",
	"faction.utusan_daerah.mood.3": "Nervous",
	"faction.utusan_daerah.mood.4": "Demanding Funds",
	"faction.utusan_daerah.mood.5": "Seeking New Patrons",
	"faction.utusan_daerah.mood.6": "Habibie Must Go",
	"faction.utusan_daerah.name": "Fraksi Utusan Daerah",
	"faction.utusan_daerah.portrait_name": "Fraksi Utusan Daerah",
	"faction.utusan_daerah.short": "U. Daerah",
	"faction.utusan_daerah.summary": "The [color=__CLR_MUTED__][b]Regional Delegates Faction (Fraksi Utusan Daerah)[/b][/color] brings together 135 provincial representatives—five delegates elected by each of the twenty-seven provincial legislatures ([i]DPRD Tingkat I[/i]) under Law No. 4/1999. More akin to a loose congress of provincial barons than a disciplined parliamentary party, this caucus answers to no single national chairman. Without a central whip in Senayan to enforce uniformity, delegations from Sumatra, Kalimantan, Sulawesi, and eastern Indonesia bargain province by province, trading their ballots to whichever camp offers the best terms for their home capitals.\n\nFor thirty-two years under the New Order, Jakarta treated the outer islands as resource colonies, siphoning oil from Riau, liquefied natural gas from Aceh and East Kalimantan, and copper and gold from Irian Jaya while returning a fraction of the proceeds through central [i]Inpres[/i] grants. Now that Suharto's iron grip has broken, governors, regents, and customary ([i]adat[/i]) elders demand fiscal restitution and self-rule. Delivering macroeconomic recovery and preserving civic order across the provinces give the Palace decisive leverage over these regional delegates, who prize solvent development budgets and protection from separatist upheaval above ideological crusades.",
	"faction.utusan_golongan.biography": "Born out of the 1945 Constitution's provision for societal representation in the MPR, the [color=__CLR_MUTED__][b]Utusan Golongan[/b][/color] seats were subverted after 1966 into an instrument of New Order state corporatism. In the wake of the 1965–1966 purge of the leftist labor federation [i]SOBSI[/i], Suharto's security apparatus herding urban factory workers into the state-policed All-Indonesia Workers Union (SPSI), while independent organizers like Muchtar Pakpahan and Dita Indah Sari were thrown into prison and the murdered East Java strike leader Marsinah became a martyr for underground labor.\n\nThe collapse of Suharto's regime in May 1998 shattered that corporatist monopoly. Within weeks of taking office, your cabinet freed Muchtar Pakpahan from Cipinang Prison, ratified ILO Convention No. 87 on freedom of association, and opened the [color=__CLR_MUTED__][b]Utusan Golongan[/b][/color] nomination process to independent NGOs, the Indonesian Women's Coalition (KPI), LIPI researchers, and the interfaith councils (PGI, KWI, PHDI, and Walubi). Though grateful for the breathing room of the post-1998 thaw, these sixty-five delegates remain vigilant against any relapse into military impunity or New Order authoritarianism.",
	"faction.utusan_golongan.deal.golongan_final_appeal.alert": "The scholars, unionists, and interfaith leaders of Fraksi Utusan Golongan hear your appeal with thoughtful gravity. Having weighed the laws you signed against the authoritarian system you inherited, your allies inside the caucus rise to rally their colleagues before the ballot boxes open.",
	"faction.utusan_golongan.deal.golongan_final_appeal.desc": "Unlike the party machines trading cabinet seats in the hotel suites, the sixty-five scholars, labor organizers, women's advocates, and interfaith leaders of [color=__CLR_MUTED__][b]Fraksi Utusan Golongan[/b][/color] judge your administration on its reform ledger: press freedom, political prisoner releases, the Komnas Perempuan commission, and democratic elections. Meet their caucus in Senayan before the roll call and ask them to weigh your sixteen months of reform on the merits. Redeems every reform commitment and political obligation banked with the civil-society caucus.",
	"faction.utusan_golongan.deal.golongan_final_appeal.text": "Deliver a candid appeal to the sixty-five civil-society and minority delegates before the ballot",
	"faction.utusan_golongan.deal.golongan_ilo_labor.alert": "Independent trade unionists and International Labour Organization monitors in Geneva praise the regulations as the death knell of New Order corporatist labor control, cementing goodwill across the Utusan Golongan benches.",
	"faction.utusan_golongan.deal.golongan_ilo_labor.desc": "Although Manpower Minister Fahmi Idris ratified ILO Convention No. 87 in June 1998, factory owners and local security commanders still favor the New Order's corporatist union monopoly (FSPSI) to suppress strikes in Tangerang, Bekasi, and Surabaya. Issue binding ministerial regulations compelling industrial estates to recognize independent labor federations at the bargaining table. Secures a major political obligation from labor and civic delegates in the MPR.",
	"faction.utusan_golongan.deal.golongan_ilo_labor.text": "Enforce ILO Convention No. 87 and grant collective-bargaining rights to independent unions",
	"faction.utusan_golongan.deal.golongan_komnas.alert": "Civic and religious delegates inside Fraksi Utusan Golongan hail the presidential backing for Komnas HAM as proof that the era of state impunity is ending, even as generals in Cilangkap bristle at civilian investigators summoning active-duty officers.",
	"faction.utusan_golongan.deal.golongan_komnas.desc": "The National Commission on Human Rights (Komnas HAM)—spearheaded by figures like Marzuki Darusman, Asmara Nababan, and Saparinah Sadli—is probing abuses ranging from the 1997–1998 activist abductions to mass graves in Aceh and militia violence in East Timor. Throw the authority of the presidency behind Komnas HAM's investigative teams and expand their independent budget. Earns a lasting political commitment from the Utusan Golongan caucus, while antagonizing ABRI's senior brass.",
	"faction.utusan_golongan.deal.golongan_komnas.text": "Grant Komnas HAM subpoena backing and budget autonomy for its human rights inquiries",
	"faction.utusan_golongan.deal.golongan_pakpahan.alert": "Photographs of the former political prisoner reviewing legislative drafts with you at Istana Merdeka run across the national press, winning praise from labor and civil-society delegates in Senayan.",
	"faction.utusan_golongan.deal.golongan_pakpahan.desc": "Four days after taking the oath of office in May 1998, you signed the amnesty releasing Indonesian Prosperous Workers Union (SBSI) founder Muchtar Pakpahan from Cipinang Prison, where Suharto's prosecutors had held him on subversion charges. Welcome Pakpahan and independent labor delegates to Istana Merdeka to help draft the new Trade Union Bill.",
	"faction.utusan_golongan.deal.golongan_pakpahan.text": "Invite freed SBSI union leader Muchtar Pakpahan to Istana Merdeka to co-draft the Manpower Bill",
	"faction.utusan_golongan.deal.golongan_rights.alert": "Human rights advocates at YLBHI and civic delegates inside the MPR applaud the presidential directive, while territorial commanders in Cilangkap complain that NGO lawyers are tying the hands of field officers.",
	"faction.utusan_golongan.deal.golongan_rights.desc": "Across the provinces, regional military commands ([i]Kodam[/i]) and local police still harass public-interest lawyers from the Indonesian Legal Aid Foundation (YLBHI), missing-persons investigators at KontraS, and peasant land-rights advocates. Sign a presidential instruction barring security forces from interfering with registered legal-aid, women's, and agrarian NGOs.",
	"faction.utusan_golongan.deal.golongan_rights.text": "Issue executive safeguards for YLBHI legal aid lawyers, KontraS investigators, and agrarian NGOs",
	"faction.utusan_golongan.mood.0": "Supportive",
	"faction.utusan_golongan.mood.1": "Favorable",
	"faction.utusan_golongan.mood.2": "Observing",
	"faction.utusan_golongan.mood.3": "Skeptical",
	"faction.utusan_golongan.mood.4": "Vocal Critics",
	"faction.utusan_golongan.mood.5": "Protesting",
	"faction.utusan_golongan.mood.6": "Irreconcilable",
	"faction.utusan_golongan.name": "Fraksi Utusan Golongan",
	"faction.utusan_golongan.portrait_name": "Fraksi Utusan Golongan",
	"faction.utusan_golongan.short": "U. Golongan",
	"faction.utusan_golongan.summary": "The [color=__CLR_MUTED__][b]Functional Group Delegates Faction (Fraksi Utusan Golongan)[/b][/color] seats sixty-five non-partisan representatives drawn from Indonesia's independent labor unions, women's coalitions, academic bodies, agrarian cooperatives, and religious minorities. For three decades under the New Order, Suharto used corporatist umbrella organizations—such as the state labor monopoly SPSI, the civil wives' association Dharma Wanita, and regime-vetted youth fronts—to pack these seats with pliant appointees who rubber-stamped presidential decrees in the name of organic state harmony.\n\nUnder the reform rules of Law No. 4/1999, however, the independent General Elections Commission (KPU) stripped the presidency of appointment power and awarded the sixty-five mandates to autonomous civil-society organizations. This class of [color=__CLR_MUTED__][b]Utusan Golongan[/b][/color] brings human rights lawyers, feminist organizers, Protestant and Catholic synod leaders, Buddhist and Hindu representatives, and independent trade unionists straight onto the Senayan floor. Viewing themselves as the moral conscience of the MPR, they reject backroom patronage envelopes. Demonstrating genuine reformist credibility at home and earning respect from international human rights and labor monitors give the Palace strong leverage over this principled caucus.",
	"faction_label.abri": "TNI",
	"faction_label.golkar_akbar": "Golkar (DPP Slipi)",
	"faction_label.golkar_habibie": "Golkar (Iramasuka)",
	"faction_label.other_parties": "Other Parties",
	"faction_label.pdip": "PDI-P",
	"faction_label.pkb": "PKB",
	"faction_label.poros_tengah": "PAN / Poros Tengah",
	"faction_label.ppp": "PPP",
	"faction_label.utusan_daerah": "U. Daerah",
	"faction_label.utusan_golongan": "U. Golongan",
	"friction.high.line": "Unrest in the streets is making backroom negotiations costlier to secure.",
	"friction.low.line": "Calm across the country is smoothing the Palace's negotiations.",
	"friction.normal.line": "The machinery of state is operating normally.",
	"fx.aberration.desc": "Text splits into red and cyan fringes, with a brief glitch shake every few seconds.",
	"fx.aberration.label": "RGB Chromatic Aberration",
	"fx.crt.desc": "Horizontal scanlines across the whole screen.",
	"fx.crt.label": "CRT Scanlines",
	"fx.curve.desc": "Darkened edges, rounded glass corners and a hint of glare, like a curved tube.",
	"fx.curve.label": "Curved Glass Vignette (Curvature)",
	"fx.flicker.desc": "A faint brightness flicker, moving static noise and a slow rolling bar. Flickering can bother people who are sensitive to flashing light.",
	"fx.flicker.label": "Screen Flicker & Static",
	"fx.glow.desc": "Text gets a soft glowing halo and the screen a faint bloom of light.",
	"fx.glow.label": "Phosphor Glow & Bloom",
	"gazette.empty": "No extraordinary decrees or omnibus bills have been signed into the State Gazette yet.",
	"gazette.title": "STATE GAZETTE",
