	"title.settings": "Settings",
	"title.tutorial": "How to play",
	"tutorial.0.text": "You are [b]B.J. Habibie[/b], the 3rd President of Indonesia. You have [color=__CLR_NAVY__][b]23 turns[/b][/color] (June to October 1999) before the [b]700 delegates[/b] of the [color=__CLR_NAVY__][b]MPR[/b][/color] vote on your [i]Pidato Pertanggungjawaban[/i] (Accountability Speech) on [b]October 19, 1999[/b].\n\n• [color=__CLR_DARK_GREEN__][b]Win:[/b][/color] at least [color=__CLR_DARK_GREEN__][b]351 votes[/b][/color] accept your speech and you keep the presidency.\n• [color=__CLR_DARK_RED__][b]Lose:[/b][/color] fewer than 351 votes.\n• The vote is a [color=__CLR_NAVY__][b]secret ballot[/b][/color]. Delegates can defect.\n• By default, metrics and factions are shown as qualitative tiers and stances (only [color=__STAT_PC__][b]Political Capital[/b][/color] and MPR seat counts are numbers). Anytime in Settings, you can toggle [color=__CLR_NAVY__][b]Show Exact Numbers (0–100)[/b][/color] for precise bars, floors, and post-choice deltas.",
	"tutorial.0.title": "I. The Goal",
	"tutorial.1.text": "Each turn has two parts.\n\n[b]1. [color=__CLR_NAVY__]Crisis Event[/color][/b][color=__CLR_NAVY__][/color]: a historical event. Pick one response. Every option changes your metrics and factions.\n\n[b]2. [color=__CLR_NAVY__]Action Phase[/color][/b][color=__CLR_NAVY__][/color]: you may do both of these once per turn.\n• One [color=__CLR_NAVY__][b]Executive Action[/b][/color]:\n  – [color=__CLR_NAVY__][b]Routine Action[/b][/color]: costs nothing, earns [color=__STAT_PC__][b]Political Capital[/b][/color], has a cooldown, and pays less each time you repeat it.\n  – [color=__CLR_NAVY__][b]Extraordinary Decree[/b][/color]: costs [color=__STAT_PC__][b]Political Capital[/b][/color], has requirements, and its effects are permanent.\n• One [color=__CLR_NAVY__][b]Faction Engagement[/b][/color]: negotiate with a faction. It costs [color=__STAT_PC__][b]Political Capital[/b][/color], and repeating the same deal with the same faction pays less. You can engage with a faction more than once, however, each interaction after the first one costs you 5 extra [color=__STAT_PC__][b]Political Capital[/b][/color]\n\nAll option cards and action filters sit in the lower thumb zone for effortless one-handed portrait play. Tap [color=__CLR_NAVY__][b]CONCLUDE AGENDA[/b][/color] to end the turn.",
	"tutorial.1.title": "II. Every Turn",
	"tutorial.2.text": "Seven metrics are on the [color=__CLR_NAVY__][b]Stat[/b][/color] tab at the bottom navigation bar for comfortable one-handed portrait access. [color=__STAT_PC__][b]Political Capital[/b][/color] ([color=__STAT_PC__][b]PC[/b][/color]) is your spending money (maximum 100).\n\n• [color=__STAT_POP__][b]Popularity[/b][/color]: public mood. High warms delegates every turn. Low erodes their trust.\n• [color=__STAT_MIL__][b]Military Support[/b][/color]: standing with Cilangkap. Tied to the [color=__FAC_ABRI__][b]ABRI[/b][/color] bloc.\n• [color=__STAT_REF__][b]Reformasi Credibility[/b][/color]: trust of students, the press and reformers. If it collapses, the streets erupt.\n• [color=__STAT_ECON__][b]Economic Health[/b][/color]: the rupiah and food prices. Freefall hurts [color=__STAT_POP__][b]Popularity[/b][/color] and [color=__STAT_STAB__][b]National Stability[/b][/color].\n• [color=__STAT_INTL__][b]International Standing[/b][/color]: credibility with foreign capitals and the [color=__STAT_INTL__][b]IMF[/b][/color]. Low standing causes capital flight.\n• [color=__STAT_STAB__][b]National Stability[/b][/color]: civic order. When it drops, every decree and negotiation costs more [color=__STAT_PC__][b]Political Capital[/b][/color].\n• [color=__STAT_CENDANA__][b]Cendana Influence[/b][/color]: the power of Suharto's inner circle. [color=__CLR_DARK_RED__][b]High is harmful:[/b][/color] it drains [color=__STAT_PC__][b]Political Capital[/b][/color] every turn, erodes [color=__STAT_REF__][b]Reformasi Credibility[/b][/color] and sabotages wavering delegates in the final vote.\n\nTogether they set your [color=__CLR_NAVY__][b]Government Stability[/b][/color] ([color=__CLR_DARK_GREEN__][b]SECURE[/b][/color], [color=__CLR_DARK_GREEN__][b]STABLE[/b][/color], [color=__STAT_ECON__][b]PRECARIOUS[/b][/color], [color=__CLR_DARK_RED__][b]UNSTABLE[/b][/color], [color=__CLR_DARK_RED__][b]COLLAPSING[/b][/color]). [color=__CLR_DARK_GREEN__][b]STABLE[/b][/color] or better gives free [color=__STAT_PC__][b]Political Capital[/b][/color] each turn. [color=__CLR_DARK_RED__][b]UNSTABLE[/b][/color] or worse drains it.",
	"tutorial.2.title": "III. The Metrics",
	"tutorial.3.text": "Each faction cares about specific metrics. Keeping those high gives you [color=__CLR_NAVY__][b]Bargaining Leverage[/b][/color]: negotiations cost less and win more goodwill.\n\n• [color=__FAC_PDIP__][b]PDI-P[/b][/color] (153 seats): [color=__STAT_POP__][b]Popularity[/b][/color], [color=__STAT_REF__][b]Reformasi Credibility[/b][/color].\n• [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]Golkar (Slipi)[/b][/color] (80): [color=__STAT_ECON__][b]Economic Health[/b][/color], [color=__STAT_STAB__][b]National Stability[/b][/color], [color=__STAT_CENDANA__][b]Cendana Influence[/b][/color].\n• [color=__FAC_GOLKAR_H__][b]Golkar (Loyalists)[/b][/color] (40): [color=__STAT_REF__][b]Reformasi Credibility[/b][/color], [color=__STAT_ECON__][b]Economic Health[/b][/color], [color=__STAT_INTL__][b]International Standing[/b][/color].\n• [color=__FAC_AXIS__][b]PAN[/b][/color] (34): [color=__STAT_REF__][b]Reformasi Credibility[/b][/color], [color=__STAT_POP__][b]Popularity[/b][/color].\n• [color=__FAC_PKB__][b]PKB[/b][/color] (51): [color=__STAT_POP__][b]Popularity[/b][/color], [color=__STAT_REF__][b]Reformasi Credibility[/b][/color].\n• [color=__FAC_PPP__][b]PPP[/b][/color] (58): [color=__STAT_STAB__][b]National Stability[/b][/color], [color=__STAT_POP__][b]Popularity[/b][/color].\n• [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]Other Parties[/b][/color] (46): [color=__STAT_STAB__][b]National Stability[/b][/color], [color=__STAT_POP__][b]Popularity[/b][/color].\n• [color=__FAC_ABRI__][b]ABRI[/b][/color] (38): [color=__STAT_MIL__][b]Military Support[/b][/color], [color=__STAT_STAB__][b]National Stability[/b][/color].\n• [color=__CLR_MUTED__][b]Utusan Daerah[/b][/color] (135): [color=__STAT_ECON__][b]Economic Health[/b][/color], [color=__STAT_STAB__][b]National Stability[/b][/color].\n• [color=__CLR_MUTED__][b]Utusan Golongan[/b][/color] (65): [color=__STAT_REF__][b]Reformasi Credibility[/b][/color], [color=__STAT_INTL__][b]International Standing[/b][/color].\n\nLate in the game [color=__FAC_AXIS__][b]PAN[/b][/color], [color=__FAC_PKB__][b]PKB[/b][/color] and [color=__FAC_PPP__][b]PPP[/b][/color] unite as the [color=__FAC_AXIS__][b]Central Axis[/b][/color] (163 seats).\n\n[b][color=__CLR_NAVY__]Favors[/color][/b][color=__CLR_NAVY__][/color]: some big concessions make a faction owe you a [color=__STAT_PC__][b]Favor[/b][/color]. Cash it in with a [color=__CLR_NAVY__][b]Final Appeal[/b][/color] in the last three turns for a large loyalty surge, or keep it for election night to steady wavering delegates. Each faction can hold only a few Favors, depending on difficulty.",
	"tutorial.3.title": "IV. The Factions",
	"tutorial.4.text": "Two factions react to how you treat them. Check the bars on their screens.\n\n• [b][color=__CLR_DARK_RED__]Military patience and anger[/color][/b][color=__CLR_DARK_RED__][/color] ([color=__FAC_ABRI__][b]ABRI[/b][/color] screen): ignore the generals and their patience drains into [color=__CLR_DARK_RED__][b]anger[/b][/color]. Anger cuts what every other faction gives you and your [color=__STAT_PC__][b]Political Capital[/b][/color] income. Meeting the generals holds patience. [color=__FAC_ABRI__][b]ABRI[/b][/color] loyalty above 55 slowly drains anger.\n• [b][color=__CLR_DARK_RED__]Street Mobilization[/color][/b][color=__CLR_DARK_RED__][/color] ([color=__FAC_PDIP__][b]PDI-P[/b][/color] screen): rises every turn you do not deal with [color=__FAC_PDIP__][b]PDI-P[/b][/color], and faster when they are hostile. At 25%, 50%, 75% and 100% it cuts your [color=__STAT_PC__][b]Political Capital[/b][/color], [color=__STAT_POP__][b]Popularity[/b][/color] and [color=__STAT_REF__][b]Reformasi Credibility[/b][/color] gains and makes [color=__FAC_PDIP__][b]PDI-P[/b][/color] costlier to talk to. At [color=__CLR_DARK_RED__][b]100%[/b][/color] they vote to reject to the last delegate.\n• [b][color=__STAT_CENDANA__]Cendana Influence[/color][/b][color=__STAT_CENDANA__][/color]: cutting it too fast in one turn can trigger bank runs and street sabotage. Lower it steadily.",
	"tutorial.4.title": "V. Meters to Watch",
	"tutorial.5.text": "[b]How delegates vote on October 19:[/b]\n• Disciplined blocs ([color=__FAC_PDIP__][b]PDI-P[/b][/color], [color=__FAC_ABRI__][b]ABRI[/b][/color]) follow their leadership.\n• Fragmented caucuses ([color=__FAC_GOLKAR_A__][b]Golkar (Slipi)[/b][/color], [color=__CLR_MUTED__][b]Utusan Daerah[/b][/color], [color=__CLR_MUTED__][b]Utusan Golongan[/b][/color], [color=__FAC_OTHER__][b]Other Parties[/b][/color]) split by their goodwill toward you, your [color=__CLR_NAVY__][b]Government Stability[/b][/color] and [color=__STAT_CENDANA__][b]Cendana Influence[/b][/color] interference.\n• Once the session starts, decrees that change seats, ban caucuses or rewrite election rules are closed.\n\n[b]Tips:[/b]\n• Never let [color=__STAT_PC__][b]Political Capital[/b][/color] sit idle. Spend it on factions that matter.\n• Watch the leverage line on each faction before you pay.\n• Turn on [color=__CLR_NAVY__][b]Outcome Forecast Tooltips[/b][/color] in Settings to preview effects. They are disabled on Historical.\n• Historical is the recommended difficulty. Beat it to unlock [color=__CLR_NAVY__][b]Severe State Situations[/b][/color].\n• Your campaign autosaves after every decision, and [color=__CLR_NAVY__][b]5 manual save slots[/b][/color] (with backup export/import) are available in the [color=__CLR_NAVY__][b]More (≡)[/b][/color] tab without disabling achievements.",
	"tutorial.5.title": "VI. Election Night and Tips",
